1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * '''Residence''': 1860 - Peru, Miami, Indiana, United States
2 CONT * '''Residence''': 1870 - Peru, Peru Township, Miami, Indiana, United States
2 CONT ** Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40001-774164259/elbert-hamilton-shirk-in-familysearch-family-tree FamilySearch Family Tree] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 9 2021, 6:01:
2 CONC 25 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Elbert Hamilton Shirk, h/o Mary Wright
2 CONT
2 CONT The Shirk family were highly respected citizens of Peru. They are listed in the History of Miami County, Indiana books. Elbert Hamilton became the president of the First National Bank in Peru in 1864.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elbert Hamilton Shirk came to Peru, IN the summer of 1844 in a two-horse wagon. He went into business with John Harlan in the mercantile business which dissolved a year later with Elbert continuing alone. He married an English des
2 CONC cent lady; Mary Wright, of Franklin County, 18 June 1845. They were blessed with 4 known children; Milton, Alice and Elbert Wright and an infant, James J.
2 CONT
2 CONT Between 1850 and 1855 he invested in Mexican war land warrants, in Iowa and other western States, which in turn were exchanged for improved farms in Miami County. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was considered the wealthiest man in northern Indiana, and one of the most affluent in Indiana.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a mansion style landmark house still standing in Peru (2020) that was built by the Edwards/Shirk families in 1862. It stands off of Hood Street and Main. It was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1995.*
2 CONC  Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/217929568/elbert-hamilton-shirk Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 9 2021, 6:12:29 UTC''
