1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alice Shirk Edwards, w/o Richard Arthur Edwards.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Edwards and Shirk families were highly respected citizens of Peru.  They are listed in the History of Miami County, Indiana books.  Alice's father was the president of the First National Bank in Peru.  Richard came to Peru aft
2 CONC er teaching at Knox College and started worked at the bank.  He quickly climbed the ranks and earned great respect among his piers.  Alice and Richard married Jan 1, 1880 and were blessed with 2 sons; Richard Elbert and Milton Art
2 CONC hur and 3 daughters; Mary Alice, Clara Ellen and Florence Esther.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice, daughter of Elbert H. Shirk and Mary R. Wright.  There is a mansion style landmark house still standing in Peru (2019) that was built by the Edwards/Shirk families in 1862.  It stand off of Hood Street and Main. It was list
2 CONC ed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1995.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice had been ill with agranular cystic angina for 3 days following a gall stone surgery.  She passed away at Methodists Hospital.
2 CONT
2 CONT Age: 76 Marital status: M Birth Date: 14 Nov 1853 Birth Place: Indiana Death Date: 9 Jan 1931 Death Place: Indianapolis, Marion, Indiana, USA Father: Elbert H. Shirk Mother: Mary R. Wright Shirk Spouse: Richard A. Edwards* Referen
