1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From "Pioneers of Old Hopewell" by Ralph Ege
2 CONT
2 CONT David Stout married first, Amy, daughter of Nehemiah Stout , and after her death married her sister Rachel, and removed to Mays Lick, now Maysville, Kentucky. He had at least two sons, Jonathan and Nathan, but we have no further r
2 CONC ecord of the family.
2 CONT
2 CONT From "History of the Stout Family" by Nathan Stout, 1823
2 CONT
2 CONT Annie (Amy) married David Stout and died childless, and Rachel married soon after to the same David Stout, by whom she has a number of children.
2 CONT --------------------
