1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Mrs. Margaret Gapen - Lewis Honecker received a telegram Wednesday morning announcing the death of Mrs. Margaret Gapen which occurred at 5 o'clock that morning at her home on Franklin street in Greensburg.  She ha
2 CONC d been sick for about 3 weeks with stomach trouble but was thought to be getting along nicely, especially on the day before her death when she seemed very much better.  About four o'clock she was attacked with heart trouble and di
2 CONC ed within an hour.
2 CONT      Mrs. Gapen was born Dec. 27th, 1825 in Franklin county near Brookville and was the daughter of Abner and Malinda Stout, who were the heads of one of Decatur county's earliest families.  While she was yet a little girl the fam
2 CONC ily moved to Decatur county and settled near Sardinia where Mrs. Gapen spent her girlhood days and lived much of her life.
2 CONT      She was married in 1875 to Stephen Gapen, of this place, and while no children were born to her she acted as the kindest of mothers to her step-granddaughter, Mrs. Harry Mock, formerly Miss Vetha Honecker.  After her husband'
2 CONC s death some fifteen years ago she continued to reside here until in June 1902, when with her grand-daughter she moved to Greensburg.  Since the latter's marriage, in June, her sister Rachel Stout, has made her home with her who w
2 CONC ith her brother, Oliver Stout and her grand-daughter are the only immediate relatives who survive her. 
2 CONT      Mrs. Gapen was a woman highly respected here, where in church affiliation she was a Baptist and a pillar of the church.  Lewis Honecker went to Greensburg Wednesday where the funeral service was held Friday forenoon and the b
2 CONC ody brought here for interment."
2 CONT Obituary, in The Thorntown Argus, Thorntown, Boone Co., Indiana, Saturday October 17, 1903, from microfilm from the Indiana State Library in Indianapolis* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/20698559/margaret-gapen Fin
2 CONC d A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Nov 30 2022, 8:59:20 UTC''
