1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Richard Arthur Edwards, h/o Alice Shirk.  They married Jan 1, 1880 and were blessed with 2 sons; Richard Elbert and Milton Arthur and 3 daughters; Mary Alice, Clara Ellen and Florence Esther.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard was the son Rev. Richard and Betsey (Josslyn-Samson) Edwards.  Their family was known in the New England colonies history.  The family is also mentioned in History of Miami County, IN books, pg 564/565. The family moved to
2 CONC  Illinois where his father was president of IL State Normal University and was pastor of the Congregational church at Princeton, IL.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard was also very successful.  He was very educated and was a teacher of English literature at Knox College.
2 CONT
2 CONT He came to Peru and started working at the First National Bank.  He quickly advanced and gained public respect. He lived a very long and prosperous life.
2 CONT
2 CONT Age: 95 Marital status: Widowed Birth Date: 9 Nov 1851 Birth Place: Bridgewater Mass Death Date: 17 Feb 1947 Death Place: Peru, Miami, Indiana
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard passed away at Dukes Memorial Hospital from cardio vascular renal disease.  The informant was his son Richard E.
2 CONT
