1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Published in The Tipton Daily Tribune, Tipton, Indiana, Wednesday, July 5, 1922.
2 CONT
2 CONT --Milton Edwards, aged 37, died Monday night at a hospital in New York, his death being due to sleeping sickness. Mr. Edwards was vice-president of the First National bank, of Peru, and was well known in Indiana banking circles. H
2 CONC is father was the late Milton A. Edwards, prominent in Peru financial circles. The Edwards family is related to the Shirk family of this city.
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in The Brook Reporter, Brook, Indiana, Friday, July 7, 1922. Peru, Indiana.
2 CONT
2 CONT Milton A. Edwards, 37 years old, vice president of the First national bank of Peru, died last night at New York of sleeping sickness. He was the son of Mr. and Mrs. R.. A. Edwards of Peru. Mrs. Wilton A. Edwards, a child, a brothe
2 CONC r and two sisters survive.
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in New York Herald, New York, New York, Friday, July 7, 1922.
2 CONT
