1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40001-330602097/delilah-edwards-born-burch-in-familysearch-family-tree FamilySearch Family Tree] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]:
2 CONC  ''Jan 16 2018, 13:56:47 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Delilah was born in 1770. She was the daughter of William Henry Burch and Mary Ann Lawrence.  She passed away in 1848.  Delilah Burch Edwards is buried at Edwards Cemetery in Greene County, Indiana, USA.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Burch-1250 WikiTree Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 16 2018, 14:02:14 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Delilah BURCH was the daughter of William Henry BURCH and his wife Mary Ann Lawrence. She was born 26 February 1771 in Rowan, Surrey County, North Carolina. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She had many siblings. (Ten have been named, though not all have been positively identified.)
2 CONT
2 CONT WILLIAM HENRY Jr BURCH 1764–1848 Elizabeth Burch                1766– Margaret Burch                1768– Mary Burch                       1772–1773 JOHN LAWRENCE BURCH   1774–1840 GEORGE BURCH Sr            1776–1862 James Philli
2 CONC p Burch           1777–1855 Joseph Burch                    1780–1852 Charles Burch                   1783–1860 Sarah Sally Burch              1785–1863
2 CONT
2 CONT Delilah married a farmer, William Edwards (1776–1848) in Surry, North Carolina on 6 Jun 1798. She was twenty-seven. Her husband was twenty-two.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had several children. Seven are named below: James Edwards                 1799–1884 William Edwards               1801–1866 Nancy Nash                      1803–1888 Charlotte Edwards            1805–1861 Mourning Edwards   
2 CONC         1807–1896 Hardin Edwards               1809–1877 George Edwards               1811–1888
2 CONT
2 CONT Sometime after the birth of her youngest son, George, in 1811 and the 1820 census, Delilah and her husband relocated from North Carolina to Monroe & Greene Counties in Indiana. The majority of her brothers and their families reloc
2 CONC ated as well. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Delilah lived to be 77 and died 14 October 1848. She was buried in the Edwards Cemetery, in Greene County Indiana.
2 CONT
2 CONT Written by Beth Hagan.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://old.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=11542477 Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 16 2018, 19:03:59 UTC''
