1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Son of  WILLIAM HENRY BURCH Sr Birth 10 MAY 1744 in  Haw River, Surry, North Carolina, USA    Death 1817 in  Surry, North Carolina  & Mary Ann LAWRENCE Birth 1740 in  Haw River, Surry, North Carolina    Death 09 JU
2 CONC N 1785 in  William, Surry, North Carolina  
2 CONT
2 CONT  This is taken from my book, “Footsteps From Baronshill,” which documents the Collings family from England to the US, from 1600’s to 1900’s. Jackie Foster
2 CONT
2 CONT  >George Sr Burch b. 14 Oct 1777, Stokes County, NC, d. 17 Jun 1862, Greene CO, IN, buried Jun 1862 Burch Cemetery, Beech CREEK TWP, Greene Co. IN.
2 CONT
2 CONT > BIOGRAPHY: Records from Burch Family Bible in possession of Mae H. Kent (decs.) La Crescenta, Calif. From Cora S. Winkler to Edw. E. Burch George m. Martha Lawrence, daughter of Richard Lawrence and Isabella (Cherokee Indian) Ro
2 CONC ss, 13 Oct 1799, Surry County, NC. Martha b. 27 May 1779, NC, d. 7 Nov 1868, Greene Co., IN, buried Nov 1868 in Beech CREEK TWP. Wedding date from Bible records. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=5137053&ref=acom&ftm=1 From FInd-a-Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT >George and Martha brought their family to Indiana sometime between 1814 & 1820. George became the first pastor of the Beech Creek Baptist Church. He was also a farmer and a blacksmith. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Elder George Burch founded the Hebron Regular Baptist Church on Little Indian Creek Saturday February 1822 on the Greene/ Monroe Co. line. Hebron Baptist was received into the White River Association of Regular Baptist October 1
2 CONC 822 Elder Burch went on to found the Beech Creek Regular Baptist. Hebron Baptist is the oldest Church in Monroe Co., Indiana 190 years old this year (2012)." - From: John H McGath, PhD. Hebron Regular Baptist Church
2 CONT
2 CONT >Their son Hubbard died young. John, James, Jane STORM, Abigail Crane and Mary Ellen Collins moved their families west and settled in MO, IA, & NE. (Jane returned.) Elizabeth STORM and Davis remained in Indiana.
2 CONT
2 CONT >His bio is recorded in the "History of Greene County Indiana"
2 CONT
2 CONT >Tombstone reads: s/o Wm and Mary, 85yr 5m 3da 
2 CONT
2 CONT >Married on 13 Oct 1789 or 1799 in Surry County, North Carolina, Martha "Mourning Moura" LAWRENCE 1779 – 1868; parents of:
2 CONT > * John BURCH 1799 – 1876
2 CONT > * James Black (Rev.) BURCH 1801 – 1886
2 CONT > * Elizabeth BURCH 1803 – 1834 [Storm]
2 CONT > * Jane BURCH 1806 – 1886 [Storm]
2 CONT > * Elder Davis (Rev.) BURCH 1811 – 1866
2 CONT > * Abigail BURCH 1814 – 1894 [Crane]
