1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Children of (unknown) and Lucretia Brown ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Bezaleel Brown (b. 1760, Albemarle Co., VA); d. c. 1778; (Deceased prior to 1806 Will). raised by Robert Harris. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1/2 brother to Bezaleel Brown Harris (b. 1 Oct 1779) who m. Elizabeth "Polly" Thompson.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Bezaleel Brown was born in 1760 in Albemarle County, Virginia. He was the eldest son of Lucretia "Lucy" Brown (1746–1806). 
2 CONT
2 CONT His birth occurred approximately two years prior to his mother's marriage to Robert Harris. While some traditional family trees invent a brief first marriage for Lucretia to account for this child, there are no primary marriage re
2 CONC cords or probate files in Albemarle County to support the existence of a "Bezaleel Brown, Sr." It is more likely he was born prior to her legal union with Harris.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bezaleel was raised within the Harris household alongside his eleven half-siblings. Despite being fully integrated into the family, he retained his mother's maiden name. His life was short; he passed away circa 1778 at approximate
2 CONC ly 18 years of age, shortly before the family moved to Surry County, North Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Identity & Disambiguation ===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Naming Confusion: Bezaleel is frequently confused with his uncle, Bezaleel Brown (1754–1829), and his younger half-brother, Bezaleel Brown Harris (1779–1814). 
2 CONT * The "Adopted" Label: In many family records, he is listed as "adopted" to explain why a child with the surname Brown was living in a Harris household.
2 CONT * Relationship to Bezaleel Brown Harris: He was the maternal half-brother of Bezaleel Brown Harris. In this family, it was a common practice to reuse a significant name like "Bezaleel" for a younger son after the death of an older
2 CONC  child who bore the name.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT == Family ==
2 CONT
