1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * interesting ancestry dot com link:<br/>
2 CONT [https://www.ancestry.com/interactive/14300/dvm_LocHist001132-00368-1/560?backurl=https%3a%2f%2fsearch.ancestry.com%2fcgi-bin%2fsse.dll%3fdb%3dGenealogy-glh16249345%26gss%3dsfs28_ms_r_db%26new%3d1%26rank%3d1%26gsln%3dwells%26gsln_
2 CONC x%3d1%26gskw%3dNew%2bBritain%26MSAV%3d1%26uidh%3d277&ssrc=&backlabel=ReturnSearchResults&rc=452,1809,602,1849;1246,2545,1387,2592;1679,2556,1860,2602;267,2915,399,2962;399,2919,582,2964#?imageId=dvm_LocHist001132-00155-0 History o
2 CONC f Bucks County, Pennsylvania : from the discovery of the Delaware to the present time Volume I. Chapter XVII. Buckingham. 1703]
2 CONT * said by some to have been born 09/13/1775 bur this would make her roughy 40 years younger than her husband (!)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * born in Solebury or Plumstead; married Jonathan Wells; the couple then moved to Chester County
2 CONT ** estimated year of Mary's birth: ''1760s'', plus or minus 10 years (I make this est. based on the screen shot of ''The History of Bucks County, Pennsylvania : from the discovery of the Delaware to the present time''; Volume I. C
2 CONC hapter XVIII.; Solebury (1703); page 281, attached to this profile 
2 CONT * may have been known also as "Polly", as many Marys were known to be during that era of early America. > see this vague diary reference from Plumstead  (dated April 22, 1797) This is a lead because both the Rich and Wells familie
2 CONC s had lived in Bucks County but then moved to Chester County = Pennsylvania Vital Records, Vol. II; Memoranda from the Diary of [https://www.geni.com/people/John-Dyer/6000000007418598860 John Dyer of Plumstead], Bucks Co., Pa.; [h
2 CONC ttps://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/48383/images/PAVitalRecordsII-001138-30?ssrc=&backlabel=Return&rc=336%2C415%2C460%2C439&pId=323112&backurl=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ancestry.com%2F (page 42 of 841)]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Mary Wells (Rich) suffered marital discord with her husband Jonathan Wells==
2 CONT
2 CONT ''"3-27-1796   Mary Wells left her husband last fall and Wm Preston set off with her this morn. to see if he would use her better to try to reconcile them."'' < this from: ''Pennsylvania Vital Records, Vol. II
2 CONT Memoranda from the Diary of John Dyer of Plumstead, Bucks Co., Pa.'' (page 41 of 841) > see timeline<br/>
2 CONT *William Preston was an in-law of sorts and a Quaker elder > Mary's brother John Rich married Mary Preston. This sister-in-law's father is this William Preston (1746-1819). This William had a brother-in-law by the name of Thomas D
2 CONC yer. Thomas' brother is the author of ''Memoranda from the Diary of [https://www.geni.com/people/John-Dyer/6000000007418598860 John Dyer of Plumstead], Bucks Co., Pa.'' = John Dyer (1736-1811)
2 CONT ** John Dyer, the writer, has [a more direct relationship to Mary Wells (Rich)  > [https://www.geni.com/path/Mary-Wells+is+related+to+John-Dyer?from=6000000075881185847&path_type=blood&to=6000000007418598860 John Dyer is Mary Well
2 CONC s (Rich)'s third cousin once removed]
2 CONT *Jonathan Wells was an early childhood friend of John Dyer whose extensive diary chronicles events in Jonathan's life. These note several problems Jonathan had in his lifetime. See: Publications of the Genealogical Society of Penn
2 CONC sylvania, Volume 3. The original, which evidently has more detail, is at the Pennsylvania Historical Society. Here is url for examination of the abbreviated version: https://books.google.com/books?id=GdUUAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA54&lpg=PA54&
2 CONC dq=william+Walton+Plumstead+chester+county&source=bl&ots=Z23rNdRsok&sig=ACfU3U3z80qQpyoab3zlmukfNCBBypOEvA&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwi-3-ug0JHqAhVDneAKHeSmBZoQ6AEwAHoECAkQAQ#v=onepage&q=Wells%20&f=false 
