1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Palatine Ship NORRIS 1732
2 CONT
2 CONT The following immigrants were the survivors of the ship Love And Unity, which landed at Martha's Vineyard, near Boston, after over one hundred of it's one hundred and fifty passengers had died on board ship. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The incident involving the ship LOVE AND UNITY took place in May 1731 when 34 survivors reached Philadelphia in May 1732 (oaths of allegiance and abjuration signed 15 May), aboard the ship NORRIS, from Boston, Thomas Lloyd, master
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Strassburger-Hinke, vol. 1, pp. 57-58; Frank Ried Diffenderffer, _The German Immigration into Pennsylvania through the Portof Philadelphia, 1700 to 1775, Part II. The Redemptioners_ (Lancaster, PA:the author, 1900), pp. 63
2 CONC -68
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Loyd, Master, from Boston.May 15th, 1732. 
2 CONT
2 CONT •	Kasper Schirch 
2 CONT
2 CONT •	Johannes (O) Behn 
2 CONT
2 CONT •	Marthin Gassner 
2 CONT
2 CONT •	Christian (X) Reninger 
2 CONT
2 CONT •	Mathias (X) Weber 
2 CONT
2 CONT •	Johannes (H) Herman 
2 CONT
2 CONT •	Johann Philip Weber 
2 CONT
2 CONT •	V alentine (X) Westheber 
2 CONT
2 CONT •	Johann Jacob Manncher [?] 
2 CONT
2 CONT •	Johann Georg Liebenstein. 
2 CONT
2 CONT •	Johann Michael Sigmund 
2 CONT
