1 NAME John /Gregg/
2 GIVN John
2 SURN Gregg
2 _MARNM Gregg
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Goose Creek Burying Ground
2 ADDR
3 CITY Purcellville
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE DEC 1716
2 ADDR
3 STAE Delaware
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE 9 JUN 1788
2 PLAC Loudoun County, Virginia, United States of America
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/109134856/john-gregg
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Died in Parish of Shelbourn
2 CONT Goose Creek Mtg at Lincoln
2 CONT
2 CONT Born deaf, some records indicate he could neither hear nor speak and was called "Dumb John".
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of George Gregg and Sara Hogg
2 CONT m: Susannah Curle, Aug 13 1737, New Garden Meeting.  She died summer of 1765, was dau of Richard Curle of New Castle DE.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Dec. 1765, after his wife's death, John obtained a certificate of removal from Kennett Mtg in Chester Co PA to the Goose Creek Mtg at Lincoln, Loudorn CO VA. and moved there with his children.
2 CONT
2 CONT He inherited 115 acres from his father and also inherited from his Uncle John Hogg in 1748.  His own will was made June 2 1787.
2 CONT
2 CONT ch inc:
2 CONT -Mary Gregg Aug 8 1738- /Loundorn Co VA, married out of Friends Mtg Mar 25 1780 to George Nixon.  No children, raised one of his nieces.
2 CONT
2 CONT -Hannah Mar 1740, moved back to Deleware taking the family register with her.  Md: William Dixon whose will was probated June 18 1777, New Castle, had Ann (m: Wilson), Elizabeth (who m: William Underwood 1757), and William.
2 CONT
2 CONT -Amos Apr 13 1742 Kennett PA-Jan 1 1814 Scott Co KY.  M: not of Friends mtg in Loudourn Co VA on Jan 25 1766, Pricilla Gregg (1745-bef 1815, Scott Co KY.)  Ch inc: Israel Gregg, Elizabeth/m Joseph Watkins, Joseph, Samuel, Susannah
2 CONC , John L., George L., Hiram.
2 CONT
2 CONT -Amy, Oct 28 1744 m: Thomas Gregg Dec 3 1766 at Fairfax Mtg, Waterford, Londourn Co MO.  He was born 1743/PA, died 1821, son of Samuel Gregg and Elizabeth Alford.  ch inc: Nimrod, Ruth, Mary Elizabeth, Thomas, John, Dianah, Samuel
2 CONC , John.
2 CONT
2 CONT -George Apr 26 1747-Mar 1810 Middle Island VA.  m1: unk Nov 25 1769, out of Friends, m2: Margaret Todhunter, m3: Ruth Gregg, m4 Naomi Villers.  Will made Mar 21 1810 named John, George, Elsea/Elsey, and Ruth and step-dau Mary Vill
2 CONC ers.
2 CONT
2 CONT -John Sep 28 1749-d abt Jan 1 1819, Loudoun CO VA.  Will probated Jan 4 1819 left all to friend Richard Greene, his executor.
2 CONT
2 CONT -Richard b Mar 5 1753 New Castle DE, d: Nov 15 1812, Carmichaels, Green Co PA.  m: Nancy Ann Gregg (b: May 5 1756-d: Jan 20 1817 dau of Samuel Gregg and Elizabeth Alford) out of Friends Mtg.  Was Private, third class in Capt. Will
2 CONC iam Crawford's Co., Washington Co PA, Militia Fifty Battalion, Revolutionary War.  Ch: Milton Mahlen, Ruth, Permelia, Priscilla, Rezin, Craven, Presly,Aaron, Experience "Pery", Alford.  Richard may have had an early marriage with 
2 CONC a son named Levi.
2 CONT
2 CONT -Lydia Aug 12 1758/OH m: Howell
2 CONT
2 CONT -Rebecca 1758 New Castle DE-Aug 1822 Knox Co IN, m: Francis Seaton 1784.  He was born abt 1756 d: abt Nov 1 1820, both buried "Upper Indiana Cemetery" near Vincennes.  ch inc: John, Elizabeth "Betsey", James, Susan, Rebecca Seaton
2 CONC .* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/109134856/john-gregg Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 25 2024, 22:12:10 UTC''
