1 NAME Mary /Gregg/
2 GIVN Mary
2 SURN Gregg
2 _MARNM Nixon
1 NAME Mary Gregg Nixon
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 PLAC Nixon Family Cemetery, Woodburn, Loudoun County, Virginia, USA
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1743
2 PLAC County Antrim, Northern Ireland
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 29 OCT 1804
2 PLAC Loudoun County, Virginia, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary Gregg, 2nd wife of George Nixon, was born 8 mo/Oct 8, 1738 as recorded by Kennett Mtg in Chester Co, PA. Several rotating meetings were held in this area: Kennett Mtg & New Garden Mtg in Chester Co, PA with Ne
2 CONC wark Mtg & Centre Mtg in Newcastle Co, now state of Delaware. They were all in the vicinity of the 12 Mile Circle between Chester Co, PA and Newcastle on the Delaware (called Lower Counties), part of the 80 year boundary dispute b
2 CONC etween Wm Penn & Charles Calvert., finally settled by the Mason-Dixon line. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the eldest daughter of "Deaf" John Gregg and Susannah Curle, who married 8mo/Oct 13, 1737 at New Garden Meeting House.   her father: 
2 CONT John Gregg (1716 - 1788) 
2 CONT her mother: 
2 CONT Susanna Gregg (1718 - 1764) 
2 CONT Contributor: Gwynne H Seward (49350923)
2 CONT
2 CONT I posted her birth record to the Memorial herein, however no matter how I designate it, it pops up as the primary photo. Perhaps there is something that can be done on your end to designate the photos of the grave markers to be pr
2 CONC imary and push the birth record back?
2 CONT
