1 NOTE David's will proved 28 Mar 1887.
1 NOTE David lived on the road between Hopewell & Stoutsburg.  Nathan Stout in "History of the Stout Family" says David was an honist man & a Christian.   He was probably a Captain.  He was an invalid for several years before his death. 
2 CONC  (Bendedict's "History of the Baptists" says David was one of the main pillars of the Hopewell Church).  David's will proved 26 Dec 1788. Pioneers of Old Hopewell, p 262 says in his father, Jonathan Stout's will, proved 25 March 1
2 CONC 723,  he bequeathed to  his 2 youngest sons, Samuel & David (who were aged 14 & 17, respectively)  the tract on which Jonathan resided at the tiime of his death.
