2 DATE 4 MAY 1810
2 ADDR
3 STAE New Jersey
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''NOTE: James Stout is almost always confused with [https://www.geni.com/people/James-Stout/6000000208488706822 James "Turler" Stout]. These were two different men.''
2 CONT
2 CONT James Stout (b. c. 1732, d. 4 May 1810); did patriotic service in New Jersey; married to Catherine Stout. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Catherine Merrill Stout==
2 CONT "I now take up James, the third brother who married Catherine Stout, daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Stout/6000000006176075000, by whom he had three sons and four daughters - [https://www.geni.com/people/Jesse-Stout/6
2 CONC 000000041128303505 Jesse], [https://www.geni.com/people/Amos-Stout/6000000208421107824 Amos], [https://www.geni.com/people/Charles-Stout/6000000208445224849 Charles], [https://www.geni.com/people/Rachel-Manners/6000000025781854375
2 CONC  Rachel], [https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Stout/6000000207937655882 Elizabeth], [https://www.geni.com/people/Catharine-Bryant/6000000061319585877 Catherine] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Anne-Stout/6000000088577852325 An
2 CONC ne]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Jesse married [https://www.geni.com/people/Abigail-Stout/6000000024931314058 Abigail Lott], daughter of Phelix Lott, by whom he had five sons and I think seven daughters. 
2 CONT # Amos married [https://www.geni.com/people/Catherine-Stout/6000000208420985831 Catherine Drake], the daughter of William Drake, by whom he has a number of children, but as he moved to the Lake Country soon after he was married, I
2 CONC  can neither tell the names or number of his children.
2 CONT # Charles married Arlissa Saxton, a daughter of Jared Saxton, by whom he has a number of children.''
2 CONT # Rachel married [https://www.geni.com/people/John-Manners-III/6000000078076457271 John Manners], by whom she had two sons, the eldest named [https://www.geni.com/people/Gen-James-Manners/6000000144017974846 James Stout (Manners)]
2 CONC , the other [https://www.geni.com/people/Dr-John-Manners/6000000033283320508 John].
2 CONT # Elizabeth married David Stout, and after his death, to John Hoagland, but has no children. 
2 CONT #Catherine married James Bryant, and has a number of children, but as they moved soon after to the Lake Country, I am not able to tell their names or number." -- [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000207722964889 The 
2 CONC History of the Stout Family], By Nathan Stout, 1823, page 12''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Some Notes on Deaths==
2 CONT James Stout --- Catherine's husband -- died May 10, 1810, in Hunterdon County, according to [https://www.geni.com/documents/view/death_event-6000000008631054632?doc_id=6000000207730588838&event_id=6000000008631054632 an abstract] 
2 CONC of his will, which cites his children Jesse, Amos, Charles, Rachel, Elizabeth, and Catherine (Bryant). It also mentions "his share in the library."
2 CONT
2 CONT A James Stout Jr. [https://www.ancestry.com/discoveryui-content/view/11005:2793?tid=&pid=&queryid=e9e35db4-6cdf-4f92-9e20-b321e61548b7&_phsrc=DcV3235&_phstart=successSource died Jan. 31, 1807], in Hopewell. A James Stout Sr., [htt
2 CONC ps://www.ancestry.com/discoveryui-content/view/32738:2793?tid=&pid=&queryid=d1a48cef-849e-4be1-ac7f-de9f25cf56a4&_phsrc=DcV3236&_phstart=successSource died Aug. 12, 1782], and deeded his Amwell Township plantation to his son James
2 CONC . Another James Stout died in 1784 in Amwell.
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine Stout died May 4, 1805, but [https://www.ancestry.com/discoveryui-content/view/604423:8796?tid=&pid=&queryId=fccdad2e-d4f3-43fe-9289-9fc683e4141c&_phsrc=hLA545&_phstart=successSource her probate documents] appear to be e
2 CONC mpty.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia Stout died November 28, 1803, in Oxford Township, Sussex County, NJ. Apparently she died intestate, suggesting her James Stout died earlier. However, a James Stout [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CSYH-K38V-
2 CONC M?i=733&cat=220727 bought land] in Independence Township in Sussex on Sept. 5 1804. A different (younger) man one assumes.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
