2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 DEC 1935
2 PLAC Weatherford, Parker County, Texas, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Albert Eli Snow was born 1852. He was the son of Winston and Mary Burch Snow. Albert married his first wife, Elizabeth F. McGowan on 6 January 1876 in Grayson Co., Texas. They had two children William Riley and Mar
2 CONC tha Melvina. Then he married his second wife, Nancy Ann Roller on 3 October 1881 in Palo Pinto Co., Texas. They had six children: Charlie Edward, Richard Albert, Robert Harrison, Cordelia, Mable Gene, and Myrtie Rendy. Albert died
2 CONC  on 8 December 1935 and was buried on 16 December 1935 at Dobbs Valley Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary from
2 CONT The Weekly Herald 
2 CONT Weatherford, Texas
2 CONT December 12, 1935 Albert Snow Dies
2 CONT at His Home Here Saturday Night
2 CONT  Albert Snow, aged 82 years, passed away at his home, 509 Bols d'Arc street, this city, Saturday night at 11:45 o'clock. He had been ill for some time, and his death was not unexpected.
2 CONT   Mr. Snow had been a resident of Parker County, for fifteen years, having moved here from Palo Pinto County. His wife Mrs. Nancy Snow died five years ago, and he is survived by the following six sons and daughters: Mrs. Nellie Mc
2 CONC Guire, Pilot Point, R. A. Snow, Mineral Wells, R. H. Snow, Weatherford, Mrs. Cordelia Sterling, Mrs. Mable Booker, and Mrs. Myrtle Ellison, all of Fort Worth.
2 CONT   The body was taken overland to Dobbs Valley in Palo Pinto County, Monday afternoon, and burial took place in the Dobbs Valley cemetery, beside his late wife, at 2 o'clock* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/15941812
2 CONC /albert-eli-snow Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 23 2023, 17:00:05 UTC''
