1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-294742011-1-500260/winston-burch-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-a83896673c8cdfcbef726ca1036e7e28&mrid=a1ce317fcfcc14dc99de88e9caeefdf5
2 CONC  MyHeritage Family Trees] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 20 2018, 17:48:37 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Winston was the son of Charles and Elizabeth [SUTHERLAND] BURCH. He was born in Surry Co NC in 1815, but moved westward to Greene Co IN while still a boy. Winston's father and many Burch uncles and cousins had taken advantage of t
2 CONC he opening of the new state to claim land for farming.
2 CONT
2 CONT Winston married 30 Nov 1841 to Nancy Ann BRYANT, the daughter of William and Sarah BRYANT. Winston was 26 and his bride was 16. Winston and Nancy started a family. They would eventually have seven children, but the spacing between
2 CONC  births leads me to believe that there might have been other children who did not survive.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1850, Winston farmed land in Monroe Co IN near Nancy's father's property. Sometime between 1857 and 1860 Winston and Nancy moved west to Henderson Co IL. Her father, William BRYANT, already in his 70s, moved his family to Hende
2 CONC rson IL as well. William BRYANT's property is valued at $1500 in the 1860 census, while in comparison Winston's is a much more modest $440.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sometime between 1862 & 1866 Winston and Nancy moved their family further west to Nodaway County, MO. Nodaway County, MO and nearby Page Co, IA had been settlement destinations for some of Winston's Burch cousins so it's possible 
2 CONC that Winston was influenced by family to select this area. It's also likely that Nancy's parents had passed away in the early 1860s and that she and her sister inherited their property. Nancy's widowed sister Catherine Dobbins joi
2 CONC ned the Burch household. 
2 CONT
2 CONT By the 1870 Census the last of their seven children had been born. Their oldestchild Provine, had died prematurely and the second, Josephine, married. The third, Sarah, would marry in 1873. Winston continued to farm. His property 
2 CONC value had grown by 1870 to $1500. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Winston died in early 1880 at the age of 65. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Winston and Nancy's seven known children, all daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT Provine BURCH            1844 – 1862 Josephine FAKES          1849 – 1929 Sarah E COFFMAN            1852 – 1915 Ella Florence BURCH      1857 – 1929 Olive Martha HELM      1860 – 1941 Elmyriah BURCH            1862 – 1924 Louisa 
2 CONC GRIFFITH             1866 – 1941* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/9041478/winston-burch Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 14 2020, 15:15:39 UTC''
