1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/7943266/christopher-harris
2 CONT
2 CONT son of https://www.geni.com/people/Major-Robert-Harris-of-Albemarle-County/6000000003073335079?through=6000000003073165865 & https://www.geni.com/people/Mourning-Harris/6000000003073165865?through=6000000003073335079
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Harris-1877
2 CONT * https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/LKKM-Q28/christopher-harris-1725-1794
2 CONT * https://www.oocities.org/wlabach/harrisan.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT A Patriot of the American Revolution for Virginia.  [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A051551  DAR Ancestor # A051551]
2 CONT
2 CONT PATRIOTIC SERVICE Birth:  5 Feb 1725    HANOVER CO VIRGINIA Death:  (ANTE) 4 Mar 1794    MADISON CO KENTUCKY Service Source: ABERCROMBIE & SLATTEN, VA REV PUB CLAIMS, VOL 1, P 11 Service Description: 1) FURNISHED SUPPLIES, ALBEMAR
2 CONC LE COUNTY
2 CONT
2 CONT Link for Find a Grave  http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GScid=1806323&GRid=7943266&
2 CONT
2 CONT Christopher Harris, the son of Major Robert Harris, was born in Hanover Co. or the new county of Louisa, 3 Feb 1725. On 22 Feb 1745, he married Mary Dabney, daughter of Cornelius Dabney and Sarah, his wife. He married second, Agne
2 CONC s McCord, (21 Dec 1740- ) daughter of Johannes McCord (born 1685) and his wife, Isabel, born 1698. McCord's will was probated in Albemarle in 1764 and one of the witnesses was Gabriel Maupin (6). Christopher Harris died in Madison
2 CONC  County, KY, in 1794. His will was probated 4 Mar 1794. He was a member of the company of men who defended Boonesborough against the Indians and British during the Revolution.
2 CONT
2 CONT Data added @ The Story Gabriel and Marie Maupin by Dorothy Maupin Shaffett, 2000
2 CONT
2 CONT Christopher and Mary (Dabney) Harris had seven children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Dabney, Sarah, Robert, Mourning, Christopher, Mary, and Tyre (born in Virginia, February 21, 1778).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary died and Christopher remarried to Agnes McCord about 1762. They had ten additional children: John, Benjamin, William, Barnabas, James, Samuel, Jane, Margaret, Isabel, and Overton. All of Christopher children except Margaret s
2 CONC urvived to adulthood, married, and had children. [7, 9, 10]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000188931189884&size=large}}
2 CONT
