2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT The National Society of the Daughters of the American Revolution Volume 106
2 CONT page 197
2 CONT
2 CONT [p.197] Mrs. Margaret B. Harris Trimble.
2 CONT DAR ID Number: 105621
2 CONT Born in Boone County, Mo.
2 CONT Wife of John Trimble.
2 CONT Descendant of Christopher Harris, Col. James Woods, James Garland and Capt. William Pickett, as follows:
2 CONT 1. James Harris (1818-81) m. 1849 Sabra Brown Jackson (1829-1903).
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Overton Harris (1789-1844) m. 1814 Mary Rice Woods (1795-1876); Wade M. Jackson (1797-1879) m. 1814 Sara Bass (1795-1845).
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. John Harris (1765-1810) m. 1785 Margaret Maupin (1767-1855); James Woods m. 1779 Mary Garland (1760-1835); Dempsey Jackson  (1763-1836) m. 1788 Mary Pickett (1765-1839).
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Christopher Harris m. 2nd 1764 Agnes McCord (b. 1740); James Garland m. Mary Rice; William Pickett m. 1st 1767 Elizabeth Metcalf  (1739-73).
2 CONT
2 CONT Christopher Harris (1725-94) was a soldier in the Kentucky militia, 1780. He was born in Albemarle County, Va.; died in Madison County,  Ky.
2 CONT
2 CONT James Woods (1748-1822) was colonel of a regiment of Virginia infantry, 1776. He was born in Albemarle County, Va.; died in Garrard  County, Ky.
2 CONT
2 CONT James Garland (1722-1812) enlisted, 1777, as a matross, in Capt. William Pierce's company, Col. Charles Harrison's regiment of Virginia  artillery, and was acting magistrate of Albemarle County, Va., 1782, where he died. He was bo
2 CONC rn in Hanover County, Va.  Also No. 74848.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Pickett (1735-98) served as captain in Col. Thomas Marshall's regiment, Virginia Line. He was born in Virginia; died in Fauquier  County, Va.
2 CONT
2 CONT This is the will of Christopher Harris of Mad. Co, KY taken from Will Book A-
2 CONT page 54, 55. It was transcribed by Eileen Niederkorn.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHRISTOPHER HARRIFS WILL - Will Book A-pg 54, 55
2 CONT
2 CONT In the name of God Amen.  I Christopher Harris being through the abundant
2 CONT mercy and goodness of God tho weak in body yet of perfect understanding and
2 CONT memory do constitute this my last will & Testament and desire it should be
2 CONT reviewed by all as such.  Imprimis that I will & Desire that my first
2 CONT Children (Viz)  Dabney Harris, Sarah Martin, Robert Harriss, Mourning Jones,
2 CONT Christopher Harrifs, & Mary Jones should have the following negroes
2 CONT (excepting thirty pounds out of my son Dabneys Legacy which is to be paid by
2 CONT the Executors of this Part of my Will for the use & Benefit of my wife and
2 CONT Other Children) (Viz)  Ritter and her Children, Pomp, Moses, Allice, George,
2 CONT Betty, Lucy and Delphy the above Negores to be Divided Agreeable to
2 CONT Cornelias Dabneys Seniors Will and I do appoint Foster Jones, and Christoph
2 CONT Harrifs as Executors of the above part of this will and as to the Ballance
2 CONT of my Estate I Direct that first my Debts shall be paid out of what money
2 CONT I have by or is owing to me the house where I live I Direct should be
2 CONT finished which together with the tract of land whereon I live, I leave to
2 CONT my Dear & loving wife during her life and at ther death to son Overton
2 CONT Harrifs as to the Ballance of my Negroes (David, Cate, Fanny, Stephen, and
2 CONT Eddy together with my House hold furniture Stock of every kind and
2 CONT Plantation utensels I desire that my wife may have the whole Benefit of them
2 CONT during her life or widowhood and if she should Marry the  whole to be sold
2 CONT and Equally Divided amongst her & her children as to my Lands on Muddy Creek
2 CONT I will and Bequeath them as follows, the Drowning Creek Tract of land I will
2 CONT and Bequeath to my son John Harrifs the Sycamore Spring Tract to my son
2 CONT Benjamin Harris the tract on which my son Wm. has Built to my son Harris
2 CONT and the Tract Clalled the Holly Tract to my son Barnabas Harrifs and my land
2 CONT in Albemarle County together with the Stock that is thereon I direct shall
2 CONT be sold and that my sons James and Samuel Harris shall Receive of the money
2 CONT as much as Col John Miller & Robert Rodes shall Judge the land to be worth
2 CONT that I will’d to my Other sons Viz  to be made Equal to them, as to my three
2 CONT Daughters Viz Jane Gentry-Margret Harris, and Isabel Harris my will and
2 CONT Desire is that Jean Gentry should Receive ten pounds and Margret and Isbel
2 CONT Harris to have fifty pounds apeice out of the Ballance of what my Albermarld
2 CONT land and the Proffits arising from that place and if that should not be
2 CONT Sufficient that It shall be made up to htem out of any of Personal Estate
2 CONT that my wife and Executors after nemtioned shall think best as to my lands
2 CONT on Sinking Waters my will is that if they are obtained it should be sold
2 CONT and Wqually divided amongst my last Set of Children and I do appoint my dear
2 CONT & loveing wife with John Sappington and John Harris to execute that part of
2 CONT my will that respects my wife and her Children as witnefs my hand & seal
2 CONT this twentyeth day of February one thousand seven hundred and ninety four.
2 CONT Witnefs-Hartly Sappington                              Christopher Harrifs
2 CONT Rich’d Sappington  Joseph Wells
2 CONT At a Court held for Madison County on Tuesday the 15th day of March 1794
2 CONT This Will was proved to be the last will & testament of Christopher Harris
2 CONT by the oath of Joseph Wells, Hartly & Richard Sappington witnefses thereto
2 CONT and ordered to be recorded.                        Teste  Will Irvine  CMC
2 CONT Typed as spelled in will.
2 CONT
2 CONT
