1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for NORTH CAROLINA.  [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A051977  DAR Ancestor # A051977]
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of https://www.geni.com/people/Major-Robert-Harris-of-Albemarle-County/6000000003073335079?through=6000000003073165865 & https://www.geni.com/people/Mourning-Harris/6000000003073165865?through=6000000003073335079
2 CONT
2 CONT About 1723 – Tyree Glenn Harris, son of Maj. Robert Harris and Mourning Glenn, was born in Hanover County, Virginia. He later settled in Orange County, North Carolina, becoming High Sheriff there. He also took part in the Battle o
2 CONC f Alamance on May 18, 1771, on the side of Gov. Tryon. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Oct. 4, 1787 - RegLn 1315 Jessee Simpson to Richard Oldham [Richard Simpson to Jesse Oldham], 204 acres, proved by Robert Rainey.
2 CONT Chilton’s notes: Not found, but see CwDB F/178 Jesse Oldham & wife Elizabeth to Thomas Hornbuckle, 4 Oct 1787, 403 acres on S Fork of Stoney Creek, incl where Oldham lives, adj Thomas Brinsfield, Simpson, Tyree Harris, Hughes - tw
2 CONC o tracts one Richard Simpson to Jesse Oldham, other NC to Jesse Oldham.
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: Tyree Glenn Harris (b. c1723), s/o Maj. Robert Harris (c1698-1765) and Mourning Glenn (c1702-1776). Married Elizabeth Chapman. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Mollie was 2nd wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT His will - Caswell County, NC WB B, pg. 162, proved Jan court 1787.
2 CONT
