1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT This individual is the unidentified father of Bezaleel Brown (1760–c. 1778). He was an associate of Lucretia "Lucy" Brown in Albemarle County, Virginia, around 1759–1760.
2 CONT
2 CONT While many traditional family trees and 20th-century genealogical narratives assign the name "Bezaleel Brown, Sr." to this person, there is no primary archival evidence—such as marriage bonds, church vestry records, or probate fil
2 CONC ings—to confirm a man of that name married Lucretia or lived in the immediate vicinity during that specific window. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The presence of a son carrying the mother's maiden name (Brown) within the household of her later husband, Robert Harris, suggests that this individual and Lucretia were not legally married. The name "Bezaleel" was likely given to
2 CONC  the son as a tribute to Lucretia's own family lineage (specifically her brother or father's naming traditions) rather than as a patronymic from his biological father.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Identity Notes ===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Digital Phantoms: The name "Bezaleel Brown" often appears in modern databases for this individual, but this is likely a retroactive assignment to account for the son’s surname. 
2 CONT * Historical Context: In the mid-18th century, it was common for children born prior to a formal marriage to be raised by a stepfather. In this case, Robert Harris appears to have fully integrated the boy into his family, though t
2 CONC he biological father's identity remained unrecorded in surviving civil or parish documents.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT == Family ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Ex-partner:
2 CONT * Lucretia "Lucy" Brown (1746–1806)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT * Bezaleel Brown (1760–c. 1778)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT * Albemarle County, Virginia: Absence of marriage bonds for Lucretia Brown prior to 1762.
2 CONT * Woods, Edgar. Albemarle County in Virginia, 1901.
2 CONT * Analysis of the Brown and Harris administrative settlements in Albemarle County.
