2 CONC om/people/Elizabeth-Brown-died-young/6000000225108008960?through=6000000014301728338.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Brown (1744–bef. 1762); born in Hanover Co.; m. John Price. She was a daughter of Benjamin Brown and Sarah Thompson.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==== Marriage and Death ====
2 CONT She is believed to have married a '''Mr. Price''', a connection supported by early family narratives. Her death is estimated around 1762, the same year as her father’s death. Her father’s will (Albemarle County Will Book 2, Page 1
2 CONC 30) provides the primary framework for identifying his children, though forensic auditing is required to separate the two distinct sets of siblings raised together at Walnut Level.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT * '''Albemarle County Will Book 2, Page 130:''' Will of Benjamin Brown, Sr. (1762).
2 CONT * '''Brown Family Bible:''' Transcribed by Eleanor Williams Bradley, ''Virginia Genealogist'', Vol. 13, 1969.
2 CONT * '''Reuben Dabney Brown Manuscript:''' "Family of Benjamin Brown, Sr.," records of the grandson of Sarah Thompson.
2 CONT * '''Identity Audit:''' Resolution of the Wilson/Thompson sibling conflation in the Brown's Cove lineage.
