1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT William Brown was born on January 2, 1747, in Albemarle County, Virginia. He was a son of Benjamin Brown (d. 1762) and Sarah Thompson (1724–1815).
2 CONT
2 CONT Unlike his half-brother "Billy" Brown, who died during the Revolutionary War period, this William lived a notably long life. He witnessed the formation of the early Republic and died in Albemarle County on May 7, 1836, at the age 
2 CONC of 89. His extensive lifespan means he appears in later tax and land records that distinguish him from the earlier generation of the "B" Brown family in Brown’s Cove.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Disambiguation ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Because of the repetitive naming conventions utilized by the family, this individual is frequently conflated with:
2 CONT * **William "Billy" Brown (1735–1780):** His half-brother, who was a son of Benjamin Brown and his first wife, Miss Wilson. 
2 CONT * **William Gregory (1752–1835):** A neighbor in Albemarle County and son of Sarah (Thompson) Gregory. Though both had mothers named Sarah Thompson, they belong to entirely different paternal lineages.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT == Family ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT * Benjamin Brown (d. 1762) and Sarah Thompson (1724–1815)
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings:
2 CONT * Barzillai Brown (1747–c. 1813); twin. He was a son of Benjamin Brown and Sarah Thompson.
2 CONT * Elizabeth Brown (1744–bef. 1762). She was a daughter of Benjamin Brown and Sarah Thompson.
2 CONT * Lucretia "Lucy" Brown (1746–1806). She was a daughter of Benjamin Brown and Sarah Thompson.
2 CONT * Benajah Brown (1748–1814). He was a son of Benjamin Brown and Sarah Thompson.
2 CONT * Bernard Brown (1750–1800). He was a son of Benjamin Brown and Sarah Thompson.
2 CONT * Bernis Brown (1752–1814). He was a son of Benjamin Brown and Sarah Thompson.
2 CONT * Bezaleel Brown (1754–1829). He was a son of Benjamin Brown and Sarah Thompson.
2 CONT * Brightberry Brown (1762–1846). He was a son of Benjamin Brown and Sarah Thompson.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT * Albemarle County, Virginia: Death records and obituary notices, May 1836.
2 CONT * Pension and Land Records: Documentation distinguishing the younger William (d. 1836) from the elder William "Billy" (d. 1780).
2 CONT * Woods, Edgar. Albemarle County in Virginia, 1901.
