1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bernis Brown (1752–1814); born at Walnut Level; m. Henrietta Rodes. He was a son of Benjamin Brown and Sarah Thompson.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Rev. Bernis Brown'''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/86130722/bernis_brown
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernis Brown was one of the early Methodist preachers in Albemarle County, entering the ministry before the end of the eighteenth century. He also was a signer of the Albemarle County Declaration of Independence on 2 April 1779.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernis Brown married Henrietta Rhodes, daughter of John Rhodes and Sarah Harris. From this union were the following issues:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Sarah Brown, married Thomas Jones
2 CONT 2. Henrietta Brown, married John Ruff
2 CONT 3. Ann Brown, married John Dickerson
2 CONT 4. Judge Bernis Brown Jr., name of wife unknown, she died, leaving Bernis with 12 children. Emigrated to Saline County, Missouri.
2 CONT 5. Tyre Brown, born 13 Jun 1793, he married Sarah Nicholas at Rockingham County, Virginia.
2 CONT 6. Benjamin T. (Long Thompson) Brown, married Lucy Ann Richards who lived to the age of 90 years.
2 CONT 7. Elizabeth Brown
2 CONT 8. John R. Brown, married Candace Hall, no issues from this union.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: https://archive.org/stream/cu31924028785703/cu31924028785703_djvu.txt
