1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Dabney Brown was born on June 18, 1751, in Albemarle County, Virginia. He was a son of Benjamin Brown (d. 1762) and Sarah Thompson (1724–1815).
2 CONT
2 CONT Dabney was a member of the "B" Brown family of Brown’s Cove. His life was notably short; he passed away on June 22, 1773, at the age of 22. Because he died prior to the American Revolution and before the major westward migrations 
2 CONC of his siblings, he appears less frequently in secondary genealogical narratives than his brothers who lived into the 19th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Disambiguation ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Dabney Brown is often the subject of genealogical scrutiny regarding the "Dabney" surname in the Brown family:
2 CONT * Surnames as Given Names: His name reflects the close associations between the Brown, Thompson, and Dabney families in the Hanover and Albemarle regions. 
2 CONT * The "Dabney Fortune" Claim: He is sometimes confused with the lineage of his nephew, Dr. Charles Brown, who pursued a claim to a Dabney estate in England. However, the Dabney connection in Charles's line came through his mother,
2 CONC  Elizabeth Dabney, whereas for this Dabney Brown, it was a given name likely honoring family associates.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT == Family ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT * Benjamin Brown (d. 1762) and Sarah Thompson (1724–1815)
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings:
