2 CONT
2 CONT 1800 U.S. Reconstructed Census indicates Brightberry Brown was living in the District of Fredricksville Parish in Virginia. Fredricksville is a city on the Rappahannock River in Virginia, south of Washington, D.C. It is not in any
2 CONC  county as it has been an independent city since 1879. This is the only documentation found where Brightberry Brown is not residing in Albemarle County, Vrginiai.
2 CONT
2 CONT Until this very moment in time I had found no record of my ancestors owning slaves, of course, with them living in Virginia I knew it was possible. The following 1810 and 1830 census accounts has changed my life forever and I am t
2 CONC ruly saddened by this turn of events. To any descendants of people included in my family as slaves I humbly extend my sincere apology.
