2 CONT Alexanders, Our Family Legacy  Alexanders, Our Family Legacy  Jerry Lamar Alexander  Name: Jerry Lamar Alexander; Date: 2012;  @R16@  Y 
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT p. 276  0 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Celia was the daughter of Ratcliff Boon, Jr and Nancy Harris and the first wife of William (Hopping Billy) Alexander. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family stories passed down through the generations was that Celia was the most beautiful woman in Pickens County. People around the area called her the "Belle of the Keowee River."
2 CONT
2 CONT Celia hunted Ginseng most of her life, she along with most of the family used it to make medicine & tea. Family lore states she was in the woods hunting for 'sang' and was attacked by a bear, as she tried to climb a small tree, th
2 CONC e bear followed. She had to turn and fight the bear only having the Ginseng hoe to defend herself,  she killed the bear with that little hoe. That hoe has been passed down generation to generation for almost 200 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Exact date & cause of death is not known.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/128530759/celia-alexander Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 7 2023, 18:25:31 UTC''
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/128530759/celia-alexander
2 CONT ----
