2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph was born 05 Oct 1715 at Truro.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Rich fathered a child out of wedlock, Joseph Rich, born at Eastham, Massachusetts, on 21 Sep 1739, to Mercy Brown.[1] The mother may have been the Mercy Brown who married Simeon Newcomb in 1745; see the Research Note on her
2 CONC  profile for the evidence. There is no further record of the child, who probably died before the birth of his half-brother of the same name on 10 Nov 1761,
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Rich married 09 Mar 1742 at Truro Susanna Collins daughter of Jonathan and Elizabeth (Vickery) Collins
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Susanna b: 05 Feb 1743
2 CONT Richard b: 01 Jun 1748
2 CONT James b: 05 Jun 1750
2 CONT Anne b: 08 Oct 1752
2 CONT Sylvanus b: 05 Mar 1755
2 CONT Elizabeth b: 16 Apr 1757
2 CONT Deborah b: 08 Nov 1759
2 CONT Joseph b: 10 Nov 1761
2 CONT He died between 11 July 1783 and 18 August 1783 at Truro
2 CONT
2 CONT Probate
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of Joseph Rich of Truro, yeoman was dated 11 July 1783 and proved on 18 August 1783 in Barnstable. He mentioned his wife Susanna, and his children, Jonathan Rich, Richard Rich, Joseph Rich, Susanna Thayer, Anna Treat, Eli
2 CONC zabeth Holbrook, Sabra Rich, and James Rich (executor). [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT His inventory was taken on 9 October 1783 in Truro.[3] In 1784, his widow Susanna received her dower.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
