1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ~• This profile was first entered on GENi by me, MMvB, on June 23, 2020.<br/>
2 CONT According to the extensive diary of [https://www.geni.com/people/John-Dyer/6000000007418598860 '''''John Dyer'''''], this Jonathan? Wells' parents did not always get along. Mother Mary left her husband [https://www.geni.com/people
2 CONC /Jonathan-Wells-who-moved-to-Goshen-Chester-County/6000000001045185278 Jonathan (Sr.)] for a while in the 1790s. I wonder if she took her children with her when she left her husband in Chester County and went back to Plumstead/Buc
2 CONC kingham, where both she and her husband were born? No, for these children would have been grown and married. After all, by 1795 her purported grandson Valentine would have been 11 years old
2 CONT
2 CONT I irks me is that I do not have a confirmed list of https://www.geni.com/people/Jonathan-Wells-who-moved-to-Goshen-Chester-County/6000000001045185278 and his wife Mary's children. We do know that Mary outlived her husband. Much wo
2 CONC rk needs to be done on sourcing here.<br/>
2 CONT Central to the sourcing process here are: [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000075610148855 tax records of the 1780s]
2 CONT
2 CONT It is doubtful that Jonathan(?) Wells is the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Jonathan-Wells/6000000076169146925 as that man was married in 1761 which would mean that he was born on or before 18 years earlier (1743). htt
2 CONC ps://www.geni.com/people/Jonathan-Wells-who-moved-to-Goshen-Chester-County/6000000001045185278 was born c. 1733. That would make him too young to be his father.
