2 CONC 9 and settled in Rapho Township, Lancaster Co.,PA.  His father, a weaver, lived and is buried in teh CAnton of Bern,Switzerland.  The number of his offspring was corrected from theearlier records and is reflected here on his memor
2 CONC ial stone placed inthe Wenger cemetery in 1994.  His will was dated Sept. 15, 1771 andprobated June 1, 1772 so his date of death is sometime between thesetwo dates.  His son John was executor.  Hans is no doubt buried in theWenger
