2 CONT Judith Wenger born January 13, 1732, died March 4, 1812. She was born in Switzerland although one sources says that she was born inRhenish Bavaria, Palatinate, Germany. She married Martin Funck in 1759 and lived on a farm near Leb
2 CONC anon where the Bethlehem Steel Plant is located. Judith was a Mennonite. She and her husband were buried in the Funck farm graveyard but was moved in 1898 to Ebenezer Cemetery, north of Lebanon City when the Bethleham Steel Plantd
2 CONC  was built. She is a twin to John Wenger. Arrived on the Ship "Patience" with her father Johannes Wenger on Sept. 16, 1748
2 CONT --------------------
