2 CONT Judith Funck (Wenger) Judith Wenger born January 13, 1732, died March 4, 1812. She was born in Switzerland although one source says that she was born in Rhenish Bavaria, Palatinate, Germany. She married Martin Funck in 1759 and li
2 CONC ved on a farm near Lebanon where the Bethlehem Steel Plant is located. Judith was a Mennonite. She and her husband were buried in the Funck Farm graveyard but was moved in 1898 to Ebenezer Cemetery, north of Lebanon City when the 
2 CONC Bethlehem Steel Plant was built. She is a twin to John Wenger. Arrived on the ship “Patience” with her father Johannes Wenger on September 16, 1748.
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith was born on January 19, 1732 in Seftigen, Bern, Switzerland. She was the daughter of Johannes Wenger and Anna Shirk. She married Martin Funk, Sr., in 1759 in Quittapahilla Creek, Lebanon, PA. She passed away on March 4, 181
2 CONC 2 in Lebanon, PA. She is buried in the Covenant Greenwood Cemetery in Ebenezer, PA (formerly Ebenezer Cemetery)
