1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *This memorial is a cenotaph which is permissible under Findagrave guidelines because a memorial stone with his name is located at the Wenger Meeting House Cemetery in Jonestown, Pennsylvania.*
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry was the sixth child of Johannes 'Hans' Wenger and Anna Shirk (Sherrick). The family of ten immigrated to Philadelphia together on September 16,1748 aboard the ship Patience.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry moved near Oil City in Venango County and owned land on the west bank of the river. He married a Seneca Indian woman named Sarah. He sold that land and most researchers believe he moved to Canada during the American Revoluti
2 CONC on because he was a Tory.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry may have changed his name to 'Winger.' His descendants have sometimes been confused with those of Lazarus Wengert (1715-1796 Berks Co. PA). According to many family trees he may have been the father of the following children
2 CONC :
2 CONT
2 CONT 1-Henry Wenger, Jr. (1762- ?) 2-Joseph Wenger (1782 Venago Co. PA- ?) married 1807, son Benjamin Wenger (1808) 3-Josiah Wenger (1784 Venango Co. PA- 1812)
2 CONT
