1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Felix Light had been an effective minister in the Mennonite Church. He became a United Brethren preacher, even though there is no indication that he was ever formally licensed or ordained as such. He is the father 
2 CONC of 3 UB preachers Casper Light (1804-1857), John Light (1808-1845) Joseph Light (1813-1870); grandfather of 4 UB preachers Rudolph Light (1826-?), Ezekiel Light (1834-1903), Job Light (1839-1888) and Joel Light (1840-1904); and gr
2 CONC eat-grandfather of 1 UB preacher John C.H. Light (1872-1950). Gibble's 1951 History of the East Pennsylvania Conference, page 40, gives a detailed account of the extended Light ministerial family. The 1911 Eberly-Albright-Brane La
2 CONC ndmark History of the United Brethren Church, page 207, gives a brief biography of Felix Light and, on page 209, the story of Light's meeting house. 
2 CONT --------------------
