1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rezin married Nancy Ann (or Frances) GROVES.
2 CONT
2 CONT Childrens: Samuel GREGG Elma Maria GREGG Eliza May GREGG  m. William J. GREGG Priscilla GREGG Louisa GREGG Aaron GREGG Mary Ann GREGG Schenck  Rezin GREGG
2 CONT * Updated from [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=55254513 Find A Grave Memorial] via son [http://www.geni.com/profile-34680975394 Aaron Gregg] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: '
2 CONC 'Nov 25 2015, 18:43:31 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Well, I can't tell you about their marriage, but I can tell you about Rezin. This is from howard Lechey's Tenmile Country & Its Pioneer Families. Resiz is listed along with 10 other children in a Gregg Family Bible. It gives his b
2 CONC irth dated 30 Nov 1783, died 25 July 1843, married (according to this) Frances Grove. Rezin was the 5th child. Siblings: Meylon, Ruth, Permelia, Priscilla,Craven, Presley, Aaron, Pera, Susannah, and Alford.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rezin and other children were the children of Richard and Ann Gregg Gregg. Richard was born 5 Mar 1752 and died in Greene Co., PA 15 Nov 1812. His will is in Greene Co will book 1 pp. 108 and was probated 15 April 1813. Richard Gr
2 CONC egg served in Captain William Crawford's Company of the Fifth Battalion Washington Co Militia. ( PA archives Series VI, Vo. 2, pp 166) He married about 1775 to Ann Gregg, born 5 May 1756, daughter of Samuel & Elizabeth Alford Greg
2 CONC g. She died in 1817 in Greene Co., PA.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a good deal more on the Greggs in this book. You need to get a copy. FYI Samuel Gregg was born in Ireland and acmae to US to Loudon Co., VA where he died and will on file 7 April 1803. The other Gregg family goes back to 
2 CONC about 1695 and also is discussed in Ireland and possible origins in Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT As for the Grove lady. Nothing more.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genforum.genealogy.com/pa/greene/messages/236.html
