1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Children taken from:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~familiesareforever/pafg1393.htm#34900
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Francis SEATON   1758.Winchester,Frederick.Co,VA-08JUN1820.Knox.IN 
2 CONT
2 CONT ..May have been referred to as 'Esquire' which probably was a title rather than name.
2 CONT
2 CONT BUR: Upper Indiana Cemetery 2 1/2 miles Northeast of Vincennes IN.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He warranted 360 1/2 acres of land called "Elizabeth" in Washington/Greene Co. PA area on 26MAY1765.  He surveyed this land in 1794 and patented the land on 27OCT1801 to Wm. S. & Margaret E. CARMICHEAL(Horn Papers p.46:170). He wa
2 CONC s listed as a 'distiller' in the 1798 Greene Co. PA Tax rolls and is also known to have owned a 'Grist Mill' on Muddy Creek in Cumberland Twp., Greene Co. PA.  Flour ground in his Grist Mill was shipped to Spanish controlled New O
2 CONC rleans down the Ohio and Mississippi thru Indian Country in casks on keel boats.  
2 CONT
2 CONT During the Revolutionary War, he served in the 8th PA Regiment of the Continental Line and was an ensign in Crawford's Militia Company.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He married .c1780 New Castle, DE Rebecca GREGG(1758DE-1822IN d/o John & Susannah ).  
2 CONT
2 CONT He died 01NOV1820 in Knox Co. IN.
2 CONT
2 CONT FATHER: [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=seaton&GSfn=james&GSbyrel=in&GSdy=1779&GSdyrel=in&GSob=n&GRid=15065843& James SEATON]
2 CONT
2 CONT MOTHER: Elizabeth KENNER died after 1800 near Carmicheals, Greene Co,PA.
