2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sergeant William Larrison served with 1st Regiment, Hunterdon County Militia, New Jersey Militia during the American Revolution.
2 CONT
2 CONT WikiTree contributors, "William Larrison (abt.1708-1777)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Larrison-98 : accessed 17 August 2024).
2 CONT
2 CONT William Larrison was the son of William Larrison of New Brunswick Township, Middlesex County, New Jersey. He is listed in his father William Larrison's will dated 7 April 1749.[1] He is estimated as born about 1708 in New Jersey, 
2 CONC roughly aligned with his siblings.
2 CONT
2 CONT He served as Sergeant in 1st Hunterdon County Militia with Captain William Tucker.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Patience ___.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Larison wrote his will on 1 Sept 1777 in Roxbury Township, Morris County, New Jersy. The estate passed probate in 1777 in Morris, New Jersey, United States.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT His will listed his wife Patience, sons Andrew, James and David, and daughters Elizabeth, Mary and Nancy.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT * William Lawrason, Thomas Larrison, James Lawrason, Andrew Lawrason
2 CONT
2 CONT This William ?
2 CONT
2 CONT Citing this Record
2 CONT *"Pennsylvania Births and Christenings, 1709-1950," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:V2NJ-L7F : 11 February 2018), William Larrisson, 24 Aug 1707; Christening, citing FIRST PRESBYTERIAN CHURCH,PHILAD
2 CONC ELPHIA,PHILADELPHIA,PENNSYLVANIA; FHL microfilm 974.8 B2P V.19
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT From:BELL, NIXON, BARROWS, McKINLEY, COOPER FAMILIES by Judie Clarkare many spellings of the last name in this family: Laurenson, Larrison, Lorrison, Larison, Lorison, Larisun, Larason...take your pick. Larisun Familie History see
2 CONC ms to skip William's generation and attaches his son James to William's father John. The age difference would make this possible, but considering that John died before the birth of at least some of Williams children, it become imp
2 CONC ossible. A Chronical of Everyday People does name these children of William.
2 CONT
2 CONT "A Chronicle of Everyday People" States that William is known to have been with an emigration from Newtown and the Inventory of the estate of Theophilius Phillips of Maidenhead, NJ has the item of L131-11s-2d due from William Lari
2 CONC son March 19th, 1708/09. 1708/10 he settled near what now is Hopewell, NJ. He was on the tax list of Hunterdon Co., in 1722.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Pioneers of Old Hopewell"do make and Constitute my beloved son John Larison and son-in-law David Stout to be my executors of this my will and do Empower them to Collect in my debts and dispose of my Estate to the best advantage a
2 CONC t discretion of my Executors and after paying my Just Debts Funeral Charges and my aforesaid Legacy to Divide the remainder as aforesaid among my aforesaid sons William Thomas John and George and I do hereby revoke and Disannul al
2 CONC l other Wills, Whatsoever heretofore by me made Ratifying and Conforming this and only this to be my Last Will and Testament. "In witness Whereof I the said William Larison have hereunto set my hand & seal this seventh day of Apri
2 CONC l in the year of our Lord Christ one thousand seven hundred and forty nine. (David Stout was husband of daughter Elizabeth) William Larison "Witnesses Jediah Higgins-Samuel Wilson and Robert Rolfe"
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT From:BELL, NIXON, BARROWS, McKINLEY, COOPER FAMILIES by Judie Clark There are many spellings of the last name in this family: Laurenson, Larrison, Lorrison, Larison, Lorison, Larisun, Larason...take your pick.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Larisun Familie History seems to skip William's generation and attaches his son James to William's father John. The age difference would make this possible, but considering that John died before the birth of at least some of W
2 CONC illiams children, it become impossible. A Chronical of Everyday People does name these children of William.
2 CONT
2 CONT "A Chronicle of Everyday People" States that William is known to have been with an emigration from Newtown and the Inventory of the estate of Theophilius Phillips of Maidenhead, NJ has the item of L131-11s-2d due from William Lari
2 CONC son March 19th, 1708/09. 1708/10 he settled near what now is Hopewell, NJ. He was on the tax list of Hunterdon Co., in 1722.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Pioneers of Old Hopewell" I do make and Constitute my beloved son John Larison and son-in-law David Stout to be my executors of this my will and do Empower them to Collect in my debts and dispose of my Estate to the best advantag
2 CONC e at discretion of my Executors and after paying my Just Debts Funeral Charges and my aforesaid Legacy to Divide the remainder as aforesaid among my aforesaid sons William Thomas John and George and I do hereby revoke and Disannul
2 CONC  all other Wills, Whatsoever heretofore by me made Ratifying and Conforming this and only this to be my Last Will and Testament. "In witness Whereof I the said William Larison have hereunto set my hand & seal this seventh day of A
2 CONC pril in the year of our Lord Christ one thousand seven hundred and forty nine. (David Stout was husband of daughter Elizabeth)
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed William Larison "Witnesses Jediah Higgins-Samuel Wilson and Robert Rolfe"
