1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Kesiah Larison
2 CONT *Birth:	1725 - New Brunswick, Middlesex Co., NJ
2 CONT *Parents:	William Larison, Anna Larison (born Pashuns)
2 CONT *Siblings:	James Larison, Thomas Larison, John Larison, William Larison, Martha Larison, William Larison, Mary Larrison, Elizabeth Garrison (born Larison), Rebecca Larison, Deborah Larison, George Larison
2 CONT *Marriage to: Willem van Tilburg Dec 20 1745  Somerville, Somerset Co, New Jersey, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT William (Willem) was born 1720 in Port Richmond, Staten Island, New York. His father was Pieter Johannsen Van Tilburg and his mother was Metie Bouwman. He was Christened 11 Dec 1720 in the Dutch Reformed Church in Port Richmond, N
2 CONC ew York.
2 CONT
2 CONT Willem married Keziah Larison on Dec 20, 1745 in Somerset County, New Jersey. Her parents were William Larisaon and Anna Pashuns. After their marriage, they resided in Kingston, Somerset County, New Jersey. William’s occupation wa
2 CONC s a tavern owner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were
2 CONT
2 CONT #Johannes Van Tilburgh 1751 - 1826
2 CONT #Henry Van Tilburgh 1756 - 1842
2 CONT
2 CONT It is likely that Gen Washington or his troops visited the Sign of the Mermaid Tavern owned by William Van Tilburgh.
2 CONT
2 CONT Record show that William married Rebecca about 1760 (b, 1739). There is no record to indicate Willem and Kesiah divorced, but records evidenced Kesiah died in 1791.
2 CONT
