2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {{New Netherland Settler}}In April, 1665 Anne's father James set sail for America from England in Philip Carteret's ship, ''''Philip''," with about thirty passengers.There is no surviving passenger list. However, it is known that 
2 CONC the passengers included James Bollen. James then settled in northeastern New Jersey, under British rule (since Sept. 1664) of this part of New Netherland as it was in dispute for the next decade until full Dutch capitulation in 16
2 CONC 74. No doubt Anne came with her parents on that same ship, or was born here after arrival.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT Anna Bollen, daughter of James Bollen, Secretary of the Province, married Jonathan Stout, son of Richard and Penelope Kent Van Princin Stout, August 27 1685.  With the death of James Bollen in 1682, Anna and her brother James chos
2 CONC e Samuel Moore and Nathaniel Fitzrandolph as their guardians.  She married Jonathan Stout, son of Richard and Penelope Kent Van Princin Stout, August 27 1685.
2 CONT
