2 CONT Son of Richard Stout and Penelope Van Princes (Van Prince, Prince). Husband of Anna Bollen.
2 CONT
2 CONT One of their sons, Jonathan Stout (1660 - 1722), moved westward and helped establish the town of Hopewell, in Hunterdon Co., New Jersey. Several generations of Stouts followed in the Hopewell area, some of whom founded and were as
2 CONC sociated with the Hopewell Baptist Church and meeting place. The church building, established in 1715 and rebuilt in 1822, still stands as a historical site in Hopewell.  (wdgordon.com, Stout Family History,)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan and Anna lived on a farm at Hopewell, south of Amwell township. Together with Nathan Drake, John Hart, and the Bowne Family, Jonathan helped establish the Baptist Church of Hopewell. For forty-one years the meetings were 
2 CONC held at the home of Jonathan or at that of one of his children, before a meetinghouse was built in the early 1700's.
2 CONT
2 CONT Suggested by Delores Rush 
2 CONT p. 5 = https://archive.org/details/stoutalliedfamil00stou/page/4/mode/2up/search/Baptist
