1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT Benjamin Stout, son of Jonathan and Anne Bollen Stout, was born December 14 1691 in Middletown, NJ and died February 8 1772 in Hopewell, Hunterdon County, New Jersey.  He married Hannah Bonham born 1695, daughter of Hezekiah and M
2 CONC ary Dunn Bonham.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref: “The Bonham Family'', SamuelJeremah Bonham. 1955, page 27 [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=wu.89062850912;view=1up;seq=91 Hathitrust] ''Bonham, 1631-1973. Letters, quotations, genealogical charts, military record, dire
2 CONC ctory index. '', Emmet Lincoln Smith, 1973 page 19 [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=wu.89062850920;view=1up;seq=579 Hathitrust]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a descendant of Edward Fuller who signed the Mayflower Compact and Captain Francis Drake, relative of Sir Francis Drake.  
2 CONT
2 CONT They were the parents of:
2 CONT #Jonathan
2 CONT #Hezekiah
2 CONT #Benjamin
2 CONT #Ezekiel
2 CONT #Hosea, all of whom were early settlers in Harrison County, WV. 
2 CONT #Nathaniel
2 CONT #Hannah
2 CONT #Mary
2 CONT #Sarah all remained in New Jersey.  
2 CONT
2 CONT From The History of the Stout Family, First Settling in Middletown, Monmouth County, New Jersey By Nathan Stout, 1823 Second printing by H.G. McCarter, "Herald" Office, Hopewell, N.J., 1878 with additions by Mrs. Sarah Weart, Thir
2 CONC d printing in 1906 by Joab B. Stout, with additions and corrections. Fourth printing in 1929 by George A. Chandler, Bethlehem, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://files.usgwarchives.net/nj/monmouth/history/family/stout01.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT “I shall now introduce Benjamin, a brother of Zebulon, whose family I have last delineated. Benjamin was born in the year 1696, and married Hannah Bonham by whom he had six sons and three daughters, viz: Jonathan, Hezekiah, Benjam
2 CONC in, Nathaniel, Ezekiel, Hosea and Mary, Hannah and Sarah. Jonathan married a woman by the name of Jewell, and raised a large family of children and lived till he was a hundred years old.  Hezekiah married a widow Smith, they had n
2 CONC o children, and after her death he married a widow Sortor, with whom he lived until he was between ninety and a hundred years old, and died without issue.  Benjamin married Rebecca Dulhangal, by whom he had a large family of child
2 CONC ren, and after her death he married Martha Skyhauk and had another large family of children.  Nathaniel married Charity Furman, by whom he had one child, a daughter, whose name was Rhoda.  She married Zephaniah Stout, and had issu
2 CONC e.  After his death she married Burges Allison, by whom she had children.  Ezekiel married a Drake by whom he had a large family of children.  Hesea went into the back parts of Virginia a single man, where he married and raised a 
2 CONC large family of children, as I have been informed.  Mary married William Heabron, and had by him two sons and one daughter, viz; John, William and Hannah.  Hannah married David Ollivent, and raised a family of children.  Sarah mar
2 CONC ried Andrew Bray and died without issue.”
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Note
2 CONT
2 CONT There are various spellings of the spouses of Benjamin and Hannah's spouses.  The ones used are from Russell Ray Stout's book "Richard Stouts Descendants in West Virginia" 1966 page 19.   "CHAPTER VI THE BENJAMIN AND REBECCA DOOLH
2 CONC AGEN--MARTHA SCHENK STOUT FAMILY"
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT *“'An American Family History:Hannah Bonham Stout'', Roberta Fuller, 2017 [http://www.anamericanfamilyhistory.com/Bonham%20Family/BonhamHannahStout.html Link]
2 CONT *JonathanStout “Historical and genealogical miscellany"John Stillwell, 1916, page 333 [http://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal04stil#page/333/mode/1up/search/jewel archive.Org]
2 CONT * Richard Stout Descendants in West Virginia", Russell Ray Stout, 1966, page 7 [https://books.google.com/books/about/Richard_Stout_Descendants_in_West_Virgin.html?id=IN5jHAAACAAJ GoogleBooks]
2 CONT * “History of the Stout Family", Nathan Stout, 1823 page 9-10 http://files.usgwarchives.net/nj/monmouth/history/family/stout01.txt Jonathan m Hannah Jewell, Hezekiah m (1) Widow Smith (2) Widow Epenetus Sortor
2 CONT *"The Sortor Family: Family Documents: Wills of Sortore and Allied Families" www.sortore.com  Benjamin m (1) Rebecca Doolhagen (2) Martha Schenk, Nathaniel m Charity Furman, Ezekiel m Miss Drake, Hosea went to Virginia, Mary m Wil
2 CONC liam Heabron, Hannah m David Ollivant and Sarah m Andrew Bray.  
