2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {{New Netherland Descendant}}
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT Zebulon Stout, son of Jonathan and Anne Bollen Stout, was born March 14 1700 and died August 27 1788.  He married Charity Burroughs (Burrows). The living children are named in his will proved September 10 1788 along with grandchil
2 CONC dren: Rachel's sons, Stout Brinson and Zebulon Brinson, Sarah's daughters, Lorany Bryant and Charity Sortor, Mary's daughter, Ann (Amy) Rodgers<ref>Hutchinson, Elmer T. Ed. ''Archives of theState of New Jersey.'' First Series. Vol
2 CONC  XXXVI. Vol VII of Calendar of wills 1786-1790. MacCrellish & Quigley Co. Printers. Trenton, N. J.:1941. Pages 217-218. https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.39015026886682;view=1up;seq=219</ref>
2 CONT They were the parents of:<ref>Stout, Nathan. ''History of the Stout Family.'' Monmouth County, N. J. Nathan Stout:1823. Page 8 http://files.usgwarchives.net/nj/monmouth/history/family/stout01.txt</ref>#John born 1730, married Mabe
2 CONC l Sexton<ref>Ege, Ralph. ''Pioneers of Old Hopewell.'' Paterson, N. J. Race and Savige:1908. page 251 https://archive.org/details/pioneersoldhope00egegoog/page/n260</ref>#Zebulon Jr married (1) Sarah Stout m Oct 11 1762 <ref>Nelso
2 CONC n, William, Ed. ''Documents relating to the Colonial History of the State of NewJersey.'' Vol XXII. Marriage Records 1665-1800. Paterson, N. J. The Press Printing and Publishing  Co.:1900. Page 388. https://archive.org/stream/marr
2 CONC iagerecords103nels#page/388/mode/1up</ref>(2) Widow Sutphin<ref>Stout, Nathan. 1823. Page 9 http://files.usgwarchives.net/nj/monmouth/history/family/stout01.txt</ref>#Anne, married Ichabod Leigh Jul 12 1744<ref>Nelson, William. 19
2 CONC 00. Page 387. https://archive.org/stream/marriagerecords103nels#page/387/mode/1up</ref>#Rachel married (1) __________Brinson, (2) Stephen Barton (Bartow?) Dec 22 1747<ref>Nelson, William. 1900. Page 387. https://archive.org/stream
2 CONC /marriagerecords103nels#page/387/mode/1u/p</ref>#Mary married (1) __________ Rodgers, (2) Francis Carbines Mar 14 1790<ref>Nelson, William. 1900. Page 387 https://archive.org/stream/marriagerecords103nels#page/387/mode/1up</ref>#C
2 CONC harity married Nathaniel Stout, son of David and Ann Merrill Stout.<ref>Stout, Nathan. ''History of the Stout Family'', Nathan Stout, 1823, Page 26. http://files.usgwarchives.net/nj/monmouth/history/family/stout01.txt</ref>#Sarah 
2 CONC married (1) Abraham Skillman (2) Nathaniel Stout, widow of her sister Charity, Jun 4 1764.<ref>Nelson, William. 1900. Page 375 https://archive.org/stream/marriagerecords103nels#page/375/mode/1up</ref><ref>''Historical and genealog
2 CONC ical miscellany'', John E Stillwell, 1916, Vol V, page 334 http://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal04stil#page/334/mode/1up</ref><ref>Stout, Nathan. 1823, Page 8. http://files.usgwarchives.net/nj/monmouth/history/family/stout01.
2 CONC txt</ref> 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Research Note==In Zebulon's will there is no child named Hannah as given in William RStout's, unsourced family tree, who married John Brinson, son of Barefoot and Mary Popinga.  It also names Stout and Zebulon as their sons alon
2 CONC g with two other.  His will names their mother as Rachel Barton (Bartow) which is in conflict with this source, states John married an Arrowsmith and was named in his father's will along with his children, Daniel and Mary.<ref>Som
2 CONC erset Historical Quarterly, A. Van Doren Honeyman, Ed., 1914, Vol III, "The Brunson (Brinson - Bryson) Family, William H Benedict, p. 289 https://play.google.com/books/reader?id=vxFJAQAAMAAJ&printsec=frontcover&output=reader&hl=en
2 CONC &pg=GBS.PA289</ref> It appears that Nathan Stout cited above may have begun this error and John E Stillwell, who used Stout as a source, perpetuated it.  Clearly, in the will Rachel Barton is identified as the mother of two grands
2 CONC ons: Stout Brinson and Zebulon Brinson.  There is a bond against Stephen Barton, Rachel's current husband.  This is also true for two granddaughters, Charity Sortor and Larany Bryant, and children of Charity,  his deceased daughte
2 CONC r.  Natte (Nathaniel) Stout, her widower married Sarah, her sister who was a widow and has a bond against him for the two girls. 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
