2 CONT Zebulon STOUT was born in Feb 1699 in Middletown, Monmouth Co., New Jersey. He was Slave Owner on 27 Oct 1735 in Somerset Co., NJ. (259) Tom (a Negro), age c. 35 - runaway from Zebulon Stout of Somerset Co., N .J. He signed a will
2 CONC  on 7 Apr 1788.(260) .........Barton, as part of said legacy. Daughter, Sarah Stout, also 1 /4, and after her death, to her heirs and my grandchildren, Lorany Brya nt and Charity Sortor; allowing a bond I have against her husband,
2 CONC  Natt e Stout. Daughter, Mary Corbine, also 1/4, and after her death, to her h eirs and my granddaughter, Ann (Amy) Rodgers; allowing a bond I have ag ainst her husband, Francis Corbine, in part of said legacy. Sons, John a nd Zeb
2 CONC ulon, debt I have against Thomas Allen, John and Peter Nephew, Da niel McCarty and Jessey Hart. Exectutors -- sons, John and Zebulon. W itnesses --Nathaniel Stout, Sr., Susanna Gordon, Peter Gordon. Proved S ept 10, 1788. 
