2 CONT Samuel Stout Sr, son of Jonathan and Anne Bollen Stout, born 1709 in New Jersey.  He married (1) Catherine Simpson Stout, widow of his cousin James Stout in 1729.  <ref>''A General History of The Baptist Denomination in America, a
2 CONC nd other parts of the World '', David Benedict, Vol 1, page 571 https://books.google.com/books?id=fMI4AAAAMAAJ&q=samuel+stout#v=snippet&q=samuel%20stout&f=false </ref><ref>''Pioneers of Old Hopewell'', Ralph Ege, 1908, page page 2
2 CONC 61-ff https://archive.org/stream/pioneersoldhope00egegoog#page/n270/mode/1up/search/samuel+stout</ref>, <ref>''History of the Stout Family'', Nathan Stout, 1823, page 10 http://files.usgwarchives.net/nj/monmouth/history/family/sto
2 CONC ut01.txt</ref> <ref>''Historical and genealogical miscellany'', John Stillwell, 1916,page 335 http://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal04stil#page/335/mode/1up]</ref> She was the mother of seven children one of whom wasonly four 
2 CONC years younger than him.   After Catherine's death in 1749 he married the widow Limbrook  (Neeltje Tenbroek De Witt ) More about them may be found here. <ref>Ralph Ege, 1908, page 263 https://archive.org/stream/pioneersoldhope00ege
2 CONC goog#page/n272/mode/1up/search/samuel+stout</ref> <ref>Find A Grave Tombstone  https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=pv&GRid=68941312&PIpi=41756741</ref> <ref>Nathan Stout, page 10 http://files.usgwarchives.net/nj/monmout
2 CONC h/history/family/stout01.txt</ref><ref>John Stillwell, page 334 http://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal04stil#page/334/mode/1up</ref> The child of Samuel Sr and Catherine Stout was Samuel Jr and the children of Samuel Sr and Ne
2 CONC eltje Stout were Jonathan m Sarah Phillips and Andrew. <ref>Nathan Stout, page 10 http://files.usgwarchives.net/nj/monmouth/history/family/stout01.txt</ref><ref>John Stillwell, page 334 http://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal04
