1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT 'Polly'- a daughter of Freegift Stout II, son of Freegift Stout I & Mary Higgins 
2 CONT and of Elizabeth Stout a daughter of David Stout and Elizabeth Larrison.
2 CONT -
2 CONT Pennsylvania Marriages Prior to 1790
2 CONT Pennsylvania Marriages; C.1778, May 1. Crawford, Elijah, and Elizabeth Stout; Page 237
2 CONT -
2 CONT Her death from Elijah's Pension File.
2 CONT -
2 CONT Her burial from "Volume 3, Washington, PA Cemetery Records"
2 CONT -
2 CONT Parents from: "Historical & Genealogical Miscellany, NY & NJ, Vol 4, #42" 
2 CONT -
2 CONT  "Commemorative Biographical Record of Washington County, Pennsylvania, containing..." J.H.Beers & Co., 1893, Chicago.
2 CONT -
2 CONT Elizabeth'Polly' Stout Crafford TIMELINE
2 CONT 1755/60-1837
2 CONT
2 CONT 1757-60-Elizabeth 'Polly' Stout was born possibly in NJ; daughter of Freegift Stout & Elizabeth Stout (2nd cousin) U.S.and International Marriage Records, 1560-1900 :
2 CONT Name: Freegift Stout, Birth Year: 1724, Spouse Name: Elizabeth Stout (daughter of David Stout & Elizabeth Larrison)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1778– Elizabeth 'Polly' Stout married Elijah Crafford” PA Marriages says May 1, 1778, probably date of intention published Pennsylvania Marriages Prior to 1790; [p.237] 1778, May 1.Stout, Elizabeth, and Elijah Crawford. Marriage l
2 CONC icense issued by Lewis Gordon, Esq. of Northampton Co, PA
2 CONT Marriage date 22 June 1778 at Northampton Co, PA.
2 CONT -
2 CONT Elizabeth had six known children:
2 CONT 1. Elizabeth Crafford, b.1779 Northampton Co, PA; d. bef 1828 (assume Washington Co, PA)Elizabeth married George P Jackson, son of Joesph Jackson andElizabeth. She had 12 known children.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.Joseph Crafford, b. 11 Oct 1780 Northampton Co, PA, d. 19 Feb 1863Macomb, McDonough, IL; He married Deborah Jackson, daughter of JosephJackson and Elizabeth.
2 CONT Theyhad 12 known children.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.Anne or Anna Crafford, b. abt 1781, probably Northampton Co, PA, d.aft 1860; she married Phelom or Felem Boyles abt 1800; they had 5known children.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.Freegift Crafford, b. 22 Oct 1785 at Northampton Co, PA; d. 15 Sep1854 in Washington Co, PA; he married Sarah Cole 12 Jan 1811,probably at Washington Co, PA; they had 5 known children.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.Rebecca Crafford, b. abt 1786/87 in Northampton Co, PA; she married Thomas Thomson; they had 2 known children.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.Isaac Crafford, b. 1794 probably in Northampton Co, PA; d. 10 May1824; he married Effie; they had 4 known children.
2 CONT -
2 CONT 1811– Elizabeth, Elijah and family removed to Washington Co, PA about the time of 1803-1811, depending on the source of information, where they took up a large farm in Smith /Hanover Twp.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1836– Elijah died, bequeathed to Elizabeth: “I give and bequeath to my wife Elizabeth one case of drawers one bed and bedding one horse and one cow her choice of my stock her saddle and bridle one spinning wheel and as much of my 
2 CONC kitchen furniture as she may choose all in perpetuity together with a comfortable maintenance from my two sons Joseph and Isaac hereinafter directed and full possession of the best room in my house on the place where I now live du
2 CONC ring her natural life.” From the Will of Elijah Crafford Washington Co, PA Will Book 5, Pgs 243-44 LDS Film#0863626.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1836– 18 April 1836 Elizabeth signed her Will with her mark; items mentioned in her will include her cow, large chest, large kettle,armed chair, bake iron, copper tea kettle, bedstead, stand of curtains, silver tea spoons, linen t
2 CONC able cloth, table, small trunk,china, glassware, Delf and Queensware, bed, wearing apparel, and looking glass; she named Isaac, her son as Executor; Witnesses, James McFarren and John Horner. From the Will of Elizabeth Crafford,Wa
2 CONC shington Co, PA, Will Book 5, Pages 308-9. LDS Film#0863626.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1837– Elizabeth died before 11 Jan 1837, the date her will was probated.
2 CONT Elizabeth is buried at the cemetery at Florence Presbyterian Church (Old Crossroads Presbyterian Graveyard), Florence, Washington, PA. Source: Volume 3, Washington, PA Cemetery Records.
2 CONT -
2 CONT WILL OF ELIZABETH CRAFFORD
2 CONT Dated 8 April 1836
2 CONT Probated: 11 Jan 1837
2 CONT Smith Twp, Washington Co, PA
2 CONT Will Book 5 Pages 308-309
2 CONT
2 CONT The last will and testament of Elisabeth Crafford of Hanover Township Washington County
2 CONT Witnesseth that I dispose of my worldly good[s] and Chattles in the following manner viz I give and bequeath to my son Isaac Crafford my cow my chest my large kettle my armed chair my bake-iron and I also direct that a note I hold
2 CONC  upon my said son Isaac shall be given up to him without payment
2 CONT I give and bequeath to my grand-daughter July Ann Crafford my copper tea kittle my bedstead and stand of curtains
2 CONT I give and bequeath to my grand-daughter Elizabeth Huffman my silver tea spoons
2 CONT I give and bequeath to my grand-son Isaac Crafford my linen table Cloth
2 CONT I give and bequeath to my grand-son Robert Crafford my table and small trunk
2 CONT I direct my cupboard furniture consisting of China Glass delf [Delft] & queens-ware to be divided equally between my son Isaac Crafford's four children viz Elijah Crafford, Isaac Crafford, Robert Crafford and July Ann Crafford
2 CONT I give and bequeath to my two daughters Rebecca Thompson and Ann Boyles my bed and bedding my wearing apparel including all my bed clothes Table linen towels & to be divided between them share and share alike.
2 CONT I give and bequeath to my grand-daughter Ruth Crafford my looking glass.
2 CONT Lastly I direct all my property not heretofore disposed of to be sold at the discretion of my executor and after the payment of my funeral expenses I direct the remainder to be equally divided between my two daughters Rebecca Thom
2 CONC pson and Ann Boyles.
2 CONT I hereby appoint my son Isaac Crafford executor of this my last will and testament. In testimony whereof I have hereunto set my hand and seal April 8, 1836.
2 CONT In presence of Ja. McFarren John Horner
2 CONT Elisabeth (herXmark) Crafford
2 CONT
2 CONT Washington County SS.
2 CONT Be it remembered on this 11th day of January A.D. 1837 before me Sam'l Cunningham Register for the Probate of Wills and greeting letters of Administration in and for said County cause James McFarren Esq and John Horner the subscri
2 CONC bing witnesses to the within Last Will and Testament Of Elisabeth Crafford dec'd who being duly sworn as the law directs doth depose and say that they were personally present and did see the Testatrix herein named make her mark to
2 CONC  the within will and did hear her publish and pronounce and declare the same as and for her last will and Testament & that at the time she did so she was of sound and disposing mind memory and understanding to the best of their Kn
2 CONC owledge observation and belief
2 CONT Jas McFarren
2 CONT John Horner
2 CONT And sworn to and subscribed before me
2 CONT Sam'l Cunningham Register
2 CONT
2 CONT January 11 - 1837 Letter Testemantary with copy of the will and probate entered issued to Isaac Crafford within named who on same day was duly sworn
2 CONT Sam'l Cunningham Register
