0 @I5415693973130117104@ INDI
1 NAME Margaret /Hanna/
2 GIVN Margaret
2 SURN Hanna
2 _MARNM Stout
2 NICK Margaret (Hanna) Stout
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 PLAC Whitehouse Cemetery, Arnett, Washington County, Arkansas, USA
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 21 NOV 1810
2 PLAC Kentucky, USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 23 AUG 1899
2 PLAC Arnett, Washington County, Arkansas, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Margaret Hanna was probably born in Floyd County, Kentucky, where her parents were enumerated in the 1810 and 1820 census, and where she married Jonathan Stout in 1825. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Along with many other Floyd County families, the couple soon found themselves in Vermilion County, Illinois, circa 1828. Their daughters Elizabeth, Cynthia, and Celia all were born in Illinois.
2 CONT
2 CONT The couple seems to have come to Washington County, Arkansas, circa 1833 with - again - many other Floyd County families. However, Margaret's daughter Elizabeth mentioned in her pension application that the family was in Tennessee
2 CONC  for 1837. Whatever the reason for this, the Margaret and her brood were back in Washington County by 1840 and for every census year after that.
2 CONT
2 CONT Interestingly, Margaret and Jonathan had five daughters in a row followed by six sons. The rest of the couple's children (born in Arkansas) were Julian A. (a daughter), Keziah Jane, Samuel J., David S., John A., William, Jeremiah 
2 CONC H, and James M.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to "The Stout-Hanna-Whyte Families" by Dan E. Westphal, Margaret was "big, heavy-set woman of Irish descent."
2 CONT
2 CONT A photo of Margaret and husband Jonathan can be easily found on popular genealogy sites.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/14710431/margaret-stout Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18
2 CONC 783 SmartCopy]: ''Nov 29 2022, 20:45:58 UTC''
1 FAMS @F5415693973220117105@
1 RFN geni:5415693973130117104
1 SUBM @S5211346194020031861@
1 OBJE
