1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *  Elizabeth “Betsy” Bland Burch
2 CONT * BIRTH May 1843 Greene County, Indiana, 
2 CONT * DEATH 12 Jan 1930 Greene County, Indiana, 
2 CONT * BURIAL  Bays-Burch Cemetery  Solsberry, Greene County, Indiana
2 CONT * Children 
2 CONT * * James Burch 1860–1933 
2 CONT * * Andrew Jackson Burch 1865–1947 
2 CONT * * Cleola Alice Burch Groome 1873–1963 
2 CONT * * Wiley Franklin Burch 1875–1943 
2 CONT * * Clara Estella Burch 1877–1879 
2 CONT * * Augdeon Burch 1878–1963 
2 CONT * * Ollie Etta Burch Hamlin 1880–1926 
2 CONT * * Dalton Burch 1883–1912 
2 CONT * * General Marion Burch 1885–1960 
2 CONT * * Francis Burch 1888–1967
2 CONT
2 CONT History of Greene County Indiana 188-1989 (1990, Taylor 
2 CONT        Publishing, Dallas, Tx.) pg. 182-3 Andrew Jackson Burch, 
2 CONT
2 CONT 	     Elizabeth died in 1861, Greene County, Indiana. Andrew 
2 CONT        Jackson had entered government land in Indiana in 1853. He 
2 CONT        served in the Civil War. He then married in 1861 to 
2 CONT        Elizabeth Bland, born  in 1843, the daughter of Hiram and 
2 CONT        Rachel Bays Bland. Their children: James, 1863-1932; Jack 
2 CONT        1865-1947; John, 1867-1919; Mattison, 1871-1953; Cleola, 
2 CONT        1874-1963; Wiley, 1875-1943; Augden, 1878-1963; Ollie, 
2 CONT        1880-1923; Dalton, 1882-1912; General, 1885-1960; Francis, 
2 CONT        1888-1967.
2 CONT
2 CONT             Andrew Jackson Burch, 1816-1904, and second wife 
2 CONT        Elizabeth, 1843-1919, are both buried in Jack Burch 
2 CONT        Cemetery on State Road 54, east of  Ridgeport, Indiana. His 
2 CONT        first wife is also buried there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=16642351 Hiram] and Rachel S. (Bays) Bland (poss. buried [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid= 13039579 here]). Married Andrew Jackson Burch June
2 CONC  6, 1861 in Greene Co., Indiana.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of:  [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=11554412 James], [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=11553922 Andrew Jackson Jr.], [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=128047
2 CONC 18 John], William Mattison, [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=5757952 Cleola], [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=11554238 Wiley Franklin], Ogdon, [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?
2 CONC page=gr&GRid=16799376 Ollie Etta], [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=11554085 Dalton], [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=18309379 General Marion], [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi
2 CONC ?page=gr&GRid=30789189 Clara], and [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=11555753 Francis].
