1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Note from Curator Pam Wilson (Jan 2020): It appears that the wrong James Glenn has been attached as father of Mourning Glenn Harris, based upon the will of James Glen of St. Martin's Parish, Hanover County, VA writ
2 CONC ten 11 June 1762 who specifically names the children of Mourning Glenn Harris and Robert Harris in his will. For this reason, I am disconnecting her from this father.
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see the will of the other James Glenn (likely his son) at  https://www.jstor.org/stable/4244917 (it is also transcribed in his profile at https://www.geni.com/people/James-Glenn/6000000000048130131
2 CONT
2 CONT =------------------------------=
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=kbkeeley&id=I2308
2 CONT
2 CONT James and John GLENN are not proven to be brothers (the link is tentative). John GLENN settled in New Kent Co., VA and was the father of Mourning GLENN (b. ca. 1660) who married (1) Thomas PETTUS, (2) James BRAY II. James GLENN se
2 CONC ttled in Accomac County.
2 CONT
2 CONT The GLENN family probably had some relationship to the TYREE family, since the name Tyree Glenn was prominently passed down in the Glenn family. see http://users.aol.com/ATTText1/a/EarliestTyrees.html for details about the early T
2 CONC yrees in Virginia and many possible connections to the GLENN (Glann, Glen, etc.) family.
2 CONT
2 CONT The GLENN family of Scotland belonged to the MacIntosh clan.
2 CONT
2 CONT James GLENN was born 1636, St. Ninians, Stirlingshire, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Purchased land Dec 1691 in Accomack co., VA from Woodmen Stokeley
2 CONT     (Accomack co. Deeds, Wills and Orders, 1682-1697).
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. In 1695 he gave 217 acres of land in Accomack co., VA to his son, Lazarus Glenn (Accomack co., Deeds, Wills, 1692-1713).
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. The children of James Glenn, Sr., were born to Elizabeth Mitchell.
2 CONT     Catherine Winn was his second wife whom he probably married after settling in Accomack co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Georgia Monroe suggests that Mourning Winn might have been either a sister or a daughter of Catherine Winn.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Wills and Administration of Accomack County, 1663-1800 by Stratton Nottingham: "Orders 1690-1697. Glenn, James - Adm. his est to Catherine Glenn, wid of sd. James - Henry Toles & John Morris security, 15 Sep 1696."
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. The parish records of St. Ninian's list the christening of Alexander as a son of James and Elizabeth Glenn.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES INCLUDE: 
2 CONT * Correspondence with Georgia Munro, 350 Orchard Avenue, Grand Junction, CO 81501. (She had obtained information from Gretta Marshall of 7507 Cliffbrook Dr., Dallas, TX and from parish records (births of St. Ninians, Sterlingshire
2 CONC , Scotland: LDS Reel 79, p. 199; Reel 4, p. 223-224; Reel 5, p. 79-80)).
2 CONT * Correspondence (1996) from Tim M. Thompson, 113 Normandy Dr., Belleville, IL 62223.
2 CONT * Odom, Fred. Note posted 17 Mar 2000 on the Glenn Family Genealogy Forum (GenForum) (Re: who are the parents of James Glenn Jr.?)
2 CONT * Note posted 29 Sep 2000 on the Glenn Family Genealogy Furum (GenForum) (Re: Glenn, Mourning, Albemarle County, VA).
2 CONT * World Family Tree, Vol. 6, Pedigree #1124. (submitted by Audrey L. Parker, 6212 Baker N.E., Alburquerque, NM 87109-2742).
2 CONT * WFT 7:4242, 17:927.
2 CONT * GenServ: od007aa (Odom, Fredwin, M., 6139 Saufley Pines, Pensicola, FL 32526-3721 [fredodom@ix.netcom.com].
2 CONT * Genserv: fora6db (Forinash, Rena V., 26611 Balerna Dr., Saugus, CA 91350 [forinash@scvnet.com].
2 CONT
