2 CONT In the name of God, amen, the eleventh day of June 1762, I , James Glen of St. Martin's Parish, in the County of Hanover, Being praised be to God, of a sound mind and memory, do make this my Last Will and Testament, in manner and 
2 CONC form following, that is to say first and principally I commend my soul to God, who gave it and my body to be buried at the discretion of my executors-hereafter named, and as touching such worldly estate as it hath
2 CONT pleased God to bestow on me, my desire is that the same be divided as is hereafter directed.
2 CONT Item, I give to my son Gideon Glen all that part of my estate, as is present in his possession to him and his heirs forever,
2 CONT Item: I give to my son Nehemiah Glen 300 acres of land on the upper side of Great Guinea Creek, including the plantation whereon he now lives and bounded as by a plan drawn by Robert Harris together with one half of the hogs and c
2 CONC attle the said Nathan Glen received on the plantation, and three-fourth of the increase of the said hogs and cattle, and all the rest of my estate that is in his possession except a negro man named Pompey and a negro girl named Na
2 CONC n, to him and his heirs forever.
2 CONT Item: I give to my son James Glen Three Hundred Fifty acres of land in Cumberland County on the upper side of Great Guinea Creek, bounded as by a plan drawn up by Robert Harris, and the sum of thirty five pounds current money and 
2 CONC that part of my stock of hogs and cattle that is in the hands of my son Nathan Glenn, to him and his heirs forever.
2 CONT Item, I give to my daughter, Jemima Symes all that part of my estate as is in her possession to her and her heirs forever.
2 CONT Item: I give to my grand daughter Frances Harris one negro boy named Daniel when she shall arrive at the age of eighteen years or marrys to her and her heirs forever.
2 CONT Item, I give to my granddaughter Jude Harris one negro boy named Charles when she shall arrive at the age of eighteen years or marrys to her and her heirs forever. Item: I give to my granddaughter Anna Glen Harris one negro girl n
2 CONC amed Nan, when she shall arrive at the age of eighteen or marrys to her and her heirs forever.
2 CONT Item, I give to my granddaughter Molley Glen Harris one negro boy named Dick when she shall arrive at the age of eighteen or marrys to her and her heirs forever.
2 CONT Item: I give to my grandson, Peter Harris one negro girl named Jenny to him and his heirs forever.
2 CONT Item: I give to my grandson Tyre Harris one negro boy named Harry to him and his heirs forever.
2 CONT Item: my will and desire is that if either of my grandchildren, that is to say Frances Harris, Jude Harris, Anna Glen Harris, Molley Glen Harris, Peter Harris, and Tyre Harris should before they arrive at to lawful age or Marrys h
2 CONC ave the misfortune to lose their negro given as before, the Loss to be made up out of the increase of Befs, if any the mother of said negroes but if there should be no loss then the said negro woman Befs and her future increase sh
2 CONC ould be sold, and the money arising by such a sale to be equally divided between my six grandchildren that is to say Frances Harris, Judy Harris Anna Glen Harris Molley Glen Harris, Peter Harris and Tyre Harris or their heirs fore
2 CONC ver.
2 CONT Item I give to my daughter Mary Hopkins, all that part of my fore estate she has allready received to her and her heirs forevere.
2 CONT Item, I give to my daughter Elizabeth Byars forty pounds current money to her and her heirs forever.
2 CONT Item I give to my daughter Anna Glen my best feather bed and furniture one good cow, and calf, and one pound ten shillings current money to her and her heirs forever.
2 CONT Item, I lend to my loving wife Hannah Glen after the payment of my jsut debts and the Legacies in this will
2 CONT given, the plantation whereon I now live and four negroes, named Pompey, John, Nan, and Sarah and all my personal estate not before given during her natural life and after her decease my will is that my daughter Anna Glen should h
2 CONC ave one negro woman named Sarah to her and her heirs forever, then the rest of my estate to gether with the land and plantation whereon I now live to the same of what kind whatsoever to descent to my son Thompson Glenn and the hei
2 CONC rs of his Body lawfully begotten forever.
2 CONT Item my will and desire is that if my son Thompson Glenn whould die without lawful issue that then the estate
2 CONT lent to my loving wife andand given to him both real and personal shall be sold by my executors and the money arising from such sale to be equally divided between all my children except my daughters Keziah harris and Sarah Dabney,
2 CONC  who have already had their part of my estate.
2 CONT Lastly I nominate constitute and appoint my sons Gideon Glen, Nehemiah Glen and Nathan Glen to be the
2 CONT Executors of this my Last Will and Testament hereby making void all other wills by me heretofore made. In witness whereof I have hereunto set my hand and seal the day and year before written.
