1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ancetry.com contains multiple trees connecting children to this man and his wives. However, due to the fact that the dates of marriage to the wives (and therefore the '''*sequence*''' of the wives' marriage) is unc
2 CONC ertain, the ancestry.com attribution of motherhood of some children is inconsistent. In some ancestry.com trees, maternity for one child is attributed to Mary Roe, while in others it is attributed to the other wife, Sarah Garland.
2 CONC  There are as yet insufficient other clues to allow deduction of maternity attribution (for instance, if a child was born after one spouses' death, this would assure attribution to the other wife, etc.).
2 CONT
2 CONT For sake of simplicity, all children (with the exception indicated in the next paragraph) are being attached to Sarah Garland. However, the researcher should be made aware of the fact the trees do exist which attribute some childr
2 CONC en to Mary Roe. When marriage dates can be pinned down, the children can be moved to Mary Row with certainty.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son, William Bird Glenn, which ancestry.com trees substantially indicate was born (1759) after the death of Sarah Garland, and whose mother is also attributed to Mary Roe, is being moved to Mary Roe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Example:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/29508623/person/330099255291/facts
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
