1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Name                  	Col William Claiborne Harris
2 CONT Gender                  	Male
2 CONT Birth Date          	1669
2 CONT Birth Place       	New Kent County, Virginia, United States of America
2 CONT Death Date        	8 Mar 1730
2 CONT Death Place         	Hanover County, Virginia, United States of America
2 CONT Cemetery         	Cedar Hill Cemetery
2 CONT Burial or Cremation Place	Hanover County, Virginia, United States of America
2 CONT Has Bio?	Y
2 CONT Father	Robert Harris
2 CONT Spouse	Mary ''Claiborne'' Rice
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/93941470/william_claiborne-harris
2 CONT
2 CONT Col. William Claiborne Harris was the son of Maj. Robert Harris, born 1630 in Glamorgan, Wales, who died 1730 in Hanover Co., VA. William's mother, Mary (Claiborne) Rice, was born 1630 in King William Co., VA and died 9 Feb 1710 a
2 CONC t Doswell, Hanover Co., VA. Mary Claiborne was the daughter of Col. William Claiborne, the first Secretary of the Virginia Colony.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1695, Col. William Claiborne Harris married Temperance Overton, daughter of William Overton, the immigrant, and his wife, Mary Waters. This William Overton was the son of Colonel Overton, Governor of Hull, England, under Oliver
2 CONC  Cromwell and later commanded a brigade at Dunbar and Inver Keithing.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT === William Harris  
2 CONT *Born	1669 / Abt 1672	Forks, Hanover County, Virginia 
2 CONT *Gender	Male 
2 CONT *Died	before October 21, 1726  / 8 Mar 1730 	Cedar Hill, Hanover County, Virginia 
2 CONT * Son of Major Robert Harris of "The Forks" and Mary ‘Elizabeth’ 
2 CONT *Husband of Temperance Overton (BIRTH 2 MAR 1679 • Forks, New Kent (now Hanover), Virginia DEATH 19 FEB 1716, married 1695
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I114938&tree=tree1 cites 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Virginia Genealogist Volume 22, 1978, 3. 
2 CONT
2 CONT No family Bible record is known to exist and the will of Capt. William Harris was lost in the fire which destroyed the Hanover County records. The following list of children of Capt. William Harris has been derived from both court
2 CONC  and family records:
2 CONT * (1) Major Robert Harris of Albemarle County
2 CONT * (2) Benjamin Harris of Hanover County
2 CONT * (3) William Harris, Junior, of St. Paul's Parish
2 CONT * (4) John Harris of Hanover County
2 CONT * (5) James Harris of Hanover County
2 CONT * (6) Jemima Harris who married her cousin William Overton.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Col. William Claiborne Harris was the son of Maj. Robert Harris, born 1630 in Glamorgan, Wales, who died 1730 in Hanover Co., VA. William's mother, Mary (Claiborne) Rice, was born 1630 in King William Co., VA and died 9 Feb 1710 a
2 CONC t Doswell, Hanover Co., VA. Mary Claiborne was [NOT] the daughter of Col. William Claiborne, the first Secretary of the Virginia Colony.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1695, Col. William Claiborne Harris married Temperance Overton, daughter of William Overton, the immigrant, and his wife, Mary Waters. This William Overton was the son of Colonel Overton, Governor of Hull, England, under Oliver
2 CONC  Cromwell and later commanded a brigade at Dunbar and Inver Keithing
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT William Cross of Botetourt Co., Va., and his descendants, 1733-1932; also a record of the related families of McCown, Gentry-Blythe, Cain-Robertson, Harris-Martin, and Conner, of Virginia, Kentucky, Illinois and Missouri / by John
2 CONC  Newton Cross and Mary Cross Cole. by Cross, John Newton, 1850- Publication date 1932. Page 157.[https://archive.org/details/williamcrossofbo00cros/page/156/mode/2up Archive.Org] - many more children are listed.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ???
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Robert Harris and Mary are:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 46 i. Mary8 Harris.
2 CONT * 47 ii. John Harris, born 1662.
2 CONT * 48 iii. Thomas Harris, born 1667.
2 CONT * 49 iv. Claiborne "Ned" Harris, born Abt. 1668.
2 CONT * + 50 v. William Capt. Harris, born 1669 in Broomfield, Essex, England; died 08 Mar 1705/06 in Cedar Hill, Hanover Co., Virginia.
2 CONT * 51 vi. Robert Jr. Harris, born Abt. 1675 in Hanover, Co., Virginia.
2 CONT * 52 vii. Benjamin Harris, born 1677.
2 CONT * 53 viii. Judith Harris, born 1681.
2 CONT * 54 ix. Edward Harris, born 17 Apr 1690. ----
2 CONT
