1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Dabney was born to John and Anna (Harris) Dabney October 2, 1740, in Hanover County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Thomas Carr Waller ca 1759/60. He was born July 29, 1732 to John and Agnes (Carr) Waller of Topping Castle, Spotsylvania County, Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had ten children: 
2 CONT #Mary, born February 26, 1761, married Joseph Woolfolk IV of Hanover County 1778, died January 10, 1822; 
2 CONT #Anna, born November 11, 1762, died August 5, 1834, married Joel Harris; 
2 CONT #Agnes, born November 17, 1764, died November 7, 1817; 
2 CONT #Sarah, born January 24, 1767, died March 22, 1829, married Joseph Spicer; 
2 CONT #Carr, born March 12, 1769, died May 7, 1843, married first to Elizabeth Martin, second to Susannah Edwards, moved to Henry County;
2 CONT # Dabney, born February 20, 1772, died June 6, 1849, married Elizabeth Minor; 
2 CONT #Pomfrett Jr., born May 8, 1774, died April 29,1814, married Sarah Minor Woolfolk; 
2 CONT #Dorothy, born March 31,1777, died December 2, 1838, married Rev. E. T. Rowzie; 
2 CONT #John, born February 10, 1780, died September 10, 1824; 
2 CONT #Elizabeth, born March 2, 1783, died June 7, 1872, probably unmarried
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT * [https://books.google.com/books?id=xxVhymOH3usC&lpg=PA482&ots=qyUD-O16Gk&dq=cedar%20point%20farm%20spotsylvania&pg=PA482#v=onepage&q=cedar%20point%20farm%20spotsylvania&f=true link] to “A History of Caroline County, Virginia: Fr
2 CONC om Its Formation in 1727 to 1924” By Marshall Wingfield
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Links
2 CONT * http://www.alleylaw.net/royfwaller.html Thomas Waller 1732 - 1787 ....................... +Sarah Dabney 1740 - 1822
2 CONT * https://www.dabney-early-virginia.info/getperson.php?personID=I678&tree=Dabney
