2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT The National Society of the Daughters of the American Revolution Volume 66
2 CONT page 50
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Ann Alice Fudge Jackson.
2 CONT DAR ID Number: 65142
2 CONT Born in Chicago, Ill.
2 CONT Wife of William Chester Jackson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendant of Rev. Matthew Woodson, Major Josiah Woodson, John Woodson, Sergt. Josiah Stone, Lieut. Nathaniel Wilson, Jacob Persinger, Peter Hansborough, Christopher Harris, and Robert Harris.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Enoch Hansborough Fudge (b. 1850) and Kate Stone (b. 1853), his wife, m. 1880.
2 CONT
2 CONT Granddaughter of Jacob Fudge (1800-74) and Elsie King Hansborough (1810-52), his wife, m. 1837; Caleb Smith Stone (1810-72) and Ann Warfield Wilson (1816-83), his wife, m. 1832.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gr-granddaughter of Conrad Fudge and Elizabeth Persinger, his wife, m. 1798; James Stone (b. 1787) and Catherine (Katy) Harris, his wife;  Dr. Nathaniel Augustus Wilson (b. 1822) and Caroline Randolph Woodson (1792-1879), his wife
2 CONC , m. 1809; Joseph Hansborough  (1783-1853) and Sallie Smith (b. 1858), his wife, m. 1806.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gr-gr-granddaughter of Josiah Stone and Mary Washington Donaldson, his wife, m. 1777; Josiah Woodson and Elizabeth (Woodson) (b. 1759), his wife, m. 1778; Jacob Persinger and Mary Kimberlin, his wife; Nathaniel Wilson and Mary Bro
2 CONC ome (1727-1809), his wife, m. 1752;  Peter Hansborough [p.50] and Elizabeth Brown, his wife, m. 1781; Robert Harris and Nancy Grubbs (1740-1835), his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gr-gr-gr-granddaughter of Matthew Woodson and Elizabeth Levillian (1737-1803), his wife, m. 1758 (parents of Elizabeth); John Woodson and Dorothy Randolph (1794-1851), his wife (parents of Josiah); Christopher Harris and Mary Dabn
2 CONC ey, his 1st wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Matthew Woodson (1731-1800) served as chaplain in the 1st Virginia regiment. He was born in Virginia; died in Goochland County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah Woodson (1758-1817) served as major in the Virginia troops. He was born in Virginia; died in Mason County, Ky.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Woodson was a member of the Virginia Convention, 1774-76. He was born in Virginia, and in 1789 died in Goochland County.
2 CONT Also No. 15768.
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah Stone (1759-1804) served as corporal and sergeant in Capt. Heaberd Smallwood's company, Col. William Grayson's regiment,  Continental troops. He was born in Maryland; died in Kentucky.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel Wilson (1754-96) was lieutenant of the Flying Camp of Maryland, where he was born; died in Kentucky.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Persinger (1749-1835) served as scout and guide, for which he was especially fitted by his knowledge of Indian character and of the  country in which the fighting was done. He was born in Pennsylvania; died in Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Hansborough enlisted, 1778, in Capt. Robert Powell's company, 3rd Virginia regiment. He was born, 1758, in Culpeper County, Va.,  where he died.
2 CONT
2 CONT Christopher Harris (1725-94), Robert Harris (1749-1833) both served in the Kentucky militia, 1780, at Fort Boonesboro. They were born in Albemarle County, Va.; died in Madison County, Ky.
2 CONT
2 CONT
