2 CONT According to the 1885 compilation "A History of Kentucky Baptists, Vol I", by J.H. Spencer, 
2 CONT page 365. . .
2 CONT
2 CONT Christopher Harris gathered Viney Fork church, was in its constitution, and served it as pastor about sixteen years. He came from Virginia to Madison county, Kentucky, where he settled, about 1785, where he united with Dreaming Cr
2 CONC eek (afterwards Mount Nebo) church. In May of 1796, he was chosen moderator of Tates Creek Association, and between this time and 1814, filled that position ten years. About 1816, he moved to the Green river country, and united wi
2 CONC th Mount Zion church, in Warren county. The next year, he was chosen moderator of Gasper River Association, and continued to occupy that position, till 1820, when he, with his church, entered into the constitution of Drakes Creek 
2 CONC Association. He was moderator of the latter fraternity five years.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/49398530/christopher_harris Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''
