1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Harris, son of Christopher Harris and Agnes McCord. See Harris Family. John Harris served through the Revolution with the rank of Captain, and soon after the war he emigrated to Kentucky, settling in Madison C
2 CONC ounty where he became a noted citizen. He was judge of the Circuit Court and he also represented the county in the legislature in 1789. In 1809, he made a trip to New Orleans on a flat boat. On the return trip, he died suddenly an
2 CONC d was buried on the banks of the Mississippi by his son, Overton, who accompanied him.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Dabney died and Christopher Harris remarried to Agnes McCord about 1762. They had ten additional children: John, Benjamin, William, Barnabas, James, Samuel, Jane, Margaret, Isabel, and Overton. All of Christopher children exc
2 CONC ept Margaret survived to adulthood, married, and had children.
2 CONT
