2 CONC ecame a noted citizen. He was judge of the Circuit Court and he also represented the county in the legislature in 1789. In 1809, he made a trip to New Orleans on a flat boat. On the return trip, he died suddenly and was buried on 
2 CONC the banks of the Mississippi by his son, Overton, who accompanied him.
