1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mourning Harris Shelton married Archibald Woods on 5 August 1773, in Virginia. They moved to Estill Station, Madison County, Kentucky, about 1782, and from there to Franklin County, Tennessee, about 1809. Mourning 
2 CONC and Archibald had 10 known children: Lucy, b. 1774, m. William Caperton; William, b. 1776, m. Mary Harris;  Susannah, b. 1778, m. William Goodloe; Mary, b. 1780, m. Col. Barbee Collins; Sarah, b. 1783, d. 1785;  Archibald, b. 1785
2 CONC , m. Elizabeth C. Shackelford; Anna, b. 1787, m. Thomas Miller; Thomas, b. 1789, d. 1806; Ann, b.&d. 1791; Mourning, b. 1792, m. Garland Burleigh Miller. Inscription: Sacred  to the memory of  MOURNING WOODS  consort of  Archibala
2 CONC  Woods  daughter of  William & Lucy Shelton  Died Sept 7th 1817  Age 61 years  & 8 months
