2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Mourning was born in 1756. She was the daughter of William Shelton and Lucy Harris. She passed away in 1817. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Archibald and Mourning (Shelton) Woods" emigrated from Albemarle Co. to Madison Co., Kentucky.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT "The remains of himself [Archibald Woods] and his first wife. Mourning Shelton, were interred in the family burying ground about two miles northeast of Richmond, not far from the residence on Otter Creek, now owned and occupied by
2 CONC  Jeptha Chenault, but were subsequently many years ago removed and re-interred in the Richmond Cemetery, where they now rest."[3]
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Entered by Richard Ragland, Sunday, September 8, 2013.
2 CONT ↑ Edgar Woods. Albemarle County in Virginia: Giving Some Account of what it was by Nature, of what it was Made by Man, and of Some of the Men who Made it. Michie Company, printers; 1901. p. 387-.
2 CONT ↑ Miller, W. H. 1907. History and genealogies of the families of Miller, Woods, Harris, Wallace, Maupin, Oldham, Kavanaugh and (illustrated), with interspersions of notes of the families Dabney, Reid, Martin, Broadus, Gentry, Jarm
2 CONC an, Jameson, Ballard, Mullins, Michie, Moberley, Covington, Growning, Duncan, Yancey and others. p. 200 (https://archive.org/details/historygenealogie00mill)
2 CONT
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT
