1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT THOMAS SHELTON was an early emigrant from Virginia to Madison county,
2 CONT Ky.  Here he became a member of Tates Creek church of Separate Baptists,
2 CONT which was gathered by Andrew Tribble, in 1786.  Mr. Shelton was a
2 CONT licensed preacher, in his church, as early as 1790.  He was a minister
2 CONT in South Kentucky Association, till 1793, when he, with others, seceded
2 CONT from that fraternity, and went into the constitution of Tates Creek
2 CONT Association.  The same year, he was appointed by the latter fraternity,
2 CONT to bear a letter of correspondence to the General Committee of Virginia
2 CONT Baptists, which met that year, at Muddy Creek meeting-house, in Powhatan
2 CONT county, VA.  He started on his journey, to perform his duty, but did not
2 CONT reach his proposed destination.  As he was traveling on horseback,
2 CONT through the mountains, he was attacked by Indians, and massacred.  He
2 CONT left a family, from whom have sprung a numerous posterity.  Among the
2 CONT latter, are the venerable Dr. Thomas Shelton Moberly, of Richmond, KY.,
2 CONT a grandson, and Rev. R. M. Dudley, D. D., Editor of the Western
2 CONT Recorder, great grandsons.
