1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''"The Paul Revere of the South"'''
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1781, the British, led by the ruthless [http://www.geni.com/people/General-Sir-Banastre-Tarleton-1st-Baronet-GCB/6000000010985123336 Colonel Banastre Tarleton], planned to attack [http://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Jefferson-3rd
2 CONC -President-of-the-United-States-of-America/6000000003849466047 Thomas Jefferson] and other revolutionaries at Monticello. Fortunately for the budding Republic, Captain Jack Jouett overheard the plans and valiantly rode his horse t
2 CONC hrough the night to warn Jefferson and the others. His heroism may not have just saved the lives of several important leaders, it may have saved the Revolution itself.
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.monticello.org/site/research-and-collections/jack-jouett... 
2 CONT * http://www.jouetthouse.org/ 
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jack_Jouett 
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/101087831/jack-jouett
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nwbKK7FQM0o "THE PAUL REVERE OF THE SOUTH"! JACK JOUETT HISTORY!
