1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert married Elizabeth Maxwell on December 26, 1786 at Richmond County, Georgia. His parents were Joel Crawford and Elizabeth Frances "Fanny" Harris.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # Frances Crawford........... B. 4/18/1788
2 CONT # David Maxwell Crawford...B. 2/6/1790
2 CONT # Elizabeth Crawford..........B. 3/25/1792
2 CONT # Joel Crawford................ B. 4/9/1794
2 CONT # Mary Crawford.............. B. 3/11/1796
2 CONT # Nathaniel Crawford.........B.5/20/1798
2 CONT # Edward Maxwell Crawford..B.2/11/1800
2 CONT # William Crawford............B. 3/7/1803
2 CONT # Charles A. Crawford........B. 9/6/1806
2 CONT # Anna Crawford...............B. 3/4/1809
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Names and birthdates of children from Bible records of Crawford-Walker Bible in Book: Historical Collections of the Georgia Chapters of Daughters of the American Revolution, online at ancestry.com.
2 CONT ****************** Abstract of Robert Crawford's Will, Columbia County, GA, written and signed by him on September 30, 1820. Probated: February 18, 1823. Sons, Nathan and Edward swore in open court on December 18, 1822: "this writ
2 CONC ing contains the true last Will of the within named Robert Crawford, deceased"
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife, Elizabeth was given any furniture she wanted, horses, hogs, cows and calves she wanted.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eight children were given each 1/8 of the property that had not been claimed by wife, plus some money in different amounts. Children named were: David M., Joel, Nathan Wm. H., Charles A., Edward M., Polly (Mary) Walker and Anne. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He wanted all property sold after the death of wife and divided into 9 parts with children, Anne and Charles getting 3 of the 9 parts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert named three of his sons as his Executors: David M. Crawford, Nathan Crawford and Edward M. Crawford.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Since daughters, Frances and Elizabeth were not named in the Will, it is assumed they had already died.
2 CONT
2 CONT To see Robert's Will: go to familysearch.org., click on search and scroll to bottom of page and click on United States, then in column to left, click on Georgia. Then go to Georgia Probate 1743-1975 and then click on Columbia Coun
2 CONC ty. Then click on Wills, 1789-1939, Crawford, C.-Hunt, M. It begins at image 16 of 661.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/112105453/robert-crawford Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/1
