1 NAME Jane /Hescott/
2 GIVN Jane
2 SURN Hescott
2 _MARNM Thompson
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE BET 1691 AND 1693
2 PLAC St. Peter’s Parish
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF OCT 1734
2 ADDR
3 CITY Greenwood
3 STAE Virginia
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jane Hescott''' (c. 1691 – bef. 1734) was a colonial resident of Virginia. She is a key figure in the maternal history of the Brown family of Albemarle County as the mother of Sarah Thompson, the second wife of Benjamin Brown, 
2 CONC Sr.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Parentage ===
2 CONT Jane was (likely) the daughter of '''Robert Hescott''' and '''Elizabeth Spencer'''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT While some genealogical databases list her parents as unknown due to the widespread destruction of early colonial records in New Kent County (often referred to as "burnt counties"), she is traditionally identified within the Hesco
2 CONC tt-Thompson-Brown lineage as the daughter of this couple. Her family was established in the Virginia Tidewater region, primarily in the area that became New Kent and later Hanover County.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Marriage and Family ===
2 CONT Jane married '''Robert Thompson, Jr.''' in 1712 in New Kent County, Virginia. As the Thompson family moved westward toward the Piedmont region, their children’s births were recorded across the shifting boundaries of New Kent and L
2 CONC ouisa Counties.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to parish registers and family reconstructions, their children included:
2 CONT # '''Robert Thompson''' (b. 1713, New Kent County)
2 CONT # '''David Thompson''' (b. 1715, New Kent County)
2 CONT # '''Jean Thompson''' (b. 1717, New Kent County)
2 CONT # '''Mary Thompson''' (b. 1719, New Kent County)
2 CONT # '''Judith Thompson''' (b. 1721, Louisa County)
2 CONT # '''Elizabeth Thompson''' (b. c. 1723; likely died young)
2 CONT # '''Sarah Thompson''' (b. 17 Jan 1724, Louisa County) – Second wife of Benjamin Brown, Sr.
2 CONT # '''Suzanna Thompson''' (b. 1729, Louisa County)
2 CONT
2 CONT === Death and Identity Clarifications ===
2 CONT Jane Thompson died before October 1734. This is confirmed by the fact that her husband, Robert Thompson, Jr., remarried at that time to a woman of French Huguenot descent.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are several common points of confusion regarding her identity in digital records:
2 CONT * '''The "Via" and "Baker" Names:''' The surnames "Via" or "Baker" are sometimes attached to her. There is no primary evidence in the St. Peter's Parish registers to support these as maiden names or prior marriages; they likely re
2 CONC present errors introduced by later researchers mixing different family lines.
2 CONT * '''Not Elizabeth Anne:''' Jane Hescott is frequently confused with a fictional "Elizabeth Anne Hescott" who is often incorrectly listed as the first wife of Benjamin Brown, Sr. Primary records (such as the Reuben Dabney Brown re
2 CONC cords) confirm the first Mrs. Brown was a '''Wilson'''. Jane was actually the mother of the *second* wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT === Sources ===
2 CONT * '''St. Peter's Parish Register:''' New Kent County, Virginia.
2 CONT * '''Chamberlayne, C.G.:''' ''The Vestry Book and Register of St. Peter's Parish, New Kent and James City Counties, Virginia, 1684-1786.''
2 CONT * '''FamilySearch Genealogy:''' [[https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/2:2:3NM1-5NN](https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/2:2:3NM1-5NN) Record for Jane Hescott].
2 CONT * '''WikiTree:''' [[https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Hescott-3](https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Hescott-3) Profile for Jane Hescott (Hescott-3)].
2 CONT * '''Brown Family Bible:''' Records of the descendants of Sarah Thompson Brown.
2 CONT * Ancestry [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/2:2:3NM1-5NN]
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Hescott-3
