1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Thompson, Jr., was a son of Major Robert Thompson, Sr., and his wife Judith (Key) Thompson. Robert was christened on April 24, 1687, at St. Peter's Parish, New Kent County, Virginia. He married Jane Hescott, b. ca. 1690, Ne
2 CONC w Kent County VA, in 1712 at St. Peter's Parish, New Kent Co. VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had these eight children together:   
2 CONT # Robert Thompson b: 1713 in New Kent, New Kent, Virginia      
2 CONT # David Thompson b: 1715 in New Kent, New Kent, Virginia      
2 CONT # Jean Thompson, b. 1717 in New Kent Co., Virginia      
2 CONT # Mary Thompson, b. 1719 in New Kent Co., Virginia     
2 CONT # Judith Thompson b: 1721 in Louisa Co., Virginia      
2 CONT # Elizabeth Thompson b: ca. 1723 [?? - may have died young]      
2 CONT # Sarah Thompson b: 17 JAN 1724 in Louisa, Virginia      
2 CONT # Suzanna Thompson b: 1729 in Louisa, Virginia 
2 CONT
2 CONT We do not know Jane Hescott's death date but several family genealogies state that Robert Thompson married in 1734, presumably to a 2nd wife. She may have been named Mary Viau or Jane Via and of French Huguenot origins. Many genea
2 CONC logies confuse her with Jane Hescott. These are the children credited to him after 1734:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Hannah Thompson b: 1735 in Louisa, Virginia (m. David Epperson)     
2 CONT # Elizabeth Thompson b: 1741in Virginia (m. Thomas Langford III) 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Thompson, Jr., lived until June 1778 when he died in Fredricksville Parish, Albemarle County, Virginia.  
2 CONT
