1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Unknown (Wilson) Brown''' (c. 1700 – c. 1742) was the first wife of Benjamin Brown, Sr., a prominent landowner in Hanover and Albemarle Counties, Virginia. While her given name is not preserved in the surviving public records o
2 CONC f the period, her surname is documented in the genealogical records maintained by her grandson, Reuben Dabney Brown, as recorded in the family Bible.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Marriage and Family ===
2 CONT She married Benjamin Brown, Sr. around 1720–1730 in the Virginia colony, likely in New Kent or Hanover County. During their marriage, the family established significant landholdings in Hanover County, totaling over 4,000 acres.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the family Bible, she was the mother of five children (though some records suggest a sixth):
2 CONT # '''Benjamin Brown, Jr.''' (c. 1737 – bef. 1781) – Executor of his father's estate.
2 CONT # '''William "Billy" Brown''' (1735 – 1780) – Migrated to South Carolina in 1769.
2 CONT # '''Bartlett Brown, Sr.''' – Landowner and progenitor of a branch of the family.
2 CONT # '''Agnes Brown''' – Named as a child of the first marriage in family narratives.
2 CONT # '''Elizabeth Brown''' - died young 
2 CONT # '''Lucinda Brown''' – Mentioned in family records
2 CONT
2 CONT === Death and Legacy ===
2 CONT She died circa 1742 in Hanover County, Virginia. Her death occurred prior to the family’s permanent relocation to the "Walnut Level" estate in Brown's Cove, Albemarle County, which took place around 1747. Following her death, Benj
2 CONC amin Brown, Sr. married Sarah Thompson, who raised the children from the first marriage alongside her own.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Research Notes ===
2 CONT Forensic auditing of the Brown family lineage is required to distinguish this individual from '''Jane Hescott''', who was the mother of Benjamin's second wife. Many digital pedigrees incorrectly assign the Hescott name to this fir
2 CONC st wife; however, primary family documentation explicitly identifies her as a '''Wilson'''. No primary source has yet been recovered to confirm her given name (often speculated as Elizabeth or Anne) or her specific parentage withi
2 CONC n the Wilson families of early Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT === Sources ===
2 CONT * '''Brown Family Bible:''' Hanover and Albemarle Counties, Virginia. Transcribed by Eleanor Williams Bradley, ''Virginia Genealogist'', Vol. 13, 1969.
2 CONT * '''Reuben Dabney Brown Manuscript:''' Records of early settlers, originally compiled by the grandson of Benjamin Brown and Sarah Thompson.
2 CONT * '''Albemarle County Will Book 2, Page 130:''' Will of Benjamin Brown, Sr. (names children from both marriages).
2 CONT * '''RootsWeb Archive:''' "The Brown Family of Brown’s Cove," accessed October 17, 2015.
