1 NAME Bartlett /Brown/
2 GIVN Bartlett
2 SURN Brown
2 _MARNM Brown
2 NICK Not William
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1735
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1784
2 ADDR
3 STAE South Carolina
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bartlett Brown (c. 1732–1786); born in Hanover Co.; m. Katherine Holcombe. He was a son of Benjamin Brown and Miss Wilson.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Bartlett served the greater part of the war with the South Carolina troops and was killed by the Indians at about the same time his brother William was killed.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bartlett Brown''' (c. 1735 – 1784) was an 18th-century planter and pioneer who migrated from the Virginia Piedmont to the South Carolina frontier. Born in Hanover County, Virginia, he was a son of Benjamin Brown, Sr. and his fi
2 CONC rst wife, '''Wilson'''. He was part of the early "B" Brown generation that expanded the family's land interests across the southern colonies.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Early Life and Migration ===
2 CONT Bartlett was raised in Hanover and Albemarle Counties. His father established the family at '''Walnut Level''' in Brown's Cove around 1747. While his younger half-brothers (the children of Sarah Thompson) remained to develop the A
2 CONC lbemarle holdings, Bartlett and his brother '''William "Billy" Brown''' moved south. 
2 CONT
2 CONT By the late 1760s, Bartlett settled in the '''Barnwell District''' (then part of the Orangeburg District) of South Carolina. He established a plantation near Brier's Creek, opposite Burton's Ferry on the Savannah River. This reloc
2 CONC ation was part of a larger migration of Virginia families seeking fresh land for tobacco and livestock in the South Carolina backcountry.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Family and Legacy ===
2 CONT Bartlett Brown married '''Katherine Holcombe'''. Their descendants remained prominent in the Barnwell and Savannah River regions. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His children included:
2 CONT * '''Bartlett Brown, Jr.'''
2 CONT * '''James Brown'''
2 CONT * '''Benjamin Brown'''
2 CONT * '''William Brown'''
2 CONT * '''John Brown'''
2 CONT * '''Mary Brown'''
2 CONT * '''Katherine Brown'''
2 CONT
2 CONT === Research Notes ===
2 CONT Forensic auditing of Bartlett's records is necessary to distinguish him from his brother William. Modern genealogical databases frequently conflate the two into a single "Bartlett William Brown." Primary documents, including their
2 CONC  father's 1762 will and South Carolina land grants, clearly identify them as two distinct individuals. Additionally, digital trees often mistakenly attribute Bartlett’s mother as "Elizabeth Hescott"; however, primary family Bible 
2 CONC records confirm his mother was a '''Wilson''', as the Hescott name did not enter the family until his father's second marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Death ===
2 CONT Bartlett Brown died in 1784 in Barnwell County, South Carolina. His estate was settled in the local courts, providing the framework for identifying this South Carolina branch of the Virginia "B" Browns.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT === Sources ===
2 CONT * '''Albemarle County Will Book 2, Page 130:''' Will of Benjamin Brown, Sr. (1762).
2 CONT * '''Brown Family Bible:''' Transcribed by Eleanor Williams Bradley, ''Virginia Genealogist'', Vol. 13, 1969.
2 CONT * '''Barnwell County Probate Records:''' Estate of Bartlett Brown (1784).
2 CONT * '''Pettibon, Bessie Z.:''' "The William 'Billy' Brown Family of Brown’s Cove, Virginia who settled in South Carolina," USGenWeb Project (2009).
2 CONT *https://www.smokykin.com/tng/getperson.php?personID=I336487&tree=smokykin
