1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bezaleel is said to have a different wife for each of these 2 sources: One source says: "Bezeleel married Elizabeth, daughter of John A. Michie, and his children were Cynthia, the wife of William H. Brown, Frances,
2 CONC  Addison, Williamson, Mary, the wife of George W. Kemper, Martha, the wife of Charles H. Parrott, and John A. M. He was cut off in the prime of his days in 1825."  Since Bezaleel Garland's death apparently is 1825, then perhaps "c
2 CONC ut off" in the above text means death.  Source: https://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/brown/8436/, extraction from: The history of Albemarle County, Virginia, A description of the founding and events of this Virginia cou
2 CONC nty including narritives on its residents families from 1727-1890. Bibliographic Information: Woods, Edgar Rev. History of Albemarle County, Virginia: The Michie Company, Printers, 1901. Another source says his wife is: Wife:	Mary
2 CONC  Brown, 2 (born Thompson) source: MyHeritage.com, Bazuin/Bogard Woodward/Stapleton Web Site. I'm struggling to find any tree in geni.com that would validate the above two claims.
