1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Daughter of William (Hopping Billy) Marion Alexander and Celia Boon Alexander.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nancy was left a widow in 1863 when her husband was killed in battle in Jackson, Missippi.  
2 CONT She had nine very young children at that time
2 CONT # Sarah,  
2 CONT # Nerva,  
2 CONT # Mary A.,  
2 CONT # Louisa,  
2 CONT # Nancy,  
2 CONT # Josie,  
2 CONT # Bill,  
2 CONT # James and  
2 CONT # Jane.  
2 CONT
2 CONT She passed away in 1865 of unknown cause at this time. 
2 CONT Her children were sent to various relatives to live until they could go out on their own.
