2 CONT
2 CONT In the US census, 1810, Scott County, KY there is a William Sublett with one each (males) as follows: one between 16 and 26; one between 26 and 45, and one over 45; only one female between 16 and 26.
2 CONT
2 CONT Here is an 1820 census for a William Sublett for Garrard Co, KY:
2 CONT
2 CONT Wm Sublett United States Census, 1820 Name	Wm Sublett Event Type	Census Event Date	1820 Event Place	Garrard, Garrard, Kentucky, United States Page	92
2 CONT
2 CONT This William Sublett is cited as having in his household in the 1820 Garrard, KY census the following: one male under 10 one male 26-45 one female child under 10, and one female between 26 and 45., 
2 CONT
2 CONT CITING THIS RECORD
2 CONT
2 CONT "United States Census, 1820", database with images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:XHLR-FV3 : accessed 4 April 2016), Wm Sublett, 1820.
2 CONT
2 CONT The following is from: GENERATIONS REMEMBERED: SUBLETTE FAMILY 1700-1850 By: Nancy Louise Sublette, pps 28-29 (Copy in Clayton Library, Houston Public Library system, http://www.houstonlibrary.org):
2 CONT
2 CONT William Sublett (4001) 1760- (no date known) Married: (1) Ruth Ford (2) Mrs. Nancy Harris Born in Albemarle County. On May 13, 1784 was issued a warrant for 14 years service in the Milita. By this date he had settled in Henry Coun
2 CONC ty Virginia. The tract he and James Sublett had acquired jointly in 1793 in Patrick County, Virginia, was disposed by him alone, 60 acres of it on 23 August 1802 to William Gray and 250 acres on Green Creek. Thereupon, he migrated
2 CONC  to Madison and Garrard Counties, Kentucky. The fact he sold these jointly granted lands by himself gives rise to the supposition that the James (4002) to whom they were jointly granted was his father James (3003).  He was married
2 CONC  the first time to Ruth Ford ca.1783 in Buckingham County, Virginia (she was a descendant of another Huguenot family in Manakintown) Following her death, he was married the second time to Mrs. Nancy Harris on 24 April 1806 in Garr
2 CONC ard County, Kentucky. His migration to Kentucky may be placed between December 1804 (land sale in Virginia) and his 1806 marriage. He is said to have resided in Madison County Kentucky near Richmond. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William (4001) and Ruth Ford Sublett had the following children: John Sublett (5001) m. Miss Phoebe James Sublett (5002) m. Sally Ford Anna Sublett (5003) m. Alexander Trimble Judith Sublett (5004) never married William Sublett (5
2 CONC 005) m. Regina Warren Daniel Sublett (5006) m. Julia Oakley Elizabeth Sublett (5007) m. Benjamin F. Chastain Mary (Polly) Sublett (5008) m. Golson Emery Jinsey Sublett (5009) m. John Pruitt Peter Sublett (5010) m. Tallulah Timberl
2 CONC ake
2 CONT
2 CONT William Sublett (4001) had the following children by his second wife, Nancy Harris: David Sublett (5011) m. Mary Ann Marshall Rebecca Sublett (5012) m. William Lewis Pleasant Sublett (5013) m. (1) Patsy Floyd, (2) Susan Sails (cou
2 CONC ld be: Sales) Clara Sublett (5014) m. Mitchell Eagy Patsy Sublett (5015) m. James Warren
2 CONT
2 CONT Citation: 34. Annie Walker Burns, Record of Marriages - Garrard County, Kentucky 1796-1851 typescript 1932
