1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Our earliest record of Pleasant Sublette is a marriage record for Pleasant Sublette, 4 August 1829, Garrard County KY, to Patsy Floyd. It lists John and Mary Floyd as Patsy's parents. It lists a David Sublette as P
2 CONC leasant's bondsman. (Likely that the bondsman was David, Pleasant's older brother.) Garrard County is in the eastern half of Kentucky, about midway between its north and south borders.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1830 Garrard Co KY census, page 221, there are two males between 20 and 30 in a Pleasant Sublet household and one female between the ages of 15 and 20.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some time between 1830 and 1840, Pleasant and his family join the westward movement and travel from Garrard Co. KY to Putnam County, IN, in search of more and better land. It is likely the journey took them through Louisville, whi
2 CONC ch was founded by George Rogers Clark in 1778. Then north they went, probably through Bloomington, Indiana, and settled in Putnam County.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1840 Putnam IN census, there is a Pleasant Sublet with two boys between 5 and 10 years of age (John and William), one male between 30 and 40 years old (Pleasant), and one between 60 and 70 (Pleasant's father-in-law? Uncle? 
2 CONC Pleasant's assumed father, William Sublett, is recorded as having passed 20 years previous). There are two girls under five (Nancy, Rebecca), one between 5 and 10 (Mary), and one adult female between 20 and 30 (we assume Patsy, Pl
2 CONC easant's wife.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT We know that Patsy passes away shortly before 1847, because that is the year that Pleasant marries Sarah Sails, in Putnam Co. IN. They seem to have left almost immediately afterwards, because their first child together, Mariam, is
2 CONC  born in Illinois. By 1850 they are settled in Platte County, Missouri. Their westward trail probably took them through Terre Haute, IN; Effingham, IL; St. Louis, MO; or possibly more north, through Tuscola and Springfield, IL; Ja
2 CONC cksonville and Hannibal; Chillicothe, Cameron, and then finally St. Joseph, MO. (They settle for a while later in Gentry County, MO until they make their final move to western Iowa after the Civil War.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Looking at the ages of the wife and of the children, it is clear from the 1850 MO census that Sarah is his second wife, with John, William Mary, Nancy, Rebecca and David (at least) being children of the first one (Patsy Floyd, fro
2 CONC m the KY marriage record.)
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1850 census they are in Buchanan, Platte County, MO:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1850: ROLE  GENDER  AGE  BIRTHPLACE
2 CONT
2 CONT Pleasant Sublett	M	38	KY Sarah Sublett		F	22	VA John Sublett		M	19	KY William Sublett	M	17	KY (fought in the Civil War) Mary Sublett		F	14	KY (this would be our Mary who marries Anderson Simmons in 1852) Nancy Sublett		F	13	KY Reb
2 CONC ecca Sublett	F	11	KY David Sublett		M	9	IN Julia Sublett		F	7	IN Mariam Sublett	F	2	Illinois  George Sublett	M	0	MO (born June 1850, listed as 5/12s)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1860: Name	 Pleasant Sublett Event Type	 Census Event Date	 1860 Event Place	 Township 62, Gentry, Missouri, United States Gender	 Male Age	 42 (should read: 48) Race	 White Birth Year (Estimated)	 1818 Birthplace	 Kentucky Page	 
2 CONC 55 HOUSEHOLD  ROLE  GENDER  AGE  BIRTHPLACE
2 CONT
2 CONT Pleasant Sublett	M	42	KY Sarah Sublett		F	30	IN (could be TN) Jackson Sublett	M	10	IL George Sublett	M	9	MO Armazinda Sublett	F	8	MO Thomas Sublett	M	6	MO Sarah Sublett		F	4	MO Caroline Sublett	F	3	MO James Sublett		M	0	MO
2 CONT
2 CONT 1870: In the 1870 census their name is spelled Sablet (in the LDS transcription, but it's clearly Sublet in the longhand): They are living in St. John, Harrison Co. IA:	
2 CONT
2 CONT Pleasant Sablet	M	63	KY  (error - should be 58) Sarah Sablet		F	40	IN George Sablet		M	19	MO Thomas Sablet	M	17	MO Sarah Sablet		F	13	MO Caroline Sablet	F	13	MO Olive Sablet		F	11	MO Joseph Sablet		M	9	IA Mary Sablet		F	5	IA Jacks
2 CONC on Sablet	M	27	IL  Mary Sablet		F	16	IA (Jackson's wife)
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1880 Bonner Twp,, Pottawatomi County, IA census there is Pleasant Sublet, 74, married, farming, with wife Sarah, 50, Joseph, 16, Enos, 13, Mary, 11 and Peter 8. All but the 8 year old and the wife ('keeping house') are list
2 CONC ed as 'working on farm'. Pleasant lists his father as born in KY and his mother b. NC. Sarah is born in IN, her parents born in IN also.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Jan. 1, 1885 Boomer, Pottawatomi, IA census Pleasant (78) is recorded with Sarah (58), Joseph (20), Mary (15), Peter (12), Enos (18). (Their name is mistakenly transcribed on the Familysearch census as "Sabler). It says tha
2 CONC t Joseph was born in Appanoose Co. IA, everyone else born Harrison Co. It also says that Sarah is born in TN. They are recorded as living in Twp 77(?), Range 43, Section 8 of that county. Also says 'SW NW' which one would assume i
2 CONC s the corner of that section?
2 CONT
2 CONT Pleasant Sublette Birth: 	1812, Kentucky, USA Death: 	1893, Harrison County, Iowa, USA (Family records indicate that Pleasant died at the home of the Marshall's near Mondamin, or perhaps Modale, IA and may be buried at Branson Cem
2 CONC etery in an unmarked grave near his second wife Sarah. Or not.) Little is known of Pleasant Sublett . The family does not know the reason for the use of the name "Pleasant" which to anyone hearing it for the first time, would cons
2 CONC ider it unusual, but the name has been used in other branches of the Sublett family. A family member remembers that her grandfather Pleasant Sublett passed away at the home of her folks when she was small child, perhaps 6 or 7 yea
2 CONC rs old or about 1893. He was buried in Branson Cemetery , Loveland, Pottawattamie County.Iowa. From information on the birth of his children, it is known that Pleasant Sublett lived in Clinton , Gentry and Andrew Counties of Misso
2 CONC uri. In a letter written to a relative it stated. "Pleasant Sublett was a wealthy land owner in Missouri. The carpet baggers ran him out." It was then that he crossed the state line in to Iowa soon after the end of the Civil War. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Another family tree linked to the Subletts: http://gw.geneanet.org/tdowling?iz=404441&n=sublett&oc=0&p=pleasant
