2 CONT
2 CONT  William Edelman was born in Green County, TN.  The date of his birth and history of his family are unknown from lack of family history.
2 CONT  He mustered into the 33rd Indiana Voluntary Infantry, Sep 19, 1864 and discharged May 10, 1865.  His discharge at the time of enrollment gave his age as 31.  This would make him 65-66 at the time of death.
2 CONT  He was twice married, 1st to Lizzie Alexander.  To them were born 5 children: John, Ella, Albert, Rebecca and Nora.  The mother and Ella have passed into the world unseen.
2 CONT  The 2nd marriage was to Miss Josie Sherman.  By this union he was the father of 3 children: May, Ernest and Marie, all of whom are living.
2 CONT  He was well known in Johnson Co, having lived here for years.  Mr. Samuel Brown said to the writer that for years Mr. Edelman lived on his farm and he had never known a person who was more conscientious and strictly upright in al
2 CONC l his dealings than Mr. Edelman.  Others corroborate this testimony.
2 CONT  He was suddenly and unexpectedly called from time to eternity, Wednesday, Mar 22, 1899.  Brief funeral services were conducted by the pastor of the North Baptist Church in Franklin, in the presence of his sorrowing wife, children
2 CONC , and other relatives and friends after which his remains were laid to rest in the Hopewell Cemetery.
