3 NOTE Delahay /Delihay families of Talbot and Dorchester County, Maryland
4 CONT BACKGROUND (then DETAILS):
4 CONT 1] Thomas Delahay (abt 1654-Feb 1699) md to Eve Rich on 9 July 1681, Talbot County, Maryland  [Eve rich was the daughter of William Rich and the widow Alice Paddison  [Pattison];  he died Feb 1699/1700.  Seven children;  (We have 
4 CONC the wills of both Thomas and Eve; and the second husband of Eve—she md 2nd 21 Sep 1703 to Richard Holmes.] Thomas Delahay and his wife Eve Rich had seven known children.
4 CONT WILL
4 CONT Delahay, Thomas,Calvert Co.,4th Apr., 1697; 10th Feb., 1699. To wife Eve, 100 A., dwelling plantation, part of “Taylor's Ridge,” during life. To son Thomas and hrs., sd. plantation at decease of wife afsd. In event of his death wi
4 CONC thout issue, to pass sucseccively to son James and hrs., dau, Sarah and hrs., dau. Mary and hrs., To James Anderson of North Shields, should he come into the Province, godsons William Harding and John Harrison, personalty. To chil
4 CONC d. afsd., personalty. Child. to be brought up Protestants. Wife Eve, extx. and residuary legatee; brother William Rich to assist sd. wife in managing the estate. Test: Dan'l Morry, Jno. Gardner, Edward Thomas. 6. 330. 
4 CONT MARYLAND CALENDAR OF WILLS: Volume 2VOLUME II.Note:  Calvert County, Maryland is right across the water from Talbot and Dorchester Counties.
4 CONT
4 CONT [see also the will of Eve Talbot Holmes, his widow who outlived him and remarried.]
