1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://dla.library.upenn.edu/cocoon/dla/pacscl/ead.pdf?id=PACSCL_HSP_HLA200505 '''Wells Family Papers''']
2 CONT
2 CONT 1850 Census:
2 CONT
2 CONT Valentine (66), a farmer, and Phebe (65) were living in Middletown Township with 13 year old Abijah Bates in the household.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Research==
2 CONT '''''First thought''''':<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Looking back in PA immigrant history there is a Wells family of Lower Dublin who, with research, may yield Valentine Wells' parents.<br/>
2 CONT See: https://www.geni.com/people/John-Wells/6000000007851496892  who with his wife were part of the Quaker immigrants to the Delaware region.<br/>
2 CONT There are big gaps in the handling of his descendants.<br/>
2 CONT This looks to be not particularly useful in determining Valentine's parents.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Second thought''''': The death record of Valentine's son records that Valentine was born in Buckingham township. Only one Wells is recorded in Buckingham at the time of Valentine's birth. This is [https://www.geni.com/people/
2 CONC Jonathan-Wells-of-Buckingham/6000000001045185278 '''''Jonathan Wells'''''], who seems to be Valentine's grandfather. See [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000075610148855& '''''summary of tax assessment records''''']
2 CONC . In these records we see just how poor the Valentine Wells family was at the turn of the century. It moved multiple times to rentals in Middletown, Bristol, Falls, and then back to Middletown before acquiring land late in Valenti
2 CONC ne's life. The children's education was given for free as the family could not afford to pay fees.
2 CONT ==wife's family==
2 CONT Valentines's father-in-law was Gideon Shaw who, unlike his own father, died leaving a will.
