1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Lot's birth, portrait, and death information are available at https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/78897559/lot-edward-brewster
2 CONT * Lot's portrait is used courtesy of Find A Grave Member#47194125.
2 CONT * Also see page 293 (section 315) of ''The Brewster Genealogy, 1566-1907''. Compiled and edited by Emma C. Brewster Jones. Volume I. New York: The Grafton Press, 1907. Available online at https://www.google.com/books/edition/The_B
2 CONC rewster_Genealogy_1566_1907/bjU2AAAAMAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=John+William+Augustus+Brewster&pg=PA409&printsec=frontcover
2 CONT * Lot was engaged in the wholesale and retail dry-goods business. He had resided in Newcastle, Pennsylvania before he relocated to Cincinnati in 1831. He died of Asiatic cholera, one of the first victims of that disease in Cincinn
2 CONC ati. Lot was a master Freemason and a member of a Freemason lodge in New York City. He was a member of the city council of Cincinnati, being elected in 1841, 1844, and 1845. He was also a member of the Harmony Division, Sons of Te
2 CONC mperance, and was one of the founders and president of the New England Historic Genealogical Society in Cincinnati. See pages 164 and 165 of ''Memorial Biographies of The New England Historic Genealogical Society''. Volume I, 1845
2 CONC -1852. Boston: Published by The Society, 1880. Available online at https://www.google.com/books/edition/Memorial_Biographies_of_New_England_Hist/Liz2Fkd8Uz4C?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=Emma+Brewster+Mellen&pg=PA165&printsec=frontcover
2 CONT
