2 CONT * Angeline's marriage, educational, and death information are available on page 679 (section 771) of ''The Brewster Genealogy, 1566-1907''. Compiled and edited by Emma C. Brewster Jones. Volume II. New York: The Grafton Press, 190
2 CONC 7. Available online at https://www.google.com/books/edition/The_Brewster_Genealogy_1566_1907/bjU2AAAAMAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=John+William+Augustus+Brewster&pg=PA409&printsec=frontcover
2 CONT * Angeline and William were married on 26 April 1857 in Cincinnati, Hamilton County, Ohio. 
2 CONT * Angeline graduated from Mrs. Ryland's School for Young Ladies in Cincinnati. "She was naturally studious, and throughout her life was a reader of the best literature, and kept in touch with current events."
2 CONT * Angeline was a member of the Daughters of the American Revolution (member number 6104). From page 35 of ''Lineage Book, National Society of the Daughters of the American Revolution''. Volume VII, 6001-7000, 1894. By Mary Jane Se
2 CONC ymour, Historian General. Washington, D.C., 1898. Available online at https://www.google.com/books/edition/Lineage_Book_National_Society_of_the_Dau/ImcZAQAAIAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=Emma+Brewster+Mellen&pg=PA356&printsec=frontcover:
2 CONT ** "Mrs. Angeline C. Brewster Mellen.
2 CONT ** "Born in New York.
2 CONT ** "Wife of William Chamberlain Mellen. 
2 CONT ** "Descendant of Maj. Bernard Hubley, of Pennsylvania. 
2 CONT ** "Daughter of Lot. E. Brewster and Eliza Rich Hubley, his wife. 
2 CONT ** "Granddaughter of Bernard Hubley and Elizabeth McCalla, his wife. 
2 CONT ** "Bernard Hubley raised and commanded a company averaging in height six feet. He fought in many battles, was wounded, but served to the close of the war and was a member of the Society of the Cincinnati."
