1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Martha Campbell Weare (Rogers)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/46692151/martha_campbell_weare
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha Campbell Rogers (born 22 June 1836) was the daughter of Gustavus Adolphus Rogers and Susan Ann Campbell. She became the second wife of the wealthy banker John Weare on 26 December 1861. On an excursion hosted by railroad ma
2 CONC gnate John I. Blair, with her husband and other railroad investor associates at St. Paul Junction, Iowa, the women were asked to choose a novel name for the locale that would someday receive a post office. They chose "La Mars," af
2 CONC ter the common first letters of their first names. As Martha Weare, she was one of the "M"s. Some details include one other woman named Mary Weare as the second "M". If Martha's stepdaughter Martha Parkhurst Weare (born 15 June 18
2 CONC 58) were present, perhaps she was the second "M". Another and perhaps stronger possibility could be her sister-in-law Mary Ann Weare Ely (b. 25 February 1819}.
