2 CONT *This memorial is a cenotaph which is permissible under Findagrave guidelines because a memorial stone with her name is located at the Wenger Meeting House Cemetery in Jonestown,Pennsylvania. She may actually be buried here with h
2 CONC er husband.*
2 CONT
2 CONT Note~Her year of birth is approximate. She died after 1773.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Benjamin Meshe who immigrated from Ireland. He had a land patent from the Penns in Rapho Township north of Manheim. Her sister Anna married Christian's brother Stephan. The name was sometimes spelled Meshey
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth married Christian Wenger. They were the parents of the following known children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1-Rev. John M. Wenger/ Wingert (1758) 2-Elizabeth Wenger (1759) 3-Maria Wenger (1760) married her uncle John Wenger's stepson Heinrich Huber  4-Amele or Anele 'Emily' Wenger (abt 1763) 5-Christian M. Wenger (1770) 
2 CONT
