2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/147245021/chefran-elizabeth-wenger
2 CONT
2 CONT This memorial is a cenotaph which is permissible under Findagrave guidelines because a memorial stone with her name is located at the Wenger Meeting House Cemetery in Jonestown, Pennsylvania. She may actually be buried here with h
2 CONC er husband John Wenger.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note~ She was born ABOUT 1740. Her maiden name was NOT Huber, rather she was the widow of John Huber when she married her second husband, John Wenger. She died AFTER 1792.
2 CONT
2 CONT Chefran was the second wife of Hans 'John' Wenger. Her first husband was John Huber (abt 1740 Switzerland- before 1764). Chefran left Europe after her husband Herr Von Huber, an officer in the German Army was killed during the Sev
2 CONC en Year War. She and her three children left one of the German Cantons of Switzerland and emigrated to America, arriving about 1764. They settled in Lebanon County in 1765. Their son Michael died at sea. (according to 'The Genealo
2 CONC gy of Heinrich Huber')
2 CONT
2 CONT John Wenger's first wife was Maria Sherrick (abt 1737-1760). The children of John Wenger and Maria Sherrick were:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1-Rev. Christian Wenger (Dec 23 1756-July 28 1841) married Maria Weaver (1759-1839)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2-Johannes 'John' Wenger (1758 or 1762- July 3 1829 Franklin Co. PA) NG married Elizabeth Bechtel (1765-1831)
2 CONT
2 CONT 3-Martin Wenger (1759-1820 Franklin Co. PA) wife unknown, children identified
2 CONT
2 CONT 4-Veronica 'Franica' Wenger (1760- after 1832) married Jacob D. Detwiler (1760 lanc Co. PA- 1832 Franklin Co. PA)
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of John Wenger and Chefran Huber Wenger were:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1-Rev. Abraham Wingert (abt 1765-1830) may have married Elizabeth Detwiler
2 CONT
2 CONT 2-Barbara Wenger (abt 1768-1847/ Florimont PA) may have been married to Hans Ulrich Amstutz
2 CONT
2 CONT 3-Elizabeth Wenger (abt 1770- ? Franklin Co. PA) married John Sollenberger
2 CONT
2 CONT 4-Susanna Wenger (abt 1773)
2 CONT
2 CONT 5-Anna Wenger (abt 1776) may be Maria Wenger born Dec. 17, 1755 who married Abraham Kobel* The Bible record itself names her "Wenerin" but another book received from the same family has a 1774 ownership inscription from "Anna Mari
2 CONC a Wengerin im Libanon"In the year of our Lord 1756, December 15, I, Abraham Kobel was born into this miserable world, and in the year of our Lord 1755, December 17, my wife Anna, born a Wenger, was born into this miserable world, 
2 CONC and in the year of our Lord 1783, September 14, we entered into the state of holy matrimony. " He then listed their seven children.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6-Rev. Jacob Wenger (Dec 1 1778- March 31 1858) married Barbara Wolf
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Chefran and her first husband John Huber were:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1-Heinrich Huber (abt 1757- ? Franklin Co. PA) married Maria Wenger (1760- ?) daughter of Christian Wenger and Elizabeth Meshe
2 CONT
2 CONT 2-Catherine (Katrina Huber) Hoover (abt 1764- Dec 12 1837 Franklin Co. PA or VA) married Joseph (Jost) Wenger (Dec 19 1767 Chambersburg PA- April 22 1840 Cave Spring VA), son of Martin Wenger and Annali Gingrich; Catherine is ment
2 CONC ioned in her stepfather John Wenger's will
2 CONT
2 CONT 3-Michael Huber (died at sea 1764)
