2 CONT # Note: Born Richen, Baden, Germany. Martin was the oldest son, at least at the time of his father's death. Arrived in Lancaster Co. (now Lebanon Co.) PA after crossing the ocean on the ship 'Brotherhood' via Philadelphia. Martin 
2 CONC was 18 years old. He immigrated with his brother Hans who settled in Frederick Co., MD. Married Judith Wenger, 1732.1.19 1811.3.5, G13, (i1748.9.16) A farmer just west of Lebanon, Bethlehem Steel Plant. Was Lancaster Co. now Leban
2 CONC on Co. Mennonite. European family has been identified. See Edward Bowman Esbenshade; My American Ancestors, p. 298. His will, WB A-1-339 is dated Dec. 3, 1796 and was probated Jan. 9, 1797 (63-10-19)
2 CONT --------------------
