1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: 	1740 Lancaster County Pennsylvania, USA Death: 	unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna was the daughter of Johannes Groh and Maria Groff.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was previously thought to be the native American named Anna Eroe who helped her husband as a translator. Many people still have this in their family trees but it was discovered to be a misreading of her name.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married to Abraham Wenger. Only her two youngest children Martin and Mary remained in the area. The others went to western Pennsylvania, Ohio, and Canada. Abraham died in Bethel township.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her known children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1-John Wenger 2-Abraham Wenger 3-Isaac Wenger 4-Jacob Wenger 5-Henry Wenger 6-Mary Wenger 7-Martin Wenger (abt 1780-Dec 1855), married Maria Schenk (1775-1843), daughter of Martin & Anna Schenk. Martin was born and died on the anc
2 CONC estral farm near Jonestown. His son Martin Wenger Jr. added a 'T' to the family surname. His wife was Anna 'Nancy' Herr. Nancy's 4th great grandparents were Bishop Hans Herr and Elizabeth Mylin Kendig.
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LHD4-7BS                                                                                     https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/132017548/anna_groff_wenger                         
