2 CONT @R1300748235@  Ancestry Family Trees  Online publication - Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com.  Original data:  Family Tree files submitted by Ancestry members. Ancestry Family Tree  http://trees.ancestry.com/pt/AMTCitationRedir.aspx?ti
2 CONC d=113982238&pid=936
2 CONT Joseph was the son of immigrants Martin Wengert and Annali Gingrich. He married Catherine 'Katrina' Huber/ Hoover and they were the parents of the following known children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1-Michael Wingert/ Wenger (abt 1790)
2 CONT 2-Martin Wingart/ Winger (Aug 5 1791)
2 CONT 3-Joseph Wingert/ Winger (abt 1794)
2 CONT 4-Henry M. Wingart/ Wingert (Jan 23 1800)
2 CONT 5-Jacob Wingart/ Vingart (1806)
2 CONT 6-Susanna Wingar (Aug 11 1807) married John Shafer
2 CONT 7-Nancy Wenger (Oct 5 1811) married Benjamin Barnhart, then Michael Rettinger
2 CONT
2 CONT [Burial location is from the late Wenger Family historian Roger Daniel Winger of Indiana. According to Daniel L. Wenger's extensive database, he died in Botetourt (now Roanoke) County and was originally buried in the graveyard bet
2 CONC ween the old poor house of Roanoke County and the river (current location of Virginia Western Community College). The poor house cemetery was moved to Roanoke City about 1900. The last burial was in 1958, and the following year th
2 CONC e graves were removed when work began on the Roanoke Technical Institute. City officials painstakingly identified as many graves as they could and removed the bodies to the city-owned cemetery at Coyner Springs.]
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no listing for the original, now defunct poor house cemetery, so he is presumed to have been moved with the others.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/170273609/joseph-winger Find A Grave Memorial] - [https:
2 CONC //www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 26 2025, 23:52:37 UTC''
