1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Felix Light, one of the oldest, if not the oldest, residents of Lebanon County died Tuesday morning at his home, 921 Maple Street. General debility is assigned as the cause of death. He was ill for thirteen weeks, 
2 CONC and death came as a relief from suffering. He was aged 84 years on March 7 last, and is survived by five children: Alfred, Arthur, Ebenezer, Lemuel and Miss Fannie B. Light, all of this city. Mrs. Light (nee Sarah Light), wife of 
2 CONC the deceased, died about ten years ago. The deceased was a native of Lebanon, having been born in the old home still standing near Tenth and Maple Streets. Early in his career, he went to North Annville township, where he engaged 
2 CONC in farming, and remained there for several years. At the expiration of that time, he returned to Lebanon, and during the past 50 years he lived in the home in which he died.  He was engaged most of this time in the horse business 
2 CONC with his cousin, Asaph Light, who is at present at  Bloomington, Ill., in the same business. They conducted an exchange stable on Maple Street, and later Mr. Light continued it as a livery. The deceased was a son of the late Jacob
2 CONC  Light, and is the last of that family, his brother, Gideon Light, having died about five years ago. [Lebanon Semi Weekly News, May 16, 1907, Page 4]
