2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 MAR 1901
2 PLAC Cearfoss, Washington County, Maryland, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mrs. ANNA HARTRAUFT died Sunday near Cearfoss, of pneumonia, aged 52 years.  Her husband is critically ill with the same trouble.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a member of the Mennonite church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are the following children: David L. and Jacob L., at home; Mrs. Emmet Hykes, Leitersburg district; brothers, John Lesher, State Line; Samuel Lesher, Pinola, Pa.; sisters, Mrs. Joseph Horst, Mrs. Israel Rieff, Mrs. Mary 
2 CONC Geist, all of Maugansville; Mrs. Tene Shafer, Latonia O.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services and interment at Reiff's Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Mail (Hagerstown, MD)
2 CONT Friday, March 29, 1901
2 CONT ***********************
2 CONT Obituary for her sons below:
2 CONT
2 CONT DAVID L. HARTRANFT, a well known farmer residing along the Cearfoss pike, died suddenly from heat trouble Saturday evening, aged 45 years.  Mr. Hartranft had been to the Joseph Horst sale at Maugansville.  After the sale he had go
2 CONC ne to the barn to harness up his team, preparing to leave for home.  His long absence caused an investigation to be made which resulted in his being found lying in one of the stalls in an unconscious condtion.  He was carried into
2 CONC   the house and Dr. V.D. Miller summoned, but Mr. Hartranft expire3d before the physician arrived.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his wife and two sons, Harold and Vernon, at home; father, Aaron Hartranft, Maugansville; step-mother, Mrs. Mary Hartranft; brother, Jacob Hartranft, near Cearfoss; and sister, Mrs. Emma Hikes, Leitersburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral Tuesday with services at Reiff's Church.  Interment in graveyard adjoining.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Morning Herald (Hagerstown, MD)
2 CONT September 24, 1917, page 3
2 CONT *****************************
2 CONT JACOB L. HARTRANFT, 532 Salem Avenue, died at the Washington County Hospital Saturday morning of paralysis after an illness of one week, aged 70 years.  He was a member of the Cedar Grove Mennonite Church and a retired farmer for 
2 CONC the last 25 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Besides his wife, Mrs. Annie E. Hartranft, his survivors are: son, LeRoy; daughter, Mrs. Wilbur Grossnickle, Mercersburg, Pa.; sister, Mrs. Emma L. Hykes, near Leitersburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services in Cedar Grove Mennonite church; intermen t in cemetery adjoining.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Daily Mail (Hagerstown, MD)
2 CONT August 16, 1948, page 2
2 CONT ******************************* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/180856821/catharine-hartranft Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 10 2026, 1:41:12 UTC''
