2 CONC fd1e73e6cc6fa887e MyHeritage Family Trees] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 12 2020, 23:45:05 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT DEATH CLAIMS MRS. HORST AT CLEONA HOME - Mrs. Barbara L. Horst, widow of Aaron Horst, who was one time commissioner of Lebanon County and who died about eight years ago, died on Monday evening at her home in Cleona. She was strick
2 CONC en with influenza during the epidemic of that disease last Fall, and she never regained her normal health, although she was able to be about since then. She was ill in bed for three weeks, when, on Monday, she was stricken with a 
2 CONC paralytic stroke, and medical aid was unavailing in bringing her back to health. She was in the 64th year of her age.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was highly respected as a member of the United Brethren Church. She was one of two children of the late John Shirk, and leaves two sons – Albert Horst, of Bellegrove, and Shirk Horst, of Cleona, who made his home with his moth
2 CONC er. A brother, John Shirk, of near Kauffman's Church, North Annville Township. There are seven grandchildren. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral will be held on Friday morning, at 10 o'clock, with services in the Cleona United Brethren Church, and burial in the afternoon at the Bellegrove United Brethren Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: This information was provided by Find A Grave contributor Debora Cayton. She has possession of the Peter Horst Family Bible 
