1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dr. John Henry Sherk was born Feb 24, 1841, in E. Hanover Township, Lebanon, PA.    At the age of twelve year he was sent to the Academy in Lebanon.  At fourteen, he was sent to school at Lititz.  While there he wa
2 CONC s attacked wit typhoid fever ,which so impaired his health that he was compelled to abandon his  intention of attending college.  He subsequently read medicine  and was graduated from the University of Pennsylvania, march 1860.   
2 CONC  The following month he opened an office in Annville, PA, but only remained there until the following October, when he moved to Philadelphia, (1163 Vine St) and opened an office on  Sixteeenteh street.  He was prescribing physicia
2 CONC n at the Catharine Street House of Industry in  1863 and 1864  He gained an hornorarium from the Philadelphia Dispensary in 1865, and again in 1868.  He examined students on Obstetrics and Diseseases of Women and Children, during 
2 CONC the winter term of 1866 and 1867, in conneciton with Drs. Vanderslice and Collins of the University.  During the winter of 1866 and 1867, he had charge of the clinic for Diseases of Women and Children in the Obstetrical Department
2 CONC  of the Philadelphia Dispensary.  He died of Phthisis pulmonalis May 24, 1870.  He was skillful, faithful and laborious as a practitioner.  His affable manners, his warm sympathy for the suffering and the poor attached him in a re
2 CONC markable manner to all his patients.  His success might be considered above the average.  He was twice married; first to Emma D. Humphries, Dec 20, 1859;  She died march 14, 1866.  On Feb. 19, 1868 he married the sister of his for
2 CONC mer wife, Maggie R. Humphries.  The issue of his first marriage were two children, as follows, Bessie H. Sherk, residing in Philadelphia. and Dr. Henry H. Sherk, who married and has children.  He is practising his profession in Pa
2 CONC sadena, CA.  
