2 CONC 51 yrs"
2 CONT       Land  	29 May 1685  [3] 
2 CONT           o On May 29, 1685 a warrant granted to his father William Gregg for 200 acres was confirmed by patent to John Gregg on February 18, 1693 and later sold to Samuel Underwook, Sr. whose executor re-sold part of it back to J
2 CONC ohn Gregg, who sold it to Jonathan Strange on February 18, 1733. John Gregg paid the taxes for the whole estate of his father 1693-1696.
2 CONT       Biographical  	1687  [3] 
2 CONT       assumed reponsibility of the home at nineteen when his father passed awa. 
