2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40001-709555630/levi-howell-in-familysearch-family-tree FamilySearch Family Tree] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 7 2019, 0:26:29 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Levi was the son of Samson Howell (1718-1803), and grandson of Hugh Howell (1659-1745).
2 CONT
2 CONT Levi married  Mary Green (1790-1861).
2 CONT
2 CONT Records indicate that they had two children: a son George Howell, and a daughter Rebecca (1790-1836).
2 CONT
2 CONT Excerpts by Eleanor (Hugg) Casagrand: 
2 CONT
2 CONT "He was a man of wealth and worth in Church and State nor scorned the poor nor feared the great [NJHS, Newark, NJ, Albertson Family File, Folder 2]."
2 CONT
2 CONT "Levi Howell, Esq., breakfasted with us.  He is from Sussex with a load of flour.  He brought it on a sled and says the snow is so deep his neighborhood that it is difficult passing ["Wintry Encores Old Hat in Morris," Sussex Coun
2 CONC ty Historical Society VF.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Correspondence from Levi to son Samson in Canada [Sussex Co HS]: 25 Nov 1816: "Dear children...Samuel minds the mill and is trusty.  Your poor brothers Levi and George have got in such a practise of drinking Spirits that I fear it
2 CONC  will ruin them both Soul and Body--and your mother is further from getting Religion than she was twenty years ago.  Pray for us 27 Nov 1819: "My dear children...Through the mercy of a good God I myself your mother and Samuel are 
2 CONC as well as common...It has got so late in the fall I  think I cant come to see you till spring, but if God spares my unprofitable life, I think I shall come once more to your country." 7 Apr 1821: "I have kept account of all the s
2 CONC nows last winter and this makes when all put together 5 feet 6 inches.  Last winter about 5 feet." 7 May 1821: "Thank God we are all alive yet, and unaling well...from your old and infirme father." 1 May 1822: "I took a cold in th
2 CONC e beginning of the winter and have a bad coff yet.  Two weeks ago my beast blundered down with me, and my right shoulder struck a stone and hurt it very much, and I can hardly write with it yet, but want to hear from you once more
2 CONC  while in this veil of teers...I feel myself declining very fast...your old and infirm father."
2 CONT
2 CONT Rev. Casper Schaeffer: said of "Levi Howell, residing in the lower part of Hardwick Township, Sussex County, N.J., was an excellent, pious man, and a local preacher in the Methodist connection.  He was for a number of years a memb
2 CONC er of the Legislature.  He was a little eccentric, but an honest, upright man, and zealous for the truth as he apprehended it.  He died in a good old age, say about seventy-five years, about 1820."
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Will & Testament 11 May 1825, pro. 24 Aug 1825: Levi Howell of Hardwick, Warren Co, NJ: wife, Mary; sons: Samuel G., John, Samson, Levi, Jonah, William; grandson George Washington Smyth; son George G.; daughters: Jane Alberts
2 CONC on, Mary Harris, Rebecca Read; executors: son John & son-in-law John Harris.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/30581070/levi-howell Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 9 2019, 2:20:14 UTC''
2 CONT
