1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Keziah Parke
2 CONT * Parents: Roger Parke, Jr. (1683- 1745) & a woman whose name is not known
2 CONT * Birth: 1713 Hunterdon, NJ	
2 CONT * Married: James Larison 1734 Mercer, New Jersey	
2 CONT * Died: 1788 Hunterdon, NJ
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # John Larison b: 1737 in , Hunterdon, New Jersey
2 CONT #  Andrew Larison b: 2 Feb 1739 in Hopewell, Mercer, New Jersey, United States
2 CONT #  William Larison b: 24 Jan 1740/1741 in Hopewell, Hunterdon, New Jersey
2 CONT #  Anne Larison b: 1743 in , Hunterdon, New Jersey
2 CONT #  Roger Larison b: 1745 in Hopewell, Hunterdon, New Jersey
2 CONT #  Elizabeth Larison b: 1747 in Hopewell, Hunterdon, New Jersey
2 CONT #  Catherine Larison b: 1750 in Hopewell, Hunterdon, New Jersey
2 CONT #  Achsah Larison b: 1752 in Hopewell, Hunterdon, New Jersey
2 CONT #  Elijah Larison b: 1754 in Hopewell, Hunterdon, New Jersey
2 CONT #  David Larison b: 8 Mar 1757 in Hopewell, Hunterdon, New Jersey
2 CONT
2 CONT notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Roger and [__?__]  Baptism dates are not a good proxy for birth in the Parke family.  The Parkes were Quakers and they baptized their children in the Anglican Church due to political necessity.
2 CONT
2 CONT Due to a scandal known as “the Coxe Affair”  ownership of the Parke’s homestead and many other pioneer families was invalidated.  Many of Roger’s relatives including their son, Roger Parke, migrated from Hopewell, NJ to Frederick 
2 CONC Co., VA  later Hampshire Co., WV and to the Jersey Settlement in Rowan County, North Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT from http://minerdescent.com/2010/05/19/roger-parkes-jr/
2 CONT
2 CONT >Roger Parke Jr. was born in 1683 Burlington County NJ. His parents were  Roger PARKE Sr. and Ann PATTISON.  He did NOT marry Susannah ROBINSON about 1698  in Crosswicks Creek New Jersey.. The name of his wife is unknown. Some mis
2 CONC taken information having to do with a will of a Thomas Robinson got this started but it has no basis in truth, having been researched extensively by many Parke family researchers.  It has also been speculated that his wife was Jan
2 CONC e Stout or a woman named Hannah before 1704, but this also is just speculation – so his wife’s name is unknown.  Roger died in 1755 in Hunterdon County, NJ.
2 CONT
