2 CONT From "The History of Union County NJ 1664-1923  by A Van Doren Honeyman 1923
2 CONT
2 CONT James Bollen came over with the English fleet in 1664, and as he was styled
2 CONT
2 CONT "Captain," he nay have been in command of one of the vessels. He was deputized by (Col.) Nicolls to receive the surrender of the fort at New Amsterdam, (Sep. 8, 1664) and was appointed by him "Commissary of the Ammunition at New Y
2 CONC ork." He remained at New York until August, 1665, as his name appears often in court records.  There is no doubt he was acquainted with Governor Carteret in England, who on his first voyage sent his dispatches from Newport News, V
2 CONC irginia, June 13, 1665, to Captain James Bullaigne in New York.  On the arrival of Governor Carteret at the port of New York, Bollen was made secretary of the new province and accompanied the governor in August to Elizabethtown."
2 CONT
2 CONT James Bollen
2 CONT
