2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth place is written "Isle of Jersey, Europe" I assume this means the island off of the coast of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT -TonyBloom
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT A sister* (or cousin) of Anna Bollen, wife of Johnathan Stout 1660-1723, Peter's brother; Anna Bollen [spelling difference sic] is "Probably a daughter of Capt. James Bollen, who first appears in New Jersey records on 28 October 1
2 CONC 664 when he witnessed the delivery of wampum to the Indians for the purchase of Elizabethtown. He was a J. P. and secretary of the province. The early records of New Jersy [sic] (1665-1667) appear in his handwriting. In 1681 he wa
2 CONC s president of the court in Woodbridge. Tradition says that he was closely related to Anne Boleyn" (p. 6).
2 CONT
2 CONT Above information from (p. 4, footnotes 7, 8) Stout and Allied Families: Volume One, 1951, Harold F. Stout, The Eagle Press, Dover, Ohio
2 CONT
2 CONT Below from http://www.solavirtusnobilitat.com/pedigree/individual.php?pid=I2668&ged=19%20jan%2008.ged
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Bollen and Ann Bollen daughters of James Bollen. This same Mary is identified as the wife of Peter Stout, confirming the likely relationship with sister Ann and father James.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Bullen, d/o James and Anne, b 1655 on Isle of Jersey, England (LDS Ancestry File) [It is unlikely that she is born in England when father is born and died in NJ, unless of course father's information is incorrect].
2 CONT
2 CONT ===========================
2 CONT
2 CONT   Noted events in her life were:
2 CONT
2 CONT • MARY BOLLEN, wife of Peter Stout, daughter of JAMES BOLLEN and ANNE VAUQUELLIN . She was born 1655 in Isle of Jersey, England, and died 1692 in Middletown, Hunterdon Co., NJ. (posted as family story at Ancestry.com)
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://woodlin.net/lindley/398.htm
2 CONT
