1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===John Stout
2 CONT * Birth: 1645 in Gravesend, Kings Co., NY, USA  
2 CONT * Moved to Hopewell, NJ with brothers Jonathan and David in 1704
2 CONT * Death: 24 Nov 1724 in Middletown, Monmouth Co., NJ, USA  
2 CONT * Father: Richard STOUT (1615-1705) 
2 CONT * Mother: Penelope Van Princes STOUT (1620-1730)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {{New Netherland Settler}}
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Stout-81
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stout, son of Richard I and Penelope Kent Van Princin Stout, was born 1643 or 1644 [1] and married Elizabeth Crawford January 12 1671 by John Bowne, Justice of the Peace.[2] He remained in Middleton, New Jersey and died befor
2 CONC e February 11 1724/5 date his will was proved [3]and as indicated by the fact that his cattle-mark was assumed by his grandson, John Stout the new Town Clerk. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT John and his wife drew Lot 19 and Lot 5 which totaled 240 acres in Middletown, December 30 1667 as one of its first settlers recorded 30 December, 1667. [5][6] This is an overview of John Stout who bought and sold land, was a farm
2 CONC er, built a home on the main street town lot, recorded his cattle-mark September 4 1672, was active in civic affairs, held several city offices and appointed an ensign under Captain John Bowne and Lieutenant James Grover July 4 16
2 CONC 81. The details of his life can be found here. [7] [8]
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of John Sr and Elizabeth Crawford Stout were:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Richard m (1) Esther Tilton, daughter of Peter and Rebecca Brazier Tilton, (2) Mary Tilton, Esther's sister.
2 CONT # John Jr m Unknown, had son Richard.
2 CONT # Hope Still
2 CONT # Deliverance
2 CONT # Frances?
2 CONT # Penelope
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stout, Jr, son of John Sr and Elizabeth Crawford Stout, based on the passing of his cattle-mark to his son Richard, died before May 12 1753. It continued to be passed from Richard to George Taylor, Jr. in 1761 to John Stout, 
2 CONC the carpenter, to Richard Stout, son of John Stout, the carpenter. [9]
2 CONT
2 CONT Hope Still and Deliverance were twins and born in the block house during an Indian attack which Samuel Smith dates as AD 1669 on p. 67. Deliverance's name was originally Faith and changed after the block house attack ended. Their 
2 CONC story may be found here [10][11] [12]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation: Farmer 
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Elizabeth were married by Justice of the Peace John Bowne.In 1675 he was chosen a magistrate of a Monthly Court of small cases. 1679-1680 he was chosen a deputy to represent Middletown in the local Assembly. On 4 July 168
2 CONC 1, John was appointed an ensign in the military company of Middletown and in 1684-5, he was appointed constable of Middletown. When Middletown was settled  in 1664-5, he drew a lot on Main Street and one in an outlying area.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stout was born in 1645 in Gravesend, Long Island, NY, the oldest son of Richard and Penelope Stout. He married Elizabeth Crawford on January 12, 1670 in Middleton, NJ. The were married by Justice of the Peace, John Bowne. Joh
2 CONC n was a farmer. In 1675 he was chosen a magistrate of a Monthly Court of small cases. 1679-1680 he was chosen a deputy to represent Middletown in the local Assembly. On 4 July 1681, John was appointed an ensign in the military com
2 CONC pany of Middletown and in 1684-5, he was appointed constable of Middletown. When Middletown was settled in 1664-5, he drew a lot on Main Street and one in an outlying area. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Will: 1724 Dec.14. Stout, John, of Middleton, Monmouth Co.; Wife and children, names not given. Real and personal estate. Executor~Hugh Hartshorne. Witnesses-Curneljuus Comton, Elisabeth Watson, Mary Estete (? ?), John Watson. Pro
2 CONC ved February 11, 1724-5. Lib. A, p 328 .  
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Unknown 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT  John Stout,  the eldest son of Richard the First, named his eldest son Richard, who when married settled at a place called Squan, and was generally after called "Squan Dick," and raised a large family, some of whom settled about 
2 CONC Barnegat and along the shore - a great number of whose descendants are there to this day. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The said John named his second son John, who, in consequence of his following the seas, was called "Sailor John," of whose family I am able to give but little account, although it was numerous. One daughter, whose name was Penelop
2 CONC e, married John Sutphen, who afterward moved near Neshanie, and had four children, viz: three sons and one daughter, whose names were Derrick, John, Stout and Sarah.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://familysearch.org/photos/stories/263682
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stout was born 1645 in Gravesend, Long Island, NY and, in 1667 drew lot no. 19 in Middletown. Marriage 1 Elizabeth Crawford b: 1650-married: 13 Jan 1671 in Middletown, Monmouth, New Jersey. Marriage 2 Anna Bollen b: 1665-Marr
2 CONC ied: 27 AUG 1685 in Monmouth, NewJersey Marriage 3 Mary Lee b. 1652-Married: 1693 Middletown, Monmouth, New Jersey, United States Occupation: Farmer John and Elizabeth were married by Justice of the Peace John BOWNE.
2 CONT
2 CONT  ------
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: FIRST TOWN BOOK OF MIDDLETOWN NY: He married Elizabeth Crawford 13 Jan 1671 in Middletown, Monmouth, New Jersey. She was born ABT 1650 in Middletown, Monmouth, New Jersey, and died in Woodbridge, Middlesex, New Jersey
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT U.S. and International Marriage Records, 1560-1900 Author: Yates Publishing Repository: Name: Ancestry.com Text: Name: Elizabeth Crawford Gender: female Birth Year: 1650 Spouse Name: Jonathan [sic: John] Stout Spouse Birth Place: 
2 CONC NY Spouse Birth Year: 1644 Marriage Year: 1671 Marriage State: NJ Number Pages: 1 
2 CONT
2 CONT ------ 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st wife, Elizabeth Crawford b: 1650 in New Jersey Married: 12 Jan 1670 in Middletown, Monmouth, New Jersey, United States Children Richard Stout b: 1678 in Middletown, Monmouth, New Jersey, United States Faith Deliverance Stout b
2 CONC : 1679 John Stout b: 1680 Penelope Stout b: 1686 in Middleton, Monmouth County, New Jersey Frances Stout b: 1700 in Middletown, Monmouth, New Jersey, United States
2 CONT
2 CONT  ---------------------- 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT === Conflicts ===
2 CONT ::In the book Space:The_History_of_the_Stout_Family|History of the Stout Family, By Nathan Stout, 1823, the author acknowledges his lackof information on Sailor John's family, and incorrectly reports that the subject of this profi
2 CONC le is Sailor John.  However, based on what wedo know of this John, he does not follow the description of a man 'following the seas'. As pointed out by John E Stillwell in "Historical and genealogical miscellany" page 322 <ref>John
2 CONC  E. Stillwell, 1916, page 322 http://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal04stil#page/322/mode/1up</ref>, this John, based on occupation and residence could not be he, and Sailor John, is instead, Stout-1165|John Stout. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ::Crannell-6|Linda Crannell proposes that another child might be named Penelope. Penelope is possibly a repetition of the conflict notedabove, which also cited that Sailor John had a daughter that was named Penelope. For this reas
2 CONC on,  and since no sources support it, Penelope is not added as a child here. Of note, however, is that Stillwell does concede that there are likely other children to this marriage. 
2 CONT
