2 CONT ===James Stout
2 CONT * Birth: 	1658, Gravesend, Kings County (Brooklyn) New York, USA 
2 CONT * Death: 	1715, Monmouth County, New Jersey, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT I shall now introduce James, the fifth son of Richard the first. I know not into what family he married, but he had three sons and four daughters, viz: 
2 CONT *1. Benjamin, 
2 CONT *2. James, 
2 CONT *3. Joseph , 
2 CONT *4. Penelope, 
2 CONT *5. Elizabeth, 
2 CONT *6. Mercy and 
2 CONT *7. Anne. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Eldest son) Benjamin married Ruth Bogart, by whom he had two sons and six daughters, viz: 
2 CONT *1. Joseph, 
2 CONT *2. Benjamin, 
2 CONT *3. Elizabeth, 
2 CONT *4. Sarah, 
2 CONT *5. Mary, 
2 CONT *6. Rachel, 
2 CONT *7. Ruth and 
2 CONT *8. Anne. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Grandchildren by eldest son):
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Joseph married a daughter of Gabriel Huff, by whom he had two children, viz: 
2 CONT *1. John and 
2 CONT *2. Mary. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Benjamin married a daughter of William Anderson, named Elizabeth, by whom he had a great number of children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Elizabeth, who was the eldest sister to the last mentioned Joseph and Benjamin , was married to John Quick, son of Francis, by whom she had three sons and four daughters, viz: 
2 CONT *1. Joseph, 
2 CONT *2. Moses, 
2 CONT *3. Benjamin, 
2 CONT *4. Sarah 
2 CONT *5. Ruth, 
2 CONT *6. Elizabeth and 
2 CONT *7. Mary. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Eldest son) Joseph married Roxana Quick, the daughter of Jacob Quick, and had no children. 
2 CONT (Second son) Moses married Sarah Saxton, the daughter of Jared Saxton, by whom he has a family of children. 
2 CONT (Third son) Benjamin married, but I know not into what family nor the number of his children.
2 CONT (Eldest daughter) Sarah, sister to the three last mentioned brothers, was married to John Taylor, by whom she had a son Peter, which is all the description I can give of her family. 
2 CONT (Second daughter) Ruth was married to an Englishman of the name of William Abbott -- can give no description of her family. 
2 CONT (Third daughter) Elizabeth is not married. 
2 CONT (Fourth daughter) Mary was married to George Agee -- can give no description o f her family. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Sarah was married to Zebulon Stout, the son of Zebulon, and died without issue.  
2 CONT 5. Mary married a Hunt.  
2 CONT 6. Rachel married Stephen Hewell. 
2 CONT 7. Ruth also married.  
2 CONT 8. Anne married Abraham Stout, by whom she had a daughter and named her Sarah.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT James's father Richard Stout was an early English settler under Dutch rule at a Gravesend, Brooklyn, Kings, western Long Island, circa 1644 to 1657. Gravesend is a neighborhood in south-central Brooklyn, along the shore of Gravese
2 CONC nd Bay and Coney Island. In 1609 Henry Hudson landed his ship the Half Moon there at the island known by the natives as Narrioch (Coney Island). In 1643 Gravesend then became one of the original towns founded in the Dutch colony o
2 CONC f New Netherland when Governor Willem Kieft granted a land patent to the Anabaptist Lady Deborah Moody, as a site where that English sect could settle free from religious persecution. Clashes with the natives delayed the town for 
2 CONC two more years, until December 19, 1645.
2 CONT
2 CONT James Stout I was born at Gravesend, Long Island, New Netherland. He was a son of Richard I and Penelope Kent Van Princin Stout. [1] James Stout, son of Richard I and Penelope Kent Van Princin, married Elizabeth Truax (?). [2]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A discussion about whether James Stout's wife, Elizabeth was a Truax may be found here. [3] One point of interest is that in 1712 there was an Elizabeth Stout who was a member of the Baptist Church in Middleton and Agnes Truax Sto
2 CONC ut, wife of Benjamin Stout who was a member also.[4] Agnes was the daughter of Jacob Truax and the wife of Benjamin Stout, James' brother. [5], The following family tree references the work of Frederick Virtus regarding Agnes' par
2 CONC ents and names Benjamin as husband of Agnes and Richard III as husband of Eve--two brothers, two sisters, two marriages why not Lizbeth and James? [6]
2 CONT
2 CONT James and Elizabeth Truax? Stout were the parents of:
2 CONT
2 CONT #     Elizabeth b about 1690, m Rev John Warford Jr 1708 
2 CONT #     Joseph b before 1700, moved to Pennsylvania 
2 CONT #     Penelope b May 20 1700, d Jul 11 1776, m (1) Jewell in 1715, (2) William Merrill about 1729, (3) Isaac Herrin in 1741.#Benjamin b Jan 24 1704, d before Sep 19 1767 m Ruth Bogart 
2 CONT #     James b 1706, d 1786, m Johana Johnson about 1732 
2 CONT #     Mercy m Mr Warner 
2 CONT #     Anne m Cornelius Johnson.[7][8][9]  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
