1 NOTE {geni:about_me} David Stout, son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Richard-Stout-of-Monmouth/6000000002545340068 Richard Stout] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Penelope-Stout/6000000003354857976 Penelope Van Princin], was born 1667
2 CONC  in Middletown, Monmouth County, New Jersey.  He married [https://www.geni.com/people/Rebecca-Stout/6000000006110954967 Rebecca Ashton], daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/James-Ashton/6000000001383940055 James Ashton] and [
2 CONC https://www.geni.com/people/Deliverance-Ashton/6000000001383940047 Deliverance Throckmorton] in 1688 and died April 1732, as shown on the monument of Capt Nathan Stout. Rebecca was born 1672 in Providence, Rhode Island, the daught
2 CONC er of James Ashton and Deliverance Thockmorton and died after 1705 in New Jersey.
2 CONT
2 CONT They first settled on Hop River and about 1725 moved to Amwell Township: "David Stout...sold all his possessions in Middletown and moved to Amwell...where he purchased a large tract of land at which place he died a very old man an
2 CONC d was buried on his own farm, which laid the foundation of a burying ground where his descendants continue to bury to this day," reads "History of the Stout Family" by Nathan Stout, 1823. Today the graveyard is is called Stout-Man
2 CONC ners Cemetery located in Ringoes, Hunterdon County, NJ.  
2 CONT
2 CONT They were the parents of: 
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/people/James-Stout-Sr/6000000006436381814 James] (1694) m. [https://www.geni.com/people/Catherine-Stout/6000000003967441262 Catherine Simpson]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/people/Freegift-Stout-I/6000000002552602617 Freegift] (1693) m. [https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Stout/6000000006176080275 Mary Higgins], daughter of Jediah and Mary Newbold Higgins
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/people/David-Stout/6000000000196461818 David] (1695) m. [https://www.geni.com/people/Ann-Stout/6000000001384006483 Anne Merrill]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/people/Joseph-Stout/6000000024905069735 Joseph] (1698) m. [https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Stout/6000000006176080185 Mary Ashland] & [https://www.geni.com/people/Martha-Stout/6000000035218324733 Martha Ree
2 CONC der]
2 CONT # Benjamin m. Widow Ketcham 
2 CONT # Mary Higgins, daughter of Jediah and Hannah Stout Higgins
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/people/Rebecca-Manners/6000000006436527369 Rebecca] (1691) m. [https://www.geni.com/people/John-Manners/6000000001384006460 John Manners]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/people/Sarah-Stout/6000000082957160212 Sarah] never married
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/people/Deliverance-Labaw/6000000006436332734 Deliverance ](1701) m.[https://www.geni.com/people/Fran%C3%A7ois-Labaw/6000000001384006453 François La Bau]
2 CONT
2 CONT Of their descendants Caleb, son of James, and Abner and Job, sons of Joseph emigrated to Western Virginia.  After page forty-five of Russel lRay Stout's book there is a discussion of the Stout Coat of Arms and line graph's of all 
2 CONC of their descendants who left New Jersey and went west.
2 CONT
2 CONT Large monument reads:
2 CONT This yard was founded on the farm of David Stout son of Richard Stout and Penelope Van Princes and herein lies his body and that of his wife Rebecca Ashton of their son James and his wife Catherine Simson of their son John and of 
2 CONC his wife Rachel Merrill of their son Nathan to whom this monument is erected and of his wife Esther Ketcham of their son William and of his wife Eleanor Lane of their son Nathan and of his wife Mary Ann Fisher and of their son Sim
2 CONC pson.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/5816186/david-stout Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Nov 28 2022, 21:05:50 UTC''
2 CONT
