1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Disputed Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Brinson-10
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth Brinson, daughter of Daniel and Frances Greenland Brinson, and Barefoot, her brother, are named in her father's will, in which, his surname is spelled Brymson.[1] Nathan Stout[2] and John E Stilwell[3] name her birth name as 
2 CONC Ruth Greenland which, in fact, was her mother's maiden name and Jamie Riggle suggests she was the daughter of John Hornor, who was, in fact, her step-father[4]all of which are in error as documented in her father's will cited abov
2 CONC e. The following sources establish she was the granddaughter of Dr. Henry Greenland, father of Frances Greenland Brinson, and the step-daughter of John Hornor, her mother's second husband.[5][6] She was born in 1690 Bucks County, 
2 CONC Pennsylvania and died before August 10 1768 and married Col Joseph Stout August 10 1705. [7][8][9]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 COL. JOSEPH STOUT, son of Jonathan Stout, 9, was born Oct. 25, 1686, and died Oct. 22, 1766. He married Ruth, daughter of Dr. Henry Greenland. She was a constituent member of the Hopewell Church, in 1715, with her husband and h
2 CONC is family.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1722. Joseph Stout was on the Hopewell Tax Roll, and had twenty-eight cattle, eighteen sheep, two hundred and thirty acres of land, and was married.
2 CONT In 1 73 1, Joseph Stout was one of many defendants to popular land ejectment suits.
2 CONT 1749, Aug. 29. Jos. Stout, Esq., of Hopewell, N. J., gave a deed to John Stout, his son. Witnesses were David and Jonathan Stout.
2 CONT In 1753, Col. Joseph Stout was assessed in Hopewell.
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue
2 CONT # 19 John Stout
2 CONT # 20 Joseph Stout
2 CONT # 21 Col. Jonathan Stout
2 CONT # 22 James Stout
2 CONT # 23 Mary Stout; married Harmon Rosenkranz. She had issue: Alexander, Joseph, John, Catharine, Mary and Rachel.
2 CONT # 24 Ann Stout; married Mr. Worth, and had children.
2 CONT # 25 Ruth Stout; married Mr. Leonard, and had children.
2 CONT # 26 Rachel Stout; married Mr. Stockton, and had issue: Joseph and Richard Stockton. Upon the death of Mr. Stockton, Rachel Stout married Mr. Reddal, by whom she had a daughter, Ann.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *Historical and genealogical miscellany : data relating to the settlement and settlers of New York and New Jersey. by Stillwell, John Edwin, 1853-1930.  Page 332-333.  < [https://archive.org/details/historicalgeneal04stil/page/332
2 CONC /mode/2up Archive.Org] >
2 CONT This is my direct ancestor.  She has been documented through Colonial Dames of the 17th Century.  Several people have requested that she be linked to different parents.  I've added and then had to unlink her several times.  Becaus
2 CONC e of this, I have chosen to keep her linked to the parents that are listed in Colonial Dames records.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Col. Joseph Stout married Aug. 10, 1705 to Ruth Greenland,the daughter of Dr. Henry Greenland."  Sources:  Five Hundred First Families of America by DuBin, p. 23.
2 CONT The History of the Stout Family First Settling in Middletown, Monmouth Co., NJ, page 7. History of the Stout Family by Nathan Stout, printed in 1823, page page 7. The American Genealogist - Volume 32 - Page 34. Franklin and Susan 
2 CONC C. Strain, Kansas pioneers published 1999. Honoria Logan Lang Phillips: Her Descendants and Ancestors published 1996.A history of the Henry and Hackley families - Page 317 published 1975. The Harts of Randolph: or, Mostly descenda
2 CONC nts of Edward and Daniel by Katherine Frame published 1976. Historical and Genealogical Miscellany published 1970. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Ruth & Joseph:
2 CONT John Stout married Catherine Stout
2 CONT James Stout married Mary Ann St. Leger Codd
2 CONT Joseph Stout married Rebecca Grover
2 CONT Jonathan Stout married Elizabeth Hunt
2 CONT Mary Stout married Harmon Rosenkranz
2 CONT Anne Stout married William Worth
2 CONT Ruth Stout married ? Leonard
2 CONT Rachel Stout married Samuel Stockton and ? Reddal.
2 CONT Suggested edit: Her mother was Frances Greenland, daughter of Dr. Henry Greenland. She married (1) Daniel Brinson, Ruth's father, and (2) John Hornor III.
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT 1. S t r a y L e a v e s , A JAMES FAMILY IN AMERICA SINCE 1650 http://www.ericjames.org/html/fam/fam41713.htm
2 CONT 2. Somerset Historical Quarterly, A. Van Doren Honeyman, Ed., 1914, Vol III, "The Brunson (Brinson - Bryson) Family, William H Benedict, page 289 http://www.ericjames.org/html/fam/fam41713.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Both Stilwell and Nathan Stout give her maiden name as Greenland which in fact was her grandfather's name. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Here is what another person sent:
