1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Hannah Bonham===
2 CONT * Birth: 14 MAR 1694/95 in Piscataway, New Jersey
2 CONT * Death: 21 JAN 1770 in Hopewell, Hunterdon Co., New Jersey
2 CONT * Father: Hezekiah BONHAM 
2 CONT * Mother: Mary DUNN
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT # Benjamin STOUT b: 14 DEC 1691 in Middletown, Monmouth Co., New Jersey Married: ABT. 1713 in New Jersey
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT * Mary STOUT b: in Hunterdon Co., New Jersey
2 CONT * Hannah STOUT b: in Hunterdon Co., New Jersey
2 CONT *Sarah STOUT b: in Hunterdon Co., New Jersey
2 CONT * Jonathan STOUT b: 14 JAN 1714/15 in Hopewell, Hunterdon Co., New Jersey
2 CONT * Ezekiel STOUT b: ABT. 1720 in Hopewell, Hunterdon Co., New Jersey
2 CONT * Hezekiah STOUT b: 1723 in Hunterdon Co., New Jersey
2 CONT * Benjamin STOUT b: 1725 in Hopewell, Hunterdon Co., New Jersey
2 CONT * Nathaniel STOUT b: 1731
2 CONT * Hosea STOUT b: AFT. 1731 in Hunterdon Co., New Jersey
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT “The History of the Stout Family: First Settling in Middletown, Monmouth County, New Jersey”  By Nathan Stout, 1823  Second printing by H.G. McCarter, "Herald" Office, Hopewell, N.J., 1878  with additions by Mrs. Sarah Weart,  Thi
2 CONC rd printing in 1906 by Joab B. Stout, with additions and corrections. Fourth printing in 1929 by George A. Chandler, Bethlehem, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://files.usgwarchives.net/nj/monmouth/history/family/stout01.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT I shall now introduce Benjamin, a brother of Zebulon, whose family I have last delineated.  Benjamin was born in the year 1696, and married Hannah Bonham by whom he had six sons and three daughters, viz: Jonathan, Hezekiah, Benjam
2 CONC in, Nathaniel, Ezekiel, Hosea and Mary, Hannah and Sarah.  Jonathan married a woman by the name of Jewell, and raised a large family of children and lived till he was a hundred years old.  Hezekiah married a widow Smith, they had 
2 CONC no children, and after her death he married a widow Sortor, with whom he lived until he was between ninety and a hundred years old, and died without issue.  Benjamin married Rebecca Dulhangal, by whom he had a large family of chil
2 CONC dren, and after her death he married Martha Skyhauk and had another large family of children.  Nathaniel married Charity Furman, by whom he had one child, a daughter, whose name was Rhoda.  She married Zephaniah Stout, and had iss
2 CONC ue.  After his death she married Burges Allison, by whom she had children.  Ezekiel married a Drake by whom he had a large family of children.  Hesea went into the back parts of Virginia a single man, where he married and raised a
2 CONC  large family of children, as I have been informed.  Mary married William Heabron, and had by him two sons and one daughter, viz; John, William and Hannah.  Hannah married David Ollivent, and raised a family of children.  Sarah ma
2 CONC rried Andrew Bray and died without issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * Reference: [http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=ronaldwebb&id=I05445 RootsWeb's WorldConnect] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 10 2016, 0:12:29 UTC''
2 CONT *https://www.anamericanfamilyhistory.com/Bonham%20Family/BonhamHannahStout.html
2 CONT *Historical and genealogical miscellany, John E Stilwell, 1916, Vol IV, page 333 [http://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal04stil#page/333/mode/1up Archive.Org].
2 CONT * “The Bonham family”.  By Samuel Jeremiah Bonham.  Page 27.  “Children of Hezekiah.”  [https://books.google.com/books?id=FdM1AAAAMAAJ&vq=Stout&pg=PA27#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LJ1B-KLD FamilySearch Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 3 2021, 3:43:59 UTC''
2 CONT  ==============================
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Bonham Stout was born on March 14, 1694/95 at Piscataway, Middlesex County, New Jersey. She was the daughter of Hezekiah Bonham and his first wife Mary Dunn.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Benjamin Stout when she was about 18 years old. Benjamin was born December 14, 1691 in Middletown, Monmouth County, New Jersey. He was the son of Jonathan Stout (Richard) and Anne Bullen (Bollen). His sister, Ann Stout
2 CONC , married Hannah’s half-brother Nehemiah Bonham.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Stout family was instrumental in organizing the Hopewell Baptist Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT After many years of meeting in homes and having problems securing a place to meet, it was decided to build a meeting house. Twenty members were baptized from 1715 to 1728 and by 1747 there were 65 members. A meeting was called on 
2 CONC June 19, 1747, held at the home of Henry Oxley in Hopewell (then known as Columbia) at which time David Stout, Benjamin Stout, and Henry Oxley were chosen managers to build a meeting house. (from the History of Hopewell Baptist Ch
2 CONC urch)
2 CONT
2 CONT They had six sons and three daughters who were all born in Hopewell:
2 CONT Jonathan Stout (about 1715, married Hannah Jewell),
2 CONT Ezekiel Stout (about 1721, married Miss Drake),
2 CONT Mary Stout (about 1723, married William Heabron),
2 CONT Hezekiah Stout (about 1723, married Mrs. Smith and Mrs. Sorter),
2 CONT Hosea Stout (about 1727),
2 CONT Hannah Stout (about 1727, married David Oliphant),
2 CONT Nathaniel Stout (about 1731, married Charity Furman),
2 CONT Sarah Stout Bray (about 1733, married Andrew Bray) and
2 CONT Benjamin Stout (married Rebecca Dolhagen and Martha Shenk).
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah died when she was 74 on January 21, 1770 and Benjamin died February 8, 1772. They both died in Hopewell, New Jersey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Stout, son of Jonathan Stout was born Dec. 14, 1691; married Hannah Bonham.
2 CONT
2 CONT There was a Benjamin Stout, Sr., on the Assessment Roll, of Hopewell, in 1753, and a Benjamin Stout, Jr., who may have been his son.
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue
2 CONT 28 Jonathan Stout; married Miss Jewell; lived one hundred years, and had a large family.
2 CONT 29 Hezekiah Stout; married, first. Widow Smith; second. Widow Sorter; lived nearly one hundred years. No issue.
2 CONT 30 Benjamin Stout; married, first, Rebecca Dillhangel; second, Sept. 17, 1772, license, Martha Schihok [Skyhawk]. He had large families by both wives.
2 CONT 31 Nathaniel Stout; married Charity Furman; had a daughter, Rhoda Stout, who married, first, Zephaniah Stout; second, Burges Allison, and had issue by both husbands.
2 CONT 33 Ezekiel Stout; married Miss Drake; had many children.
2 CONT 34 Hosea Stout; married in Virginia; had many children.
2 CONT 35 Mary Stout; married William Heabron; had issue.
2 CONT 36 Hannah Stout; married David Ollivant.
2 CONT 37 Sarah Stout; married Andrew Bray.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Bonhams are Mayflower descendants: Samuel Fuller, Hannah Fuller Bonham, Hezekiah Bonham, Amariah Bonham. 
2 CONT
