2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Bonham and Benjamin Stout  had six sons and three daughters who were all born in Hopewell: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Stout (about 1727, married David Oliphant).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT David Oliphant  (1713- 1774) was the eldest son of Duncan Oliphant (1682-1734), a pioneer settler of Staten Isl., NY, and one of the founders of Hunterdon Co., NJ. David first married Ann Lee in c1735 and had four children: Hosea;
2 CONC  John; Jerusha; and Jonathan. Later, he married Hannah Stout around 1740.  “I have land record for David and Ann Oliphant 1741-1746, so Hannah could not have been the mother.”
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/86224420/david-oliphant
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From The History of the Stout Family, First Settling in Middletown, Monmouth County, New Jersey By Nathan Stout, 1823   Second printing by H.G. McCarter, "Herald" Office, Hopewell, N.J., 1878  with additions by Mrs. Sarah Weart,  
2 CONC Third printing in 1906 by Joab B. Stout, with additions and corrections.  Fourth printing in 1929 by George A. Chandler, Bethlehem, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://files.usgwarchives.net/nj/monmouth/history/family/stout01.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT “I shall now introduce Benjamin, a brother of Zebulon, whose family I have last delineated.  Benjamin was born in the year 1696, and married Hannah Bonham by whom he had six sons and three daughters, viz: Jonathan, Hezekiah, Benja
2 CONC min, Nathaniel, Ezekiel, Hosea and Mary, Hannah and Sarah. ... Hannah married David Ollivent, and raised a family of children.”
