1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/8008361/mary-stout '''Mary ''Higgins'' Stout- Find A Grave'''] - Memorial ID: 8008361
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Higgins (1718-1789) who is the wife of Benjamin Stout (1707-1789).
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:<br/>
2 CONT Jediah Higgins 1691-1772 and Hannah Stout 1694-1779 (her parents were Jonathan Stout and Anna Throckmorton Bollen)
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse:<br/>
2 CONT   Benjamin Stout 1707-1789 buried in Hopewell 'Old School Baptist' churchyard - Revolutionary War
2 CONT
2 CONT Nine Children: <br/>
2 CONT First three died young of Dysentery - Elihu 1752-1762, Hannah 1754-1766, Rebecca 1755-1767<br/>
2 CONT Jediah 1757-1837 (married his cousin Mary Stout 1862-1842) migrated to Fayette Co, KY. She was the daughter of Abraham and Elizabeth Houghton Stout - my 5th Great Grandparents. Abraham in Revolutionary War- he was wounded and his 
2 CONC oldest son Solomon was killed at the Battle of White Plains.<br/>
2 CONT Rachel 1760-1820 (married Paul Hill 1751-1824) buried Hopewell 'Old School Baptist' Hunterdon (Mercer) Co. Benjamin Higgins 1762-1822 (married Rachel Stout 1764-1795 sister of btother Jediah's wife Mary (daughters of Abraham and E
2 CONC lizabeth Houghton)<br/>
2 CONT Sarah 1764-1806 (1st wife of Elijah 'RW' Stout 1761-1838 Son of James Stout and Mary Mattison buried Pleasant Ridge Cemetery, NJ.) James was the son of Freegift 1693-1766 and Mary Higgins 1699-1773 (We don't know what her relation
2 CONC ship was to the above Mary Higgins - she was born in Mass.) Freegift and this Mary are buried in Stout-Manners Cemetery, Ringoes, Hunterdon. Freegift was the son of David and Rebecca Ashton Stout also buried in Stout-Manners. Note
2 CONC : my 7th Great Grandparents.<br/>
2 CONT Anne 1766-1842 - (2nd wife of Elijah 'RW' Stout-sister to the above Sarah)- migrated to KY and buried there<br/>
2 CONT David 1769-1806 - 1st wife Lydia Manners 1734-1755 - 2nd wife Elizabeth Stout 1767-1844 - she was the daughter of James Turler 1732-1810 son of Capt. David and Elizabeth Larrison Stout and Catherine Stout daughter of John Stout an
2 CONC d Rachell Merrill. They are buried in Stout-Manners Cemetery.<br/>
2 CONT Note: John and Rachel Merrill Stout are my 6th Great Grandparents.<br/>
2 CONT Three of their sons served in the Revolutionary War - Abraham, Nathan and Moses and so did many of the other Stout men.
2 CONT
2 CONT The reason at least two of Benjamin's sons migrated to Ky was that he had land there, according to land records and a will. Possibly 'Bounty Land' given to Veterans of the Rev. War and War of 1812 in order to populate the Western 
2 CONC lands.
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: [https://www.findagrave.com/user/profile/46580804 Richard Arthur Norton] (1958- )<br/>
2 CONT Added: 21 Oct 2003<br/>
2 CONT Find A Grave Memorial 8008361<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/8008361/mary-stout
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {{New Netherland Descendant}}
2 CONT {{DateGuess}} [[Category: Monmouth County, New Jersey]]
2 CONT == Biography ==Benjamin Stout's second wife was Mary Higgins, daughter of Jediah Higgins and Hannah Stout<ref>''Historical and genealogical miscellany'', John E Stillwell, 1918, Vol IV, page 334 http://archive.org/stream/historica
2 CONC lgeneal04stil#page/334/mode/1up/search/mary+higgins </ref> 
2 CONT *1. Elihu 1752-1762, 
2 CONT *2. Hannah 1754-1762, *3. Rebecca 1755-1762 all died under twelve years old with dysentery. and . *4. Jediah 1757-1820 
2 CONT *5. John 1758-1758
2 CONT *6. Mary Stout (Twin) 1760-1844 m Garrison Prall, *7. Rachel (Twin) 1760-1820 m Paul Hill, Benjamin Higgins 1762-1822 m Rachel Stout, 
2 CONT *8. Sarah 1764-1806 1st wife of Elijah Stout, son of James Stout *9. Anne 1767-1842  2nd Wife of Elijah Stout, son of James Stout and mentioned in David, her brother's will*10. David 1769-1806 m Elizabeth Stout. <ref>''Richard Hig
2 CONC gins'', Mrs.Katherine Chapin Higgins, 1908, page 91 https://books.google.com/books?id=jONUAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA59&lpg</ref> <ref>"History of the Stout Family"Nathan Stout, 1823, page 27 http://files.usgwarchives.net/nj/monmouth/history/f
2 CONC amily/stout01.txt </ref> <ref>John E Stillwell, 1918, Vol IV, page 349-350 http://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal04stil#page/349/mode/1up/search/mary+higgins</ref> <ref>[http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=ST
2 CONC O&GSpartial=1&GSbyrel=all&GSst=33&GScntry=4&GSsr=4281&GRid=53763755&&ftm=1Findagrave link]</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Birth===1718 in New Jersey<ref>[http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=8008361 Findagrave]</ref>
2 CONT ===Marriage===to Benjamin Stout in 1751<ref>Yates Publishing, U.S. and InternationalMarriage Records, 1560-1900 (Provo, UT, USA, Ancestry.com Operations Inc, 2004), Ancestry.com, Source number: 1280.000; Source type: Electronic Da
2 CONC tabase; Number of Pages: 1; Submitter Code: MZS. Record for Benjamin Stout. http://search.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/sse.dll?db=WorldMarr_ga&h=1172849&indiv=try</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===1789 <ref>[http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=STO&GSpartial=1&GSbyrel=all&GSst=33&GScntry=4&GSsr=4281&GRid=53763755&&ftm=1Findagrave link]</ref>
