1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category: Hopewell, New Jersey]]
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT Charity Stout, daughter of Zebulon and Charity Burroughs (Burrows), was born in Hopewell, Hunterdon County, NJ and died before 1764.  She married Nathaniel Stout, son of David and Anne Merrill Stout. <ref>Stillwell, John E. ''Hist
2 CONC orical and genealogy miscellany.'' New York:1916 page 334, 353 http://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal04stil#page/334/mode/1up/search/ann+merrill</ref> The children are named in both Nathan Stout's work and Nathaniel's will alo
2 CONC ng with their half-siblings.<ref>''History of the Stout Family'', Nathan Stout, 1823, page 9 http://files.usgwarchives.net/nj/monmouth/history/family/stout01.txt</ref><ref>Hutchinson, Elmer T. ''Documents relating to the Colonial,
2 CONC  Revolutionary an Post-Revolutonary History of the State of New Jersey.'' New Jersey Journal Printers. Newark, J. J. 1944 page 352 https://dcms.lds.org/delivery/DeliveryManagerServlet?dps_pid=IE106701</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT They had three children:
2 CONT #Anna (Lavana/Lavinia)
2 CONT #David#Charity<ref>Stout, Nathan. 1823 page 9 http://files.usgwarchives.net/nj/monmouth/history/family/stout01.txt</ref> Children of Nathaniel Stout Sr married (2) Sarah Skillman Stout, Charity's sister and had: 
2 CONT #Zebulon
2 CONT #Nathaniel Jr
2 CONT #Elijah
2 CONT #Rebecca.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
