1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Mary Leigh
2 CONT * Born 1701 in Hopewell, Hunterdon, New Jersey
2 CONT * Died 1776 in Hopewell, Hunterdon, New Jersey
2 CONT * Wife of Jonathan Stout  (1700-1768) (Son of Jonathan Stout and Anne (Bollen) 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Jonathan Stout, son of Jonathan and Anne Bollen Stout, born in 1701 and died in 1768 married Mary Leigh (Lee).
2 CONT
2 CONT Known children Jonathan and Mary Leigh Stout: 
2 CONT >“had four sons and two daughters, viz: Zebulon, Samuel, Jonathan, David m (1) Sarah Parke and moved to Kentucky, (2) Jerusha Smith widow of David Larison and Nathan Drake [1] [2] Anne (Anna) m (1) Moses Morgan (2) Andrew Smith an
2 CONC d Sarah m Andrew Smith[3] [4] [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Leigh-72
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan Stout, son of Jonathan and Anne Bollen Stout, born 1701 and died 1768 married Mary Leigh. They were the parents of:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Zebulon never married
2 CONT # Samuel
2 CONT # Jonathan married a Sywn
2 CONT # Sarah married (1) Moses Morgan (2) Andrew Stout, Anne, her sister's widower, June 22 1777.[1]
2 CONT # David married (1) Sarah Parke, moved to Kentucky, (2) Jerusha Smith, daughter of Ethan Smith, (1) widow of David Larrison, son of James Larrison and (2) widow of Nathan Drake.
2 CONT # Anne d before June 22 1777, m Andrew Stout, son of David and Elizabeth Larrison.[2][3][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Note
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathan Stout and John Stilwell spell Mary's last name Lee and Ralph Ege spells it as Leigh.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources 
2 CONT *Pioneers of Old Hopewell, Ralph Ege, 1908, page 218, 235-236 https://archive.org/stream/pioneersoldhope00egegoog#page/n227/mode/1up/search/sarah+parke 
