2 CONT 1758-Elijah Crafford was born 22 June 1758 in
2 CONT Northampton County, PA to John and Rebecca Crafford, residents of that County in Mt. Bethel Twp.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1756/8 Elijah's birth date; 'First Settlers' of Smith Township, Washington County, PA, Page714, book by Mrs.Rachel Bell. Birth date different [22 Jun 1758]in this article; alternate birth 25 Apr 1756 [year from headstone; date fro
2 CONC m DAR record]; born at Lower Mt Bethel Twp, Northampton Co, PA to Johnand Rebecca Crafford;
2 CONT
2 CONT 1776- Elijah in the war from Easton, Northampton County, Pennsylvania in June 1776 fought in the ill-fated Battle for Long Island and may have been discharged as early as December the same year. 
2 CONT In the book by Francis S. Fox, titled: “Sweet Land of Liberty, The Ordeal of the American Revolution in Northampton County, Pennsylvania” the description of the many events where upon individuals were called upon to serve in vario
2 CONC us ways. The only military service record that exists for Elijah is one card of Company Payroll to Elijah in Capt.Arndt’s Company of Baxter’s Battalion.
2 CONT
2 CONT “Soldiers of the American Revolution, Northampton Co, PA, including Lehigh Co”; transcribed from the Pennsylvania Archives; alphabetically arranged by Williams, Danboro, PA 1979; [S=Series; V=Volume]:
2 CONT Elijah Crawford, Corporal in Arndt's Co; S2-V14-pages 573-634; S5, V8, Pg21; 1781, fined S3-V6-page 767; 1782 Private 4th Class, 2nd Co, 2ndBattalion, S5-V8- page 212;
2 CONT
2 CONT Elijah filed for invalid pension in 1832.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elijah Crafford was a patriot of the Revolutionary war.
2 CONT Elijah enlisted in the war from Easton, Northampton County, Pennsylvania in June 1776, fought in the ill-fated Battle for Long Island and may have been discharged as early as December the same year.
2 CONT
2 CONT In his pension application statement made to the Court of Common Pleas of Washington County, Pennsylvania in October of 1832, Elijah states his service in the Battle of Long Island, a battle where it is reported many losses by dea
2 CONC th and where John Arndt was wounded.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Pennsylvania Archives it shows he served on inactive duty in the local militia, card dated 20 April 1782; records of “Military Accounts: Militia. Records of the Comptroller General, RG-4”. Published in the Archives Series 5, Vo
2 CONC lume VIII, Pages 176-8.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1777- Oaths of Allegiance, from “An Alphabetized Listing of Those Subscribers to the Oaths of Allegiance, Northampton County, PA, 1777-1784”, prepared by Gaylord Griffiths, Page 12: Elijah Crafford #47, Jul 23, 1777, Justice of th
2 CONC e Peace SR; Page 12;
2 CONT and following his entry is his brother John Jr, #21 dated July 1, 1777
2 CONT and his father John Sr, # 41, dated Jul 9, 1777 all by same JP and page number;
2 CONT
2 CONT Elijah took his Oath of Allegiance at about the same time as his father and brother, John in July 1777 in Northampton County. In Davis’s 1877book “History of Northampton County, Pennsylvania” in Chapter XLIX, Local History, Townsh
2 CONC ips of Upper & Lower Mount Bethel and Hanover, record the names of some 16 early settler surnames including Crawford who settled the area shortly after 1730.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1777– Miscellaneous Public Records- Elijah was assaulted by John Carey, late of the county, yeoman, on 1 Dec 1777 at Easton; Grand Inquest was held, Mar 1778 session by Jona D Sergeant; Elijah was witness in his own defense. Sourc
2 CONC e: Section 4, Miscellaneous Public Records 1767-1779, Page 205.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1778- Elijah’s parents died in November 1778; he was named Executor of both their wills.
2 CONT
2 CONT LASTWILL & TESTAMENT
2 CONT John Crafford [File #817]
2 CONT Dated2 May 1778
2 CONT Proved15 May 1778
2 CONT
2 CONT In the name of God Amen! The second day of May in the year of our Lord1778, I John Crafford of Pennsylvania in the County of Northampton,Weaver, being very sick and weak in body, but of perfect mind and memory thanks be given unto
2 CONC  God therefore calling unto mind the Mortality of my Body and knowing that it is appointed for all men once to die do make and ordain this my Last Will and Testament! That is to say principally and first of all, I give and recomme
2 CONC nd my soul unto the hands of God that gave it and for my body I recomand it to the earth to be buried in a Christian like and decent manner, at the discretion of my Executors nothing doubting but at the General Resurrection I shal
2 CONC l receive the same again by the Mighty Power of God and as touching such worldly estate where with it hath pleased God to bless me in this life I give devise dispose of the same in the following manner and form, and I do apoind El
2 CONC ijah Crafford my son and Robert Moody to be my Executors Imprimis it is my will and I do order that in the first place all my just Debts and funeral Charges be paid and satisfied, Item I give and bequeath to Rebecca my beloved wif
2 CONC e one third of all my estate both real and personal and her choice of the Riding Creator and her saddal, Item I give and bequeath to my Grand Son Isaac Crafford Son of my oldest Son George the sum of five Pounds to be paid to him 
2 CONC when he comes to the age of twenty one, Item I give to my beloved children Martha Susanah Abigal John and Edmund Each of them one third paid as as much as one of my other children ~ Item I give to my other four children Elijah Reb
2 CONC ecca Mary and Rachel is to have all the remainder of my estate and I do hereby utterly disallow revoke and disonul all and every other former Testaments Wills Legacis and Executors by me in any way,before this time named Willed an
2 CONC d Bequeathed Rectifying and Confirming this and no other to be my Last Will and Testament in witness whare of I hear unto set my Hand and and Seal the day and year above written
2 CONT Signed Seled Published Pronounced and declared by the said John Crafford as his Last Will and Testament in the presents of us the Subscribers Vis
2 CONT Anthony Moore, John Ihrie, Thomas Moore
2 CONT His X Mark John Crafford (Seal)
2 CONT
2 CONT Northampton County ~SS~ On the 15th day of May 1778 before me John Arnett Esqr Regr for the probate of wills ***in and for said County personally appeared Anthony Moore John Ihrie and Thomas Moore the witnesses to the foregoing La
2 CONC st Will &Testament of John Crafford Deceased and being duly sworn on the Holy Evangelists of Almighty God did depose and say that they were present and *****[Taped fold blackened writing] *** and that the doing thereof he the said
2 CONC  Testator was of sound mind Memory and understanding to the best of their knowledge and Belief and that the Contents of the will was properly read and some interlinements made before him the said Testator and also that they these 
2 CONC deponents subscribed their names Thereto as witnesses in the presence and at the request of the Said Testator and in the presence of one another.John Arnett Regr
2 CONT
