2 CONC s be given unto God therefore calling unto mind the mortality of my body, and knowing that it is apointed for once all to die, do make and ordain this my Last Will and Testament; that it is to say principally and first of all, I g
2 CONC ive and Recommand my Soul unto the hands of God that gave it and for my body I recommend it to the earth to be buried in a Chrisitan like and decent maner at the discretion of my Executors ’Nothing Doubting but at the General Resu
2 CONC rrection I shall receive thesame by the mighty Power of God and as touching such worldly Estate whare with it hath pleased God to bless me in this life, I give devise dispose of the same in the following maner and form, and Ido ap
2 CONC point Elijah Crafford my son and Robert Moody to be my executors Imprimis it is my will and I do order that in the first place that all my funeral Charge be paid and satisfied Item I do give and bequeath to my well beloved son Eli
2 CONC jah Crafford my Bay Mare and one equal fouth part of my Estate.
2 CONT Item I do give and bequeath to my other three children Viz: Rebecca Mary and Rachel all the remainder of my Estate except five Pound which I do give and bequeath to my grand Son Son John Clark to be paid to himwhan he coms to the 
