2 CONT 1778- Elijah married Mary Elizabeth ‘Polly’ Stout, 1 May 1778 in Northampton Co, PA. Reference Source: Pennsylvania Archives, Series2, Vol II, Page 70, “Marriage Licenses Were Issued in the Province of Pennsylvania, last entry on 
2 CONC page 70: 1778, May 1Crawford, Elijah,and Elizabeth Stout. Alternate date given: 22 Jun 1778 in "Commemorative Biographical Record of Washington County, Pennsylvania, containing..." . J.H.Beers &Co., 1893, Chicago., page 714 under 
2 CONC a write up for Mrs Rachel Bell,daughter of Free Gift Crawford, grand daughter of Elijah. “Pennsylvania Marriages Prior to 1790”, [p.237] dated 1778, May1. Stout, Elizabeth, and Elijah Crawford. Marriage license issued by Lewis Gor
2 CONC don, Esq. of Northampton Co, PA;
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Elizabeth 'Polly' Stout (1755/60-1837) was daughter of Freegift Stout II (1724-1798) and Elizabeth Stout (1730/32- ????).
2 CONT There was Freegift Stout (1693-1760) father of Freegift II, and Freegift Stout III, son of Freegift II;
2 CONT NOTE:There was a different Freegift Stout on the expedition with Zebulon Pike under orders to find the headwaters of the Mississippi River. He was an enlisted military man, not the father of Polly but possibly a brother or nephew,
2 CONC  and was with Zebulon Pike when they arrived at‘Pikes Peak’, now in Colorado. The story of the headwaters expedition is an interesting history to read.
2 CONT Elijah and Polly named one son Freegift Crawford.
2 CONT
