2 CONT 1801/09- Elijah removed his family to Washington County and was a ‘First Settler’ in Smith Township. He purchased land in Washington County as early as 1805, as in his will he references land purchased at this date. Elijah and his
2 CONC  brother John appear in the Northampton County census for 1790, Elijah in 1800 and 1810. Elijah appears in Washington County for 1820, but not in 1830 which would have been before his death in 1833. I suspect he is living with son
2 CONC  Isaac by this time as the age group is represented in columns for both he and Elizabeth, his wife. Some information for Elijah and family is included in the the History of Washington County, by Beers
2 CONT
2 CONT 1801-Elijah purchased property of William Reid in May 1801, of Andrew Carlisle in May 1805, from Thomas Holmes at another date not noted in his will. It wasn’t until 1811 that Elijah removed to Washington County. I believe his son
2 CONC  Isaac removed here first and possibly other family members. Again, the crossover in the names and spelling of the same make sorting them difficult. More study of land records could provide clarification on this.
2 CONT
