2 CONT TheLast Will & Testament of Elijah Crafford yeoman of WashingtonCounty Pennsylvania, witnesseth That I dispose of my estate real andpersonal in the following manner viz
2 CONT Item1 I give and bequeath to my wife Elizabeth one case of drawers onebed and bedding one horse and one cow her choice of my stock hersaddle and bridle one spinning wheel and as much of my kitchenfurniture as she may choose all in
2 CONC  perpetuity together with acomfortable maintenance from my two sons Joseph and Isaac ashereinafter directed and full possession of the best room in my homeon the place where I live during her natural life.
2 CONT 2nI give and bequeath to my son Joseph Crafford that tract of land Ipurchased from Andrew Carlisle by indenture bearing the date the 14thday of May 1805 upon condition that my said son Joseph pay me [my]executors three hundred dol
2 CONC lars in four equal annual paymentscommencing one year after my decease and likewise pay my wifeElizabeth one third of the yearly value of said farm during hernatural life if she requires it.
2 CONT 3rdIn as much as I have given my son Free Crafford six hundred and fiftydollars in payment of that tract of land he bought of Thomas Holmes Igive and bequeath to my said Son Free the above mentioned money withthe interest together
2 CONC  with one hundred dollars to be paid in twoequal annual payments commencing one year after my decease
2 CONT 4thI give and bequeath to my Son Isaac Crafford that tract of land Ipurchased from Wm Reid by Indenture dated the 25th day of May 1801upon condition that my said son Isaac pay my executors three hundreddollars in four equal annual
2 CONC  payments commencing one year after mydecease and likewise pay my wife Elizabeth one third of the yearlyvalue of said farm during her natural life if she requires it [andfurther] I give to my said son Isaac my cupboard after the d
2 CONC eath ofhis mother but she is to have the use of it while she lives.
2 CONT 5thI give and bequeath to the children of my daughter Elizabeth Jacksonone hundred and fifty dollars to be divided among said children shareand share alike.
2 CONT 6thI give and bequeath to my daughter Rebecca Thompson one hundred andfifty dollars to be paid in three equal annual installmentscommencing one year after my decease
2 CONT Igive and bequeath to my daughter Ann Boils fifty dollars to be paidone year after my decease
2 CONT 8thI give and bequeath to my grandson Crafford Miller fifty dollars tobe paid two years after my decease and also one share of my turnpikestock.
2 CONT 9thI give and bequeath to my granddaughter Rachel Miller fifty dollarsto be paid two years after my decease, but if either of [the]grandchildren should die in their minority and without issue thentheir brothers and sisters shall i
2 CONC nherit their share
2 CONT 10thI give and bequeath to Elijah Crafford son of Isaac Crafford my riflegun and one share of my turnpike stock
2 CONT 11thI give and bequeath to Isaac Crafford son of Isaac Crafford my silverwatch.
2 CONT 12thI give and bequeath the remaining six shares of my turnpike stock tothe following persons viz one share to Elijah Crafford son of JosephCrafford, one share to my grandson Elijah Jackson one share to mygrandson Elijah Crafford 
2 CONC son of Free Crafford one share to mygrandson Elijah Thompson one share to my granddaughter ElizabethCrafford daughter of Isaac Crafford and one share to Robert Craffordson of Isaac Crafford
2 CONT 13thI give and bequeath to my three sons Joseph Free and Isaac my wearingapparel to be divided by them share and share alike.
2 CONT 14thall my property not heretofore disposed to be sold at the discretionof my executors and after the payment of the above legacies my justdebts and funeral expenses the remainder I bequeath to my twodaughters Rebecca and Anne and
2 CONC  the heirs of my daughter Elizabetheach of my said daughters to have one third and the heirs of mydaughter Elizabeth to have the other third of said remainder
2 CONT LastlyI do hereby appoint my two sons Joseph & Isaac Crafford Executorsof this my last will and testament. In witness whereof I havehereunto set my hand and seal the twenty ninth day of March A.D.1829.
2 CONT
2 CONT ElijahCrafford (L.S.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnesspresent Jas. McFarren, M. B. Buchanan, [and] William Livingston
2 CONT WashingtonCounty SS
2 CONT Beit remembered on the 12th day of February A. D. 1836 before me SamuelCunningham, register for the probate of Wills and granting letters ofAdministration in and for said County came James McFarren and WilliamLivingston two fo the
2 CONC  subscribing witnesses to the above and withinlast will and testament of Elijah Crafford deceased who being dulysworn as the law directs doth depose and say that they werepersonally present and did see the testator within named si
2 CONC gn thiswill, and did hear him publish pronounce and declare the same as andfor his last will and testament that at the time of his so doing hewas of sound and disposing mind memory and understanding to the bestof their knowledge o
2 CONC bservation and belief and that they signed thiswill as witnesses at the request of the testator and in his presenceand in the presence of each other and in the presence of M. B.Buchanan a subscribing witness thereto
2 CONT Andsworn to and subscribed Jas McFarren Wm Livingston
2 CONT Beforeme Saml. Cunningham, Register
2 CONT February12th 1836. Letters Testamentary with copy of the will and probateannexed issued to Joseph Crafford and Isaac Crafford the Executorswithin named who on the same day were duly sworn
2 CONT Saml.Cunningham, Register
2 CONT Registeredand compared with the original February 12th 1836
2 CONT Saml.Cunningham, Register
2 CONT
2 CONT 1836-“Abstracts of Washington Co, PA Will Book #5 (1832-1841)”, page442:
2 CONT ElijahCrafford, Yeoman, page 242, dated 29 Mar 1829, probated 12 Feb 1836,Executors: Sons Joseph & Isaac, Witnesses Jas McFarren, M BBuchanan & Wm Levingston; Beneficiaries: Wife Elizabeth, Sons:Joseph, Isaac, Free, Daughters: Reb
2 CONC ecca Thompson, Ann Boils,Elizabeth Jackson; Grandchildren: Crafford & Rachel Miller,Elijah Thompson, Elijah Jackson; Elizabeth Crafford, Elijah Craffordson of Joseph Crafford, Elijah Crafford son of Free Crafford; Robert,Isaac and
2 CONC  Elijah Crafford, sons of Isaac Crafford;
2 CONT
2 CONT 1836- Revolutionary War Burials, Washington, PA
2 CONT Headstonereads "Elijah H. Crafford, Revolutionary War", with dates.No other reference to middle initial "H" has been found.
2 CONT Burial:Florence (Cross Roads) Presbyterian Church Cemetery (Kings Creek)
2 CONT Locationon Rt 22 in Florence, Hanover Twp, Washington Co, PA
2 CONT Publishedin "Miscellaneous Cemeteries, Washington Co, PA" Vol 1,1939
2 CONT MoreInformation, An enumeration of tombstones and transcriptions ofvarious church records are contained in the booklet titled "Florence(Cross Roads) Presbyterian Church (Originally Kings Creek),Washington Co., PA" by Robert C. and
2 CONC  Agnes D. Kreutzberg, pub.1986.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1836-“History of Washington County Pennsylvania”, by Earle R Forrest,Vol I, Pub S J Clarke Pub Co, Chicago, 1926; page1137, “ElijahCrafford, of Hanover Township died February 4, 1836 aged eighty years”
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT WILLOF ELIZABETH CRAFFORD
2 CONT Dated8 April 1836
2 CONT Probated:11 Jan 1837
2 CONT SmithTwp, Washington Co, PA
2 CONT WillBook 5 Pages 308-309
2 CONT
2 CONT Thelast will and testament of Elisabeth Crafford of Hanover TownshipWashington County
2 CONT Witnesseththat I dispose of my worldly good[s] and Chattles in the followingmanner viz I give and bequeath to my son Isaac Crafford my cow mychest my large kettle my armed chair my bake-iron and I also directthat a note I hold upo
2 CONC n my said son Isaac shall be given up to himwithout payment
2 CONT Igive and bequeath to my grand-daughter July Ann Crafford my coppertea kittle my bedstead and stand of curtains
2 CONT Igive and bequeath to my grand-daughter Elizabeth Huffman my silvertea spoons
2 CONT Igive and bequeath to my grand-son Isaac Crafford my linen table Cloth
2 CONT Igive and bequeath to my grand-son Robert Crafford my table and smalltrunk
2 CONT Idirect my cupboard furniture consisting of China Glass delf [Delft] &queens-ware to be divided equally between my son Isaac Crafford’sfour children viz Elijah Crafford, Isaac Crafford, Robert Craffordand July Ann Crafford
2 CONT Igive and bequeath to my two daughters Rebecca Thompson and Ann Boylesmy bed and bedding my wearing apparel including all my bed clothesTable linen towels & to be divided between them share and sharealike.
2 CONT Igive and bequeath to my grand-daughter Ruth Crafford my lookingglass.
2 CONT LastlyI direct all my property not heretofore disposed of to be sold at thediscretion of my executor and after the payment of my funeralexpenses I direct the remainder to be equally divided between my twodaughters Rebecca Thompson
2 CONC  and Ann Boyles.
2 CONT Ihereby appoint my son Isaac Crafford executor of this my last willand testament. In testimony whereof I have hereunto set my hand andseal April 8, 1836.
2 CONT Inpresence of Ja. McFarren John Horner
2 CONT Elisabeth(herXmark) Crafford
2 CONT
2 CONT WashingtonCounty SS.
2 CONT Beit remembered on this 11th day of January A.D. 1837 before me Sam’lCunningham Register for the Probate of Wills and greeting letters ofAdministration in and for said County cause James McFarren Esq andJohn Horner the subscribing
2 CONC  witnesses to the within Last Will andTestament Of Elisabeth Crafford dec’d who being duly sworn as thelaw directs doth depose and say that they were personally present anddid see the Testatrix herein named make her mark to the wi
2 CONC thin willand did hear her publish and pronounce and declare the same as andfor her last will and Testament & that at the time she did so shewas of sound and disposing mind memory and understanding to the bestof their Knowledge obs
2 CONC ervation and belief
2 CONT JasMcFarren
2 CONT JohnHorner
2 CONT Andsworn to and subscribed before me
2 CONT Sam’lCunningham Register
2 CONT
2 CONT January11 – 1837 Letter Testamentary with copy of the will and probateentered issued to Isaac Crafford within named who on same day wasduly sworn
2 CONT Sam’lCunningham Register
