2 CONT OLDFLORENCE GRAVEYARD
2 CONT Elijah and his wife Elizabeth are buried at Old Florence Church Cemetery;Washington Co, PA
2 CONT ElijahCrafford is listed in the publication:
2 CONT
2 CONT “Florence(Cross Roads) Presbyterian Church Cemetery
2 CONT (Originally Kings Creek)
2 CONT WashingtonCounty, Pennsylvania”, published in “MiscellaneousCemeteries, Washington Co, PA”, Vol 1, 1939. More Information:“An enumeration of tombstones and transcriptions of various churchrecords are contained in” the booklet titl
2 CONC ed above, by Robert C.and Agnes D. Kreutzberg, Published 1986.
2 CONT Thereare no other publications or records of this cemetery listing ElijahCrafford as being interred here. Original records were in the churchbuilding which burned in a fire in 1963. Elijah was well acquaintedwith the Rev. Elisha B
2 CONC . Macurdy, the same as witnessed his pensionstatements for his pension application in Oct 1832.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aphoto at this cemetery shows a Memorial Plaque in tribute to thisEarly Pioneer of the Presbyterian Church in Western Pennsylvania. Volunteers have graciously gone to the Florence Cemetery to locate a headstone for Elijah Crafford
2 CONC  if one were still remaining there, but reportssay there is a large section at the west end of the cemetery covered in overgrowth with poison ivy, and that this section has many stones that are either tumbled or unreadable. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Jackson family of Elijah’s son Joseph’s wife’s family was located and photographed.
2 CONT While there, the headstone of Elijah’s son Freegift and his wife Sarah were photographed. The stone is tall and appears to be missing its ‘topknot’, but otherwise in is fair condition.
2 CONT “FreeCrayford, died Sept 15, 1854, Aged 75 Years”.
2 CONT he Rev. Elisha McCurdywas buried here, and the following is inscribed upon his tombstone:
2 CONT "In memory of theRev. Elisha McCurdy, Late Pastor of the Congregation of Cross Roads.Born October 15th, 1763. Licensed June 24th,1799. Ordained and Installed Pastor June, 1800. A Pastor 35 years andminister of the Gospel 46 years.
2 CONC  Died July 22d, 1845. He took anactive part in the great revival of 1802, and was distinguished forhis zealous labors in the cause of Indian Missions."
2 CONT
2 CONT OtherReferences:
2 CONT
2 CONT “TheEarly Ancestors of the Crawfords in America”, by Fred E Crawford,Cambridge, MA 1940, page 80 mentions an Edward, Elijah and John;
2 CONT
2 CONT “Historyof Washington County, Pennsylvania”, Page 77, Elijah mentioned asfather of Rebecca Crawford Thompson,his service in the Revolution,and his arrival in Washington Co;
2 CONT
2 CONT “TheScotch-Irish of Northampton County, Pennsylvania”, Vol I, Pub byNorthampton County Historical & Genealogical Society, 1926; Page520-521 Moutn bethel Tax for 1775: John Crafford Sr and John Jr; Page518 lists Eliojah as Corporal
2 CONC  in a list of Scotch-Irish Soldires inthe American revolution from Mt Bethel; page 586 mentions the deathof Isaac Crafford, son of John in 1765
2 CONT
