2 CONT Joseph Crafford
2 CONT 1780-1863
2 CONT
2 CONT 1780 - Joseph Crafford was born on 11 Oct 1780 in Lower Mount Bethel, Northampton, PA son of Elijah & Elizabeth Stout Crafford. “Portrait & Biographical Album”, 1890, Page 256, Joseph was Executor to his father's will with brother
2 CONC  Isaac; Alt birth date 11 Nov 1780;
2 CONT
2 CONT 1803- Joseph married Deborah Jackson daughter of Joseph Jackson and Elizabeth 'Betty' on 26 May 1803 in Washington Co, PA. Deborah was born on 14 Oct 1785in Hanover Twp, Washington, PA. She died on 13 Jan 1859 in Macomb/Bushnell, 
2 CONC McDonough, IL. She was buried in Bushnell Cemetery,Bushnell, McDonough, IL. Alt date 26 Jun 1803;
2 CONT
2 CONT 1804- Elizabeth Crafford was born in 1804. She died on 8 Nov 1882.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1806- Elijah Crawford was born on 8 Mar 1806 in , , Washington, PA.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1808- Rachel Crawford was born on 17 Oct 1808. She died on 27 Jun 1887.
2 CONT
2 CONT 18xx-JosephCrafford, “bought a tract of timbered land in Patrick's Run,eighteen miles from Pittsburgh, and on the Steubenville Pike”;“Portrait & Biographical Album”, 1890, Page 256, referencing entry for John Crafford, Joseph's so
2 CONC n.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1810- Federal Census,Robinson Twp, Washington, PA, Joseph Crawford,1-0-1-1-0/2-0-1-0-0/0-0; Joseph age 26-44 [29], one male 16-25, onemale under 10; wife age 16-25, 2 females under 10;
2 CONT
2 CONT 1811- “History of
2 CONT Washington County, Pennsylvania”,by Alfred Creigh, 1870, page 211, mentions “when he came near to the place called the Old North Star, formerly kept by Joseph Crawfordas a tavern, ...” Joseph Crafford was a tavern keeper on the ol
2 CONC d Steubenville Pike between Pittsburgh and Steubenville, OH; was postmaster of Racoon, PA “for years”and served as postmaster while in Illinois, this from an entry for George Crafford in source:“Biographical & Historical Memoirs o
2 CONC f Adams, Clay,Webster and Nucholls Counties, Nebraska”, by Goodspeed Pub,Chicago, IL, 1890, Page 230;
2 CONT Another source says that Joseph “bought a tract of timber land in Patrick's Run, eighteen miles from Pittsburgh, and on the Steubenville Pike. He erected a woolen mill, operated by tread power, generally using oxen for the power. 
2 CONC He was a man of much enterprise, and he subsequently opened a hotel, which he managed besides improving a farm. He was profitably engaged in the hotel business thirty years as there being no railways in that part of the country th
2 CONC e pike was much traveled by stagecoaches which made his tavern their headquarters for that part of their route.” Source:“Portrait & Biographical Album”, 1890,Page 256, referencing entry for John Crafford, Joseph's son
2 CONT
2 CONT 1813-Rebecca Crawford was born on 4 Feb 1813. She died in 1841.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1815- Ruth Crafford was born on 10 Nov 1815. She died on 16 Dec 1895.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1818-Joseph CrawfordJr. was born on 14 Oct 1818. He died on 1 Jan 1879.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1820-Federal Census, Robinson Twp, Washington Co, PA, Page 211, Jos Crawford, 1-1-0-1-1-0/3-1-1-1-0/0-2-2; Joseph age 26-45 [39], 1 male16-26 [unk male], 1 male 10-16 [Elijah], 1 male under 10 [Joseph Jr];Wife 26-45 [Deborah], 1 f
2 CONC emale 16-26 [Elizabeth], 1 female 10-16[Rachel], 3 females under 10 [Ruth, Rebecca, Frances];
2 CONT
2 CONT 1820 Federal Census Washington Co, PA
2 CONT
2 CONT 1822- John Crawford was born on 14 Oct 1822. He died in 1895; Joseph and family were“living a mile and a half east of Bevington Mills, where son John was born; [John Bevington's Plantation was named Milltown and was located on the
2 CONC  east fork of Racoon Creek, near or at the present location of Bavington]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1825- Deborah's father bequeath's her $34 in his will, Washington Co, Pa, Surrogate Court, WillBook No 4, Page 56; Nov 7 1825, Recorded in Washington Co, PA Probate Files, FHL Film#1683768, file J-11:“Received of George Jackson ni
2 CONC ne dollars it being the remainder of my wife legasy in full bequeath to her by her father Joseph Jackson[signed] Joseph Crafford” This is the one bit of evidence showing Deborah Jackson who married Joseph Crafford was the daughter
2 CONC  of Joseph Jackson of Washington Co, PA;
2 CONT
2 CONT 1825- Thomas Crawford was born on 19 Sep 1825.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1828- George A. Crawford was born on20 Jun 1828. He died on 4 Apr 1922.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1830-Martha Crawford was born on 1May 1830. She died on 5 Aug 1915.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1830 Federal Census,Robinson Twp, Washington Co, PA, Page 264, Joseph Crawford, 1110101000000/1012010000000; Joseph 40-50 [49], 1 male 20-30[Elijah], 1 male 10-15 [Joseph], 1 male 5-10 [Thomas or John; prob Thomas died], 1 male un
2 CONC der 5 [George]; wife 30-40 [Deborah], 2females 15-20 [Fanny, Rebecca], 1 female 10-15 [Ruth], 1 female under5 [Martha];
2 CONT
2 CONT 1832- Mary Crawford was born on 6 Aug 1832. She died on4 May 1913.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1836- Father's Will, Elijah Crafford,File C-69, Washington Co, Pa,Accounts of
2 CONT Estate 1839-1845, FHL#1683453; Joseph was named co-executor with brother Isaac for his father's estate; final accounts for this estate closed in 1841; final distribution was signed by Isaac alone; Joseph inherited Elijah's land on
2 CONC  Racoon creek which Elijah had purchased from Andrew Carlisle in May 1805, conditioned on Joseph paying the executors of the estate$300 in 4 equal annual payments, also to pay Elijah's wife, Joseph's mother, one third of the yearl
2 CONC y value from the farm for her life; 139acres: the southeast portion of the plantation in Robinson Twp known as 'Lebanon', originally patented to John Singer; Will of Elijah Crafford, Washington Co, PA Will Book 5, Pgs 242-244, FHL
2 CONC  #863626;indenture granting land to Elijah by Andrew Carlisle was recorded 30Jan 1806 Washington Co Deed Bk 1T, Pg 292; also Deed Bk 2X Pg281-283, recorded 27 Aug 1839;
2 CONT
2 CONT 1838- Land Deed, Joseph Crafford and Deborah, his wife,deeded to Andrew Donaldson, 29 Oct 1838, received $5250 for 139 acres and 62 perches strict measure and situated on the waters of Racoon Creek, Robinson Twp, with appurtenance
2 CONC s; “being part of a tract ofland granted by the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania to John Singer for400 ¾ acres strict measure by patent dated 13th day of March 1788”Patent Book N14, Pg 11; John Singer and wife Mary, 25 Oct 1793transfe
2 CONC rred 139 acres 62 perches from the SE part of said 400 ¾ acre tract to Andrew Carlisle, Bk I?, Pg 845; Andrew Carlisle by indenture dated 14 May 1805 conveyed to Elijah Crafford, recorded Bk 1T, Pg292; Elijah bequeathed the land t
2 CONC o Joseph 29 Mar 1829, recorded DeedBk 2X, Pg 281-283;
2 CONT
2 CONT 1838-Joseph, Deborah and family removed to McDonough Co, IL coming by the Ohio and Mississippi Rivers to St Louis and from thereby wagon to McDonough Co.
2 CONT Daughter Martha's obituary gives the date as 1836; daughter Ruth's obituary gives the date as1837; son George's obituary gives the date as 1838; another source:“History and Biographical Record of Iowa”, Pg 373 says Joseph immigrat
2 CONC ed to McDonough County IL in the 1830s; given that he signed of the sale of his land in Oct 1838, it is likely her removed shortly after that date or possibly immediately before; the Crafford farm was located 3 ½ miles SW of Bushn
2 CONC ell, 8 miles north of Macomb;
2 CONT
2 CONT 1838 Deed -Purchase of land from Jacob & Lucy Chase, dated 11 July 1838; N ½Sec 6, Twp 6N, Range 1W (Mound); an equal half of the section;McDonough Co, IL Deed Bk E Pg 168, Deed #1639;
2 CONT
2 CONT 1841-Joseph Crafford purchased for $1000, NE ¼ Sec35, 7N 2W (Walnut Grove Twp) from Chandler, 160 acres more or less;dated 10 Mar 1841; deed#3047, Bk H Pg 7;
2 CONT
2 CONT 1843-Josephpaid Aug 1843 $8.61 for 160acres NE ¼ Sec 35, 7N, 2W, which had been declared to be sold for taxes due; Walnut Grove Twp, Deed Book K, Pg 256;
2 CONT 1847-Joseph paid $100 fora release on quit claim on 40acres in SW Sec 26, 7N, 2W, Walnut grove twp; dated 26 May 1847,Deed Bk M, Pg 184
2 CONT
2 CONT 1840- Federal Census, McDonough Co, IL, Joseph Crofford; 0101100100000/0110101000000;Joseph 50-60 [59]; 1 male 20-30, 1 male 15-20, 1 male 5-10; 1 female40-50, 1 female 20-30, 1 female 10-15, 1 female 5-10
2 CONT
2 CONT 1844-History of McDonough County, Illinois, by Clarke, 1878, Page 94,Joseph Crawford (probably Joseph Jr ?) listed among those “out from the county” concerning the escort of Mormon's from Illinois for their safety from the anti-Mo
2 CONC rmon groups in Missouri; Lieutenants,Joseph Crawford;
2 CONT
2 CONT 1850 Federal Census, McDonough Co, IL 22 Aug 1850, listed as Jacob [Joseph] Crawford 69,Delina [Deborah] 65, John 27, George 32 [22], May [Mary] 18, Martha Linsey 18 [daughter Martha], Crawford Linsey 9 [Grandson];
2 CONT
2 CONT 1852 Joseph & Deborah sold for $513 to Thomas Plotts,son in law, 85 acres NE ¼ Sec 35 in walnut Grove Twp; dated 8 Jun1852; McDonough County deed #26,029, Book 6, Pg 452
2 CONT
2 CONT 1859-Deborah died on 13 Jan 1859 in McDonough Co, IL. She is buried in Bushnell Cemetery, Bushnell, McDonough, IL; Lot 2 Block 20, Section B, Old Section; stone reads “Deborah wife of J. Crafford Sr.”
2 CONT
2 CONT The lot has four plots, two burials, Joseph and Deborah; owned by their son George Crafford;
2 CONT Source: “Bushnell Cemetery at Bushnell, Illinois”, a book prepared by McDonough County Genealogical Society, July 1982;Source: Cemeteries of McDonough County, Illinois, Bushnell”, Page34;
2 CONT
2 CONT 1860 Federal Census,Mound Twp, McDonough, IL, Joseph Crafford, 78 [79] living with son George Crafford and family;
2 CONT
2 CONT 1862-Joseph Crafford Sr sold to Jane P Crafford, wife of Joseph Jr, for $1000 release quit claim all of the NW ¼ Sec xx in Mound Twp except 95 acres off the west side of said quarter; and all of the NE ¼ of Sec 6 in Mound Twp exce
2 CONC pt 100 acres off the east side of said quarter; and all of the NE ¼ of sec 35 in Walnut Grove Twp except those portions heretofore sold to Thomas Plotts, G F Livingston, Alexander Cubbison, Mrs Winkler, and George Crafford;dated 2
2 CONC 1 June 1862; McDonough Co, IL, Deed #30,462, Book 9, Pg 226
2 CONT 1863- Joseph Crafford died on 19 Feb 1863 in Macomb, McDonough, IL. He was buried in Bushnell Cemetery, Bushnell, McDonough, IL. Lot 2 Block 20 Section B, owned by son George Crafford;
