2 CONT Sat 19 Nov 1966:  The Republic  (Columbus, IN)  Page 3 
2 CONT Levi Brosman Dies Friday At Hospital  
2 CONT 3em>LEVI PRESTON BROSMAN, 66, former employe of Columbus Asphalt company, died Friday afternoon at Bartholomew county hospital where he had been a patient for nine days. 
2 CONT 3em>He resided on Edinburg route 2. 
2 CONT 3em>Funeral services will be at 1:30 p.m. Monday at the Reed funeral home, conducted by the Rev. Herschel Northern. 
2 CONT 3em>Burial will be at Bloomington. Persons may call after noon Sunday at the funeral home. 
2 CONT 3em>Born in Greene county near Bloomfield Sept. 20, 1900, he was the son of Alva and Ella TAG BROSMAN. 
2 CONT 3em>A resident of Bloomington for 25 years, he had lived at his present address since May. 
2 CONT 3em>On Nov. 20, 1944, he married Mrs. CAROL HILLENBURG.
2 CONT 3em>Mr. BROSMAN was a member of the Methodist church and the Moose and Eagles lodges of Bloomington. 
2 CONT 3em>Surviving with his wife are a stepson, Dewey HILLENBURG of Edinburg; two stepdaughters, Mrs. Devon NULL of Goshen and Mrs. David BROWN of 1451 Sycamore street; nine brothers, Byrd and Aden BROSMAN of Bloomington, Andy BROSMAN 
2 CONC of Monticello, Bernard and Don BROSMAN of Illinois, Virgil BROSMAN of Henderson, Nev., and Ira and Carl BROSMAN of Phoenix, Ariz. [sic, only eight listed]; and seven grandchildren.
2 CONT 3em>
2 CONT
2 CONT Tue 22 Nov 1966:  The Republic  (Columbus, IN)  Page 2 
2 CONT Levi Brosman Rites Monday 
2 CONT 3em>Funeral services were Monday at the Reed funeral home for LEVI PRESTON BROSMAN who died Friday. He lived on Edinburg route 2. 
2 CONT 3em>Rites were conducted by the Rev. Herschel Northern. Burial was at Valhalla cemetery in Bloomington. 
2 CONT 3em>Pallbearers were Elmer Snyder, David Corum, Don Fogleman, Ray Tabata, Melvin Brosman and Rodney Garrison.
2 CONT
