2 CONT NOTE:  Some lists a Willies  but by census below  there was A "WIllie" listed and is  a nickname for  William  There are several "David "Dave" Buskirks in  Greene and Owen counties Indiana and I think past researchers have gotten 
2 CONC the  children intertwined  and confused -  The census below  listed seems to be a conclusive list of children until obituaries can be  found for  David, Mary and  the siblings  that will either  corroborate  or  disprove
2 CONT
2 CONT DAVID W. BUSKIRK
2 CONT >>  WORTHINGTON, Ind. April 24.— (Special)—Services for David W. Buskirk, 81 years old, of Worthington, who died Sunday, will be at 1 o'clock Tuesday afternoon at the Myers Funeral Home.  Mrs. Naomi Downs will officiate and burial
2 CONC  will be in Newark Cemetery.  - The Terre Haute Star Terre Haute, Indiana - Apr 25 1961
2 CONT
2 CONT Find_A-Grave gives
2 CONT
2 CONT >  s/o Catherine Ellen "Kit" Buskirk Vandeventer,
2 CONT
2 CONT  >> father of Lucinda Marie, Gilbert Ivan, Goldia C., Harley, William Everett, Catherine Ann "Kate"  Luther Edward, and Betty M. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>> NOTE:  Unless  Luther Edward and Betty M was born after and died before the 1920 there is doubt that these are his children.
2 CONT
2 CONT >> Brother of Martin Luther, Ida Frances, and Samuel J. Buskirk. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >> No stone for David, he is buried with first wife, Mary Eva Ritter. 
2 CONT
