1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''LEBANON ENTERPRISE 1/20/1914 DIES IN MERCER COUNTY'''
2 CONT
2 CONT James M. Hourigan, age 83 years, formerly a resident of this county, died at his home in Mercer County, about 3 miles from Harrodsburg, Sunday after a short illness of pneumonia.  He had been in bad  health for several months, and
2 CONC  when strickened with pneumonia his weakened condition was unable to withstand the ravages of the disease.  He was ill for only a few days.  The funeral services were held at Haysville Church Tuesday   morning at 11 o'clock and we
2 CONC re conducted by Rev. R.L. Purdom.  The interment followed in the cemetery there.  Mr. Hourigan was for many years a well known farmer of this County.  Some 8 or 10 years ago, following his marriage to Miss Mary Potts, of Boyle Co.
2 CONC , he moved to Mercer and had since resided there.  Mr. Hourigan was a successful farmer and a splendid citizen, and news of his death was received with much sorrow by his friends throughout the county.  He is  survived by his 3rd 
2 CONC wife and 7 children by former marriages, 3 sons and 4 daughters and also by one sister, Mrs. Victoria Pipes, and one brother, A(pollis) Hourigan.  The family have the sympathy of many friends in their sorrow.
