1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Mary Magdalene Hostetter was born in Greenfield, Ind., May 13, 1859, and departed this life at the home of her daughter, Mrs. Emery Huddle, near Braddyville, Ia., Jan. 2, 1932, aged 72 years, 7 months and 19 days.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was united in marriage with Isaiah Linebaugh on Jan.. 23, 1876. To this union ten children were born, of whom five preceded their mother in death. Those living are Samuel Linebaugh, Clearmont, Mo.; Mrs. Ella Sharp, Oskaloosa, 
2 CONC Ia.; Mrs. Anna Reed, Braddyville, Ia.; Mrs. Emery Huddle, Braddyville, Ia.; also two sisters, Mrs. Samuel Davison, Braddyville, Ia., and Mrs. Florence Williamson, Salina, Kans.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Huddle (error - should be Linebaugh) was converted in her early life and united with the Baptist church at Clearmont, Mo. She has lived a faithful consistent Christian life, always endeavoring to set a Godly example before he
2 CONC r family and friends. She was a loving mother and sister and will be sorely missed by a large circle of relatives and friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral service was held at the Methodist church in Braddyville at 2 o'clock p.m. Jan. 4, by the pastor, Rev. C. S. Dayhoff, and the remains were laid to rest in the Burch cemetery. __________________ Burch Cemetery, Buchanan 
2 CONC Twp., Page Co., Iowa, by Paul Sarrett, Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT ROW 8 1. LINEBAUGH, Mary M., 1859-1932 (double stone)
