1 NOTE {geni:about_me}   Thursday, April 29, 1943,Volume LXVIII, Number 27, Page 1, Column 7, “John W. Bays Dies Following Long Illness.”  John W. BAYS died yesterday afternoon about 1:30 o’clock at his home in Center Township following 
2 CONC a lingering illness of several months. Mr. BAYS was a prominent Center Township farmer, having lived in that township his entire life.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born January 15, 1869, the son of Wiley and Permelia (CLEVER) BAYS. He is survived by the wife, Alice (HOLTSCLAW) BAYS; three children, Dennie BAYS, Mrs. Barge CROWE, and Mrs. Walter GOODWIN, all of Center Township. Also su
2 CONC rviving are two sisters, Mrs. Ollie WATSON of Linton and Mrs. B. F. HOLTSCLAW of Center Township.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held Saturday afternoon at the home with burial in the Bingham Cemetery. Lester Jenkins and Sons Funeral Home are in charge of arrangements.
