1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/person-1500016_424090331_424090331/earl-bays MyHeritage Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 18 2022, 18:09:44 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Bisbee Daily Review", 01-04-1973:
2 CONT   Earl Bays, 75, of 102 Park Avenue, Bisbee, died late Christmas Day at his home. Mr. Bays was a native of Missouri and had lived in Cochise County for over 50 years.  He was a veteran of World War I and retired from Civil Service
2 CONC  at Fort Huachuca.
2 CONT
2 CONT   Survivors include his wife, Mary, of Bisbee; four sons, Clyde of Bisbee, Edwin of Sierra Vista, George of Globe and Donald of Phoenix; a daughter, Mrs. Beatrice Schuller of Sierra Vista; a sister, Sarah Elder of Missouri; 28 gra
2 CONC ndchildren and six great grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT   Funeral services were held on Friday, Dec. 29, from Mitchell's Hubbard Mortuary, Rev. Father Donald officiated with interment taking place in Evergreen Cemetery. Casket bearers who served were Arthur Smith;, Robert Hardt, Jim Wi
2 CONC llson, Lee Benderach, Ralph Sproule and Sam Paken.
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/80658847/earl-bays Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 18 2022, 18:24:35 UTC''
