2 CONT 1. Bloomfield News, Weekly Newspaper. "Bertha (Burch) Hardisty, Bloomington, died Sunday Aug 14, at Hospitality House. Born Nov 3, 1903 in Greene county she was the daughter of Augustine and Dora Belle (Cullison) Burch. She was a 
2 CONC homemaker and member of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter Day Saints in Bloomington. Survivors include her husband Kinsey Ray Hardisty; one son, Morris Leion of Bloomington; three daughters, WIlma Jean Corwin of Solsberry, Norm
2 CONC a Joyce Updike of Manning, Ora. and Janice Diane Coffen of Union Mills; one sister, Bonnie Brandon of Blomfield; 13 grandchildren; one step grandson; 19 great- grandchildren and three stepgreat-grandchildren. She was preceded in d
2 CONC eath by her parents; four sisters and two brothers. Funeral services were 1 p.m. Wednesday, Aug 17 at Jenkins Funeral Home with Bishop WIlliam Morley officiating. Burial was in Walnut Grove Cemetery.August 18, 1996."
