2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha Burch Hardisty, Bloomington, died Sunday, August 14, 1994 at Hospitality House in Bloomington.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born November 3, 1903 in Greene County, she was the daughter of Augustine and Dora Belle Cullison Burch.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha Burch married Kinsey Ray Hardisty on December 5, 1925 in Greene Co., IN.  They were parents of Wilma Jean; Morris Leon; Norma Joyce; and Janice Diane.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a homemaker and member of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter Day Saints in Bloomington.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include her husband, Kinsey Ray Hardisty; one son Morris Leon Hardisty of Bloomington; three daughters, Wilma Jean Corwin of Solsberry, Norma Joyce Updike of Manning, Oregon and Janice Diane Coffeen of Union Mills; one s
2 CONC ister, Bonnie Brandon of Bloomfield; one brother, Albert Burch of Bloomfield; 13 grandchildren; one step-grandson; 19 great-grandchildren and three step-great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her parents; four sisters and two brothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be 1 p.m. Wednesday, August 17 at Jenkins Funeral Home with Bishop William Morley officiating.  Burial will be in Walnut Grove Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Friends may call from 5 to 9 p.m. Tuesday and 10 a.m. until the time of services Wednesday at the funeral home.
