1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The following is excerpted from "Glenn" [Information compiled by Karen Bray Keeley, adapted for the internet  by Sandra Shuler Bray, published on Ancestry.com by "olddiggns" on 27 Feb 2012 [9640409d-5825-4e15-9f99-
2 CONC 12c223bce2c3], then copy-edited, sourced, and reformatted for Geni.com by Curator Pam Wilson, 2020. Attached as a Source document.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is evidence indicating that our branch of the Glenn family in America descends from a James Glenn (Sr.), who was born in 1636 in St. Ninian's Parish, Stirlingshire, Scotland. He was of the MacIntosh clan. His wife was Elizab
2 CONC eth ("Lizzie") Mitchell, also of St. Ninian's Parish, and this couple emigrated to Virginia, where James Glenn died 15 Sep 1696 in Accomack County. His known children, all of St. Ninian's, Stirlingshire, Scotland, were
2 CONT
2 CONT •	Lazarus Glenn (b. abt. 1661) •	John Glenn (b. abt 1662) •	Alexander Glenn (christened 10 May 1663) •	James Glenn Jr. (b. 25 Sep 1664) •	Kathryn Glenn (b. 24 Dec 1665)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT James and John GLENN are not proven to be brothers (the link is tentative).  John GLENN settled in New Kent Co., VA and was the father of Mourning GLENN (b. ca. 1660) who married.  Thomas PETTUS,  James BRAY II.  James GLENN settl
2 CONC ed in Accomac Co..
2 CONT
2 CONT The GLENN family probably had some relationship to the TYREE family, since the name Tyree Glenn was prominently passed down in the Glenn family.
2 CONT
2 CONT The GLENN family of Scotland belonged to the MacIntosh clan.
2 CONT
2 CONT James GLENN was born 1636, St. Ninians, Stirlingshire, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Purchased land Dec 1691 in Accomack co., VA from Woodmen Stokeley (Accomack co. Deeds, Wills and Orders, 1682-1697).
2 CONT In 1695 he gave 217 acres of land in Accomack co., VA to his son, Lazarus Glenn (Accomack co., Deeds, Wills, 1692-1713).
2 CONT The children of James Glenn, Sr., were born to Elizabeth Mitchell.
2 CONT Catherine Winn was his second wife whom he probably married after settling in Accomack co., VA.
2 CONT 4. Georgia Monroe suggests that Mourning Winn might have been either a sister or a daughter of Catherine Winn.
2 CONT 5. Wills and Administration of Accomack Co., 1663-1800 by Stratton Nottingham: "Orders 1690-1697. Glenn, James - Adm. his est to Catherine Glenn, wid of sd. James - Henry Toles & John Morris security, 15 Sep 1696."
2 CONT 6. The parish records of St. Ninian's list the christening of Alexander as a son of James and Elizabeth Glenn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Georgia Munro, 350 Orchard Avenue, Grand Junction, CO 81501. (She had obtained information from Gretta Marshall of 7507 Cliffbrook Dr., Dallas, TX and from parish records (births of St. Ninians, Sterlingshire, Scotland: LDS Reel 7
2 CONC 9, p. 199; Reel 4, p. 223-224; Reel 5, p. 79-80).
2 CONT
2 CONT Tim M. Thompson, 113 Normandy Dr., Belleville, IL 62223.
2 CONT
2 CONT Odom, Fred. Note posted 17 Mar 2000 on the Glenn Family Genealogy Forum () (Re: who are the parents of James Glenn Jr.?)
2 CONT Note posted 29 Sep 2000 on the Glenn Family Genealogy Furum () (Re: Glenn, Mourning, Albemarle Co., VA).
