2 CONT
2 CONT Note from Curator https://www.geni.com/people/Pam-Wilson/6000000001724518898?through=6000000000048130117 (January 2020): Jeremiah has sometimes been ambiguated with John or James Glenn in terms of death dates and children. All fac
2 CONC ts need to be verified with documentation. Also, two Jeremiah Glenns of the same generation seem to be conflated on many family trees, creating data conflicts which may need to be resolved by examining the microfilms of the remain
2 CONC ing Louisa County will books (some were destroyed in the burning of Richmond during the Civil War) or on microfilm.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also, the identity of his wife as Hannah Thompson is questionable and needs evidence to support it. His brother James is also said to have married a Hannah Thompson, and it seems that her name may have become associated with Jerem
2 CONC iah in one of the above-mentioned mixups. A number of children named in James' will were attached to the tree under Jeremiah. However, it appears that a daughter of Robert Thompson and Judith Key married one of the Glenn brothers,
2 CONC  and based on finding two different exact birthdates (on in 1696 and one in 1698) for Hannah Thompsons, there may possibly have been cousins by the same name with ages close together who married the two Glenn brothers. I have not 
2 CONC yet identified parents for the second Hannah. I've found three different death dates among the two Hannahs--1752, 1763, and 1794. The correct birth and death dates need to be researched and assigned to the right Hannah.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
