2 CONC tofore mentioned by raised and all my debts heretofore named are discharged, my negro man Watson to him and his heirs forever. ... also I give to my son John T. Glenn after all my just debts... my negro man Sam to his and his heir
2 CONC s forever. Lastly I do constitute and appoint my sons William Glenn and John T. Glenn Executors of this my last will and Testament hereby revoking all other writen testaments by me made or heretofore safe. ... In witness whereof I
2 CONC  have hereunto set my hand and affixed my seal this 15th day of  Sept., 1830. her                           Hannah  +  Glenn markIn presence of Richard A. Woodson Stephen T. HopeGeorge GammonWill proved  22nd Dec 1830 ============
