1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/James-Glenn/6000000001212613031
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT A Patriot of the American Revolution for VIRGINIA with the rank of LIEUTENANT.  [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A045526  DAR Ancestor #: A045526] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT James Glenn Jr. was born in Cumberland, Virginia, USA  about 1743 to James Glenn and Hannah Thompson. James Glenn married Elizabeth Bowles and had 10 children. He passed away on 1805 in Chester.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT Named in the will of his father, written 11 June 1762
2 CONT
2 CONT >Item: I give to my son James Glen Three Hundred Fifty acres of land in Cumberland County on the upper side of Great Guinea Creek, bounded as by a plan drawn up by Robert Harris, and the sum of thirty five pounds current money and
2 CONC  that part of my stock of hogs and cattle that is in the hands of my son Nathan Glen, to him and his heirs forever.
2 CONT
2 CONT James Glenn, who in 1735 bought land in Chester and Union Counties, S. C., and was a Revolutionary soldier, serving with Washington's army when Cornwallis surrendered at Yorktown.
2 CONT
