2 CONT
2 CONT From Curator https://www.geni.com/people/Pam-Wilson/6000000001724518898?through=6000000003542110758
2 CONT
2 CONT >The identity of Jeremiah Glenn's wife as Hannah Thompson is questionable and needs evidence to support it. His brother James is also said to have married a Hannah Thompson, and it seems that her name may have become associated wi
2 CONC th Jeremiah in one of the above-mentioned mixups. A number of children named in James' will were attached to the tree under Jeremiah. However, it appears that a daughter of Robert Thompson and Judith Key married one of the Glenn b
2 CONC rothers, and based on finding two different exact birthdates (on in 1696 and one in 1698) for Hannah Thompsons, there may possibly have been cousins by the same name with ages close together who married the two Glenn brothers. I h
2 CONC ave not yet identified parents for the second Hannah. I've found three different death dates among the two Hannahs--1752, 1763, and 1794. The correct birth and death dates need to be researched and assigned to the right Hannah.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Hannah born 25 Feb 1696 was apparently a twin with a sister named Susannah, who only lived a few years and died c 1702.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT #Lucy (1731-) 
2 CONT #Worthen (Worsham) (1734-1810) 
2 CONT #Sarah (1737-) 
2 CONT #Tyre (Tyree) (1740-1775) 
2 CONT #William (1744-) 
2 CONT #Elizabeth (1749-) 
2 CONT #Beverly (1750-1817) 
2 CONT #Susanna (1752-)
2 CONT
