1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT GENEALOGY OF PENNSYLVANIA FAMILIES, p. 402-403:
2 CONT John Glen, son of Alexander Glen of Lenlithgow, died before 1722 went to Orange Co., NC, married Sarah Jones, daughter of Robert Jones and Mrs. Ann (Duke) Christmas*, widow of Capt. Christmas and daughter of William Duke. Robert J
2 CONC ones was a son of Edward Jones of Shocco Creek and Abigail Sugan of King and Queen Co., VA Children of John Glen and Sarah Jones: Warham, Thomas, William, Duke, Dr. John, and Edward Glenn (in 1762 all young men, with residence in 
2 CONC Orange Co., NC)....this means that they all would have been born 1741 or earlier, because they were all "of age" by 1762.
2 CONT
2 CONT THE PENNSYLVANIA MAGAZINE OF HISTORY AND BIOGRAPHY, p. 480-499, "Notes on the Family of Glen, or Glenn", which gives the same information as the above.
2 CONT
2 CONT *the facts do not support that Sarah JONES was the daughter of Robert JONES and Mrs. Ann (DUKE) CHRISTMAS, because Ann DUKE married John CHRISTMAS about 1772 in Bute Co., NC, and after Captain CHRISTMAS' death she married Robert J
2 CONC ONES 18 Aug 1779 in Wake Co., NC.  Therefore Robert & Ann couldn't possibly have been the grandparents of the GLENN children who were born before 1741.  Robert & Ann were born LATER than their alleged grandchildren: Anne DUKE, dau
2 CONC ghter of William DUKE and Mary GREEN, was born about 1752, and Robert JONES, son of Edward JONES Jr. and Abigail SUGARS, was born 17 Mar 1752 in Granville Co., NC.
