1 NAME Mary Elizabeth /Harris/
2 GIVN Mary Elizabeth
2 _MARNM Harris
2 NICK Elizabeth Rice
2 NICK Mary Claiborne
2 NICK Mary Rice Claiborne
2 NICK Rice
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1630
2 PLAC Essex, England or
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia Colony
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 BURI
2 DATE 1710
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 9 FEB 1710
2 PLAC Glen Cairn
2 ADDR
3 CITY Doswell
3 STAE Province of Virginia
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not a proven child of https://www.geni.com/people/Col-William-Claiborne/6000000008630666891?through=6000000005028403077.  Evidence needed to support as wife of https://www.geni.com/people/Edward-Rice-of-Virginia/60
2 CONC 00000004739919006?through=6000000005028403077
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary was born 1630 - if she were a Claiborne, she wasn't William's daughter, William didn't marry his wife  didn't until 1635!
2 CONT She can't be William Claiborne's daughter
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Per the Claiborne Society of Virginia'''
2 CONT John Frederick Dorman in Claiborne of Virginia places the marriage of William Claiborne and Elizabeth Butler [Boteler] as about 1635. This book contains the genealogical information for them and their children :
2 CONT
2 CONT William (abt 1636-1678)
2 CONT Jane (abt 1638-bef 1671)
2 CONT John (abt 1641- ?)
2 CONT Elizabeth (1643/45- aft 1668) Some people thought Elizabeth could be Mary, she was born abt 1645 
2 CONT Thomas (1647-1683)
2 CONT Leonard (abt 1649-1694)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Mary
2 CONT * Birth:	1630 - Elizabeth City, King William, Virginia, USA
2 CONT * Death:	Feb 9 1710 - Glen Cairn, Doswell, VA, British Colonies
2 CONT * Husband:	Robert Harris
2 CONT
2 CONT Known children of Robert and Mary include:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Mary Harris (born c. 1662) - married Joseph Royall
2 CONT # Judith Harris (born c. 1664)
2 CONT # Thomas Harris (c. 1666 – c. 1725) - married Mary Giles
2 CONT # William Harris - married Temperance Overton
2 CONT
2 CONT There have been numerous, numerous claims about the issue of Robert Harris and Mary Claiborne, most of which have unsubstantiated. The issue listed above are those who are the most certain.
2 CONT
2 CONT William (married to Temperance Overton), has been genetically linked to Robert Harris. There is no debate there. Claiborn Harris, Robert's grandson, has been genetically linked as well. Those who are interested are recommended to 
2 CONC check out the Harris DNA project for more information.
2 CONT
2 CONT "There is no primary source that identifies Mary Rice as a Claiborne or the daughter of William Claiborne. She should not be included in a list of his children...."
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: In a footnote, Dorman says "no record evidence has been found to support" a daughter of William Claiborne who married ___ Rice and Robert Harris
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I114938&tree=tree1 cites 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Virginia Genealogist Volume 22, 1978, 3. 
2 CONT
2 CONT No family Bible record is known to exist and the will of Capt. William Harris was lost in the fire which destroyed the Hanover County records. The following list of children of Capt. William Harris has been derived from both court
2 CONC  and family records:
2 CONT * (1) Major Robert Harris of Albemarle County
2 CONT * (2) Benjamin Harris of Hanover County
2 CONT * (3) William Harris, Junior, of St. Paul's Parish
2 CONT * (4) John Harris of Hanover County
2 CONT * (5) James Harris of Hanover County
2 CONT * (6) Jemima Harris who married her cousin William Overton.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Tagging https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Harris/6000000005028403077?through=6000000008630775544#/tab/discussion
2 CONT
2 CONT http://sites.rootsweb.com/~molcgdrg/sur/1h/harris-notest1.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Now, despite it not being my line and really none of my business, I'm still going to say it:
2 CONT
2 CONT THERE IS NO MARY CLAIBORNE WHO WAS A DAUGHTER OF WILLIAM CLAIBORNE!
2 CONT
2 CONT WILLIAM CLAIBORNE HAD NO SECOND DAUGHTER NAMED MARY!
2 CONT
2 CONT ROBERT HARRIS OF NEW KENT IN 1662 WAS NOT MARRIED TO ANYONE NAMED MARY CLAIBORNE RICE!
2 CONT
2 CONT If there ever was a Mary Claiborne who married a Robert Harris, it occurred two or three generations later much farther west in Virginia. If there was a Mary Claiborne then, she would have been a great granddaughter or later to Wi
2 CONC lliam Claiborne, definitely not a daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Malcolm Hart Harris is generally credited with being the source of the Mary Claiborne myth, but as Mr. Wallace indicates in his post, Malcolm Hart Harris only made a very slim case that Robert Harris MIGHT have been married to a d
2 CONC aughter of William Claiborne. Harris researchers ever since have taken that and made a whole lot more of it than Malcolm Hart Harris ever intended
2 CONT
2 CONT Phil Harris 3/2/2003
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Robert Maj. Harris: Burial: Harris graveyard, "forks" of James River, Charles City Co., VA
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Mary Claiborne: Date born 2: 1643, James City County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Robert Harris and Mary Claiborne: Marriage: 1660, King William Co., VA
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Robert Harris and Mary Claiborne are:
2 CONT *46 i. Mary8 Harris.
2 CONT *47 ii. John Harris, born 1662.
2 CONT *48 iii. Thomas Harris, born 1667.
2 CONT *49 iv. Claiborne "Ned" Harris, born Abt. 1668.
2 CONT *+ 50 v. William Capt. Harris, born 1669 in Broomfield, Essex, England; died 08 Mar 1705/06 in Cedar Hill, Hanover Co., Virginia.
2 CONT *51 vi. Robert Jr. Harris, born Abt. 1675 in Hanover, Co., Virginia.
2 CONT *52 vii. Benjamin Harris, born 1677.
2 CONT *53 viii. Judith Harris, born 1681.
2 CONT *54 ix. Edward Harris, born 17 Apr 1690.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT From the profile for Robert Harris:
2 CONT
2 CONT Major Robert Harris, of "The Forks"
2 CONT
2 CONT Possible Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT The conclusion of several researchers of the Harris family is that Robert Harris of Wales (1630-1700), about 1650, married the widowed Mrs. Mary Rice, whose maiden name was Claiborne. She, reportedly the widow of one Edward Rice, 
2 CONC was the daughter of Secretary William Claiborne and his wife Elizabeth Butler. These same researchers have concluded that Robert and Mary's son, William, born in 1665, married Temperance Overton (b. 1679), daughter of William Over
2 CONC ton.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, Dr. Harris has written, "It seems more probable that Robert Harris did marry Mary Rice, widow of Edward Rice and daughter of Col. William Claiborne and Elizabeth Butler his wife, but there is no record left to prove it, a
2 CONC s far as known [parts of sentence are italicized], for records have been destroyed." In a later publication concerning the Claiborne family, John Frederick Dorman writes in a footnote that there is no evidence of a such a marriage
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Davis also cautions that there is no definitive answer concerning the wife of Robert Harris. Neither does there seem to be evidence of the name of the wife of Edward Rice. There is no documentation that Robert Harris married Mary 
2 CONC (Claiborne) Rice, widow, nor is there documentation that William Harris was the son of Robert Harris, "the immigrant. "
2 CONT
2 CONT Davis points out that the land holdings of both Robert Harris and William Overton were in Blisland Parish, New Kent Co., not too far from the plantation where Colonel William Claiborne had established his home, after he left Kent 
2 CONC Island in the Chesapeake Bay.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===disputed ancestry===
2 CONT
2 CONT There has been much speculation about "Mary" Elizabeth Claiborne.  Some researchers claim she never exists, some claim she is not a daughter of William Claiborne, others claim she was never married to Robert Harris, while finally 
2 CONC others claim she was not married to "our" Robert Harris.
2 CONT
2 CONT *The basic premise is that Mary (Elizabeth) Claiborne was the daughter of William Claiborne, and that she was married for a short time to Edward Rice.  After Rice's premature death, Mary went on to marry Robert Harris.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/whitworth/1090
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Fr Bill Deyo  I have had a number of e-mail with J. Phil Harris about Elizabeth Mary Claiborne. I showed him where he had many holes in his thinking. I cannot understand why many are so adamant about not wanting Robert Harris to h
2 CONC ave married Mary Claiborne, when they admit Robert Harris' father was a surveryor "partner" of William Claiborne. Your referenced note of his stated that Claiborne only had a daughter, Jane, but there is proof that he also had a d
2 CONC aughter, Elizabeth! Elizabeth's patent is in walking distance from Robert Harris' land! There are many other connections as well. There is no documented record of "Mary" Claiborne because her given/legal name was Elizabeth. Mary w
2 CONC as simply her religious confirmation name that she preferred to be called by. This is the exact case of William Harris' mother-in-law, Elizabeth "Mary" (Waters) Overton, and was not uncommon. I have a Catholic friend who assures m
2 CONC e that it is still a common practice for people to use their confirmation name among friends, but their given/legal name must be the one recorded on legal documents. In the 1600s not only the Catholic Church, but also the Anglican
2 CONC  Church, kept the practice of confirmation names. After all of my e's with Phil Harris, he stated that he had no problem in Robert Harris marrying Elizabeth Claiborne!! I was glad to see the current DNA references. I had checked o
2 CONC n this a few months ago when there were no participants from the William Harris/Temperance Overton line.
2 CONT
2 CONT DNA would solve the mystery of whether the husband of Mary Giles came from the Capt. Thomas Harris line or the Robert Harris/Mary Claiborne line. The tradition is the latter and was even spelled out in an old Harris diary, but it 
2 CONC is no longer available.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: news.rootsweb.com/th/read/HARRIS-COLONIALVA/2007-01/1170310401
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no primary source that identifies Mary Rice as a Claiborne or the daughter of William Claiborne. She should not be included in a list of his children. The connection is wholly through supposition by use the Claiborne name
2 CONC  in the Rice family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Rice married Mary Elizabeth Claiborne, born ca. 1635, when she was a teenager, after 1650. They had 3 sons: James, John/Claiborne and Thomas. Edward died in 1660, leaving Mary with at least 2 babies to raise alone (the 3rd 
2 CONC likely died as an infant). As was often the case, young Mary married a local widower, also with young children, Robert Harris, in 1661. Robert, son of Thomas Harris and Adria (Osborne) Harris, had been born in England in 1615 and 
2 CONC left behind when his parents emigrated to Virginia in 1619. Raised in England, he sailed for Virginia in 1650 with his own family. His wife (Names: Unknown) died around 1660, leaving him with several young children. Robert and Mar
2 CONC y had one son together: William Harris, who married Temperance Overton in 1697.
2 CONT
