2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT REF: "The Five Thomas Harrises of Isle of Wight County Virginia" 1995 by John A Brayton, Chap 1, pg 13
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Son of #2 at  [https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=115368617]
2 CONT
2 CONT Do not confuse with the multitudes of Thomas Harris'.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT About 1693 – Capt. Thomas Harris, son of Maj. Robert Harris and Mary Claiborne, marries Mary Giles (Aug. 22, 1667-Apr. 11, 1747), daughter of Mary Sherrard Willis (c1636-c1735). Her father is uncertain. Thomas and Mary Harris resi
2 CONC ded on Cubb Creek, St. Peter’s Parish, New Kent (later Hanover) County, Virginia, near the Pamunkey River. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas is known to have purchased some land from his brother, William, which was located on Bull Swamp. 
2 CONT Thomas was elected three times to the Virginia House of Burgesses. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1725 - Capt. Thomas Harris, son of Maj. Robert Harris (c1630-c1700) and Mary Claiborne, dies in St. Peter's Parish, Hanover County, Virginia; killed by a Native American with an arrow near his home. Afterward, his widow, Mary, rem
2 CONC arried to a neighbor, Thomas Hardy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
