2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Retrieved from https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Waters-229 and then edited on 19 September 2024
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Waters''' was born December 30, 1654 in St. Sepulchre Parish, London, England, the daughter of Ann Peak and Samuel Waters.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Overton emigrated in 1669 and sent for Elizabeth to work as his maid, with the intention of her becoming his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth was a Catholic and William a protestant and they married as such to avoid the wrath of their families.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married William Overton (b. 1638 England) at the end of their journey from England 24 November 1670 in Yorktown, York River, Virginia at the age of 15. (Possibly married in England.)
2 CONT
2 CONT The eight children of William Overton and Elizabeth Waters, born at New Kent County, Virginia Colony, were:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Elizabeth b 28-6-1673-1735, m. Captain Robert Anderson
2 CONT # William 1675-d 18 Jun 1759; m. Margaret "Peggy" Garland.
2 CONT # Temperance b. 1678/79, New Kent, VA, d 19 Feb 1716, Hanover, VA. She md Capt. William Claiborne Harris abt 1695, son of Maj. Robert Harris and Elizabeth (Mary) Claiborne.
2 CONT # Margaret Overton, 1680-1704. no spouse
2 CONT # Samuel b: 14 AUG 1685 d 1759 Hanover, VA; m. Anne Carr 1710, Hanover, VA
2 CONT # James, Captain, b: 14 AUG 1688 in St. Martin's Parish, Hanover County, Virginia d 18 Jun 1749, Louisa, VA; md Elizabeth Garland.
2 CONT # Truhart Overton, 1689 - bef 1725. m. Elizabeth
2 CONT # Barbara b: 05 FEB 1690 -1766, m. William Winston
2 CONT
2 CONT The date of William Overton's death is not known with certainty. He was certainly living in 1690 when he had a land grant and when his last child was born. The will of his mother-in-law on 29 September 1697 left him a bequest of 1
2 CONC 0s. so, at the very least, she believed him to still be alive as of this date. Elizabeth was living 29 September 1697, named in the same will.  She was of St. Peter's Parish, New Kent County, Virginia (now St. Paul's Parish, Hanov
2 CONC er County).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000209175584827&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Name notes
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of William Overton's wife was '''Elizabeth Waters; it was not Mary Waters'''. The error or confusion comes from the Payne and Prior copies of the Josephus Book, both of which name the wife of William Overton as Mary. This
2 CONC  is clearly incorrect as the will of Ann (Peake) Waters names her daughter as Elizabeth Overton. Land records also name the wife of William Overton as Elizabeth. A careful analysis of the Payne and Prior copies show that it is hig
2 CONC hly likely that the name of William Overton's wife did not appear in the Josephus Book at all but was added sometime later in the 19th century. Regardless of the cause of the error, the name Mary is a 19th century error and the na
2 CONC me of the wife of William Overton was Elizabeth Waters. See her husbands profile for more discussion of the Josephus Book, and the Payne and Prior copies.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Her name was Elizabeth Waters per The Overton Waters book on Ancestry.com. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=wu.89069666733;view=1up;seq=9;skin=mobile---
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE: 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/y/a/g/Douglas-G-Yager/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0349.html]
2 CONT
2 CONT View Tree for Mary Elizabeth WatersMary Elizabeth Waters (b. December 30, 1654, d. 1697) Mary Elizabeth Waters was born December 30, 1654 in St. Sepulcher, Parish, London, England, and died 1697 in St Pauls Parish, Hanover, Virgin
2 CONC ia. She married William Overton on November 24, 1670 in Yorktown, York River, York, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Includes Notes
2 CONT Notes for Mary Elizabeth Waters: Mary, a Roman Catholic of considerable fortune, married aboard the ship she sailed on when she arrived from England, William having sent for her. She came to Virginia as "maid" to be a wife. Mary's
2 CONC  parents were Samuel born 1617 in Eastcott, Northamptonshire, England, and Anne Peak, born 1619 in St. Sepulchre, London, England. Samuel was admitted to Freedom of the Skinners of London 3 Sep 1639.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Mary Elizabeth Waters: Burial: Newgate, London, England. Record Change: February 10, 2004
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Mary Elizabeth Waters and William Overton: Marriage: November 24, 1670, Yorktown, York River, York, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Mary Elizabeth Waters and William Overton are:
2 CONT +Elizabeth Mary Overton, b. June 26, 1673, Yorktown, York River, York, Virginia, d. 1734, St Peters Parish, New Kent County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Usually referred to in contemporary documents (including her mother's will) as "Elizabeth".
2 CONT
