1 NOTE {geni:about_me} “Robert Anderson II, married Mary Overton, sister of Captain James Overton (1688-1749) militia officer and vestryman of St Paul's Parish, Hanover, and daughter of William Overton, who was born in England 3 December
2 CONC  1628, emigrated to Virginia, to whom, with Eben Jones a patent issued on 23 April 1681, for 4600 acres of land in New Kent County (later Hanover) on South side of Pamunkey River, on Falling Creek, for the transportation of ninety
2 CONC  two persons and among the headrights were William and Elizabeth. Overton, on 29 October 1690 William Overton and John Lyddall had a patent for 837 acres of land in St Peter's Parish, NewKent (later Hanover) County above the main 
2 CONC fork of Pamunkey next above land granted Jonathan Norwood and Ambrose Clare. William Overton married Elizabeth Waters, daughter of Mrs. Ann Waters, of St. Sepulchers, London ,widow; will (11) dated September 29, 1697; proved 4 Jul
2 CONC y 1700, besides her son-in-law and daughter, the Overtons, Mrs. Waters mentioned in her will her son John Waters, who had long resided in Virginia; her son Samuel Waters, and her son Thomas Waters, her son-in-law William Goodwinan
2 CONC d brother-in-law Caleb Millett.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue of Robert Anderson, Jr. follows: Richard; John; Garland; Matthew; Robert; Charity; Sarah; and David of Albemarle Co., Va., b. ca 1710 who m. Elizabeth Mills ca 1735, his LWT dtd 1791, .... , and James Anderson,
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Georgians: Genealogies of Pioneer Settlers" by Jeannette Holland Austin, Pg.8
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Robert Anderson Jr. and Mary Overton listed in this book:  Richard, John, Garland, Matthew, Robert, Charity, Sarah, David b. c1710, James b. c1690/1700
2 CONT
