1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Overton-2120
2 CONT
2 CONT Multiple people may be conflated in this profile, i.e. information about different people may be combined and confused.
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses was born about 1740.
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses passed on 1 April 1815, Halifax County, Virginia.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 1st: Susannah "Duprey", they had five children: Susannah is based on her as witness to a will with Moses and Bartholomew Dupuy and the very frequent interaction of Moses and Bartholomew Dupuy. (Bartholomew Dupuy's 5th June
2 CONC  1790 will named his daughter Susannah Dupuy so probably not her.)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT On 27 November 1755, John James Dupuy conveyed to his son Bartholomew Dupuy, for “love and affection for son,” “1 Negro wench named Doll and her daughter, Sarah,” with 200 acres in Amelia County in Ellis Fork of Flat Creek next to
2 CONC  land of Childrey, John James Trabue, Edward Jones and Overton. This showed that https://www.geni.com/people/Bartholomew-Dupuy/296071210610005467?through=6000000209171352831 may have been a neighbor of Moses Overton as early as 17
2 CONC 55.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, Bartholomew Dupuy's daughter https://www.geni.com/people/Susanna-Dupuy/6000000209171352831?through=296071210610005467 was living unmarried in 1798, and Moses' first wife Susannah was dead in 1768, when he married again.  
2 CONC So Moses Overton was not the husband of this Susannah Dupuy.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT This looks conflated.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 2nd: in 1768, Elizabeth Carleton Russell (1745-1821), Elizabeth had two children who were under the guardianship of their stepfather Moses Overton. Note: Moses Overton Jr., believed his mother's name was Elizabeth Russell.
2 CONC  (The Moses Overton who married widow Elizabeth Russell left NO widow when he died in Mecklenburg Co. in 1810. His family now has primary source documentation.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 3rd: 26 May 1800, Prince Edward, Virginia, Penelope Irby (This widow, or more likely her daughter Penelope Parrott, unless Penelope Irby lived to be over 110 years, left a will in Prince Edward Co. dated 15 Nov 1811, prove
2 CONC d 21 May 1821. Prince Edward Co. WB 5. pp. 520-521.Ancestry share)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Comments
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.support.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/overton/935/
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Overton Was the son of Moses Overton and probably Susannah Dupuy (Duprey/Dupree). Susannah has an interesting pedigree. Her father was Bartholomew Dupuy, 2nd. his father was John James (Jean Jacques) Dupuy. His father was B
2 CONC artholomew Dupuy, one of the original Hugenots in the colonies (Va). Go to Alta Search and punch in his name for more info. It doesn't show Susannah connected to Moses Overton. Moses' parents were John Overton/Elizabeth nln.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.support.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/overton/947/
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Susannah as 1st wife of Moses is based on her as witness to will with Moses & Barth(father or son?) & the very frequent interaction of Moses & Barth. BUT NO Proof!! & moses did not name a son Barth & that would be od not to do so,
2 CONC  & While we are certain that this Moses is father of Joseph & s/o of John again not hard proof. (tho little doubt)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT A different Moses Overton.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=grantpinnix&id=I104510
2 CONT
2 CONT Living in Virginia at the same time as Moses Overton and his son of the same name were other men named Moses Overton. Benjamin Overton had a son named Moses Overton who lived in Nottoway County when Moses Overton Jr. was living in
2 CONC  Amelia County. In 1782 a Moses Overton was living in Halifax County in a household of seven whites and five blacks. Although he was likely connected to the Amelia County Overton family, his relationship is unknown. Among his sons
2 CONC  was Moses Overton who married Mildred Lipscomb in Halifax County, Virginia, on 25 June 1801. She was the daughter of Luke Lipscomb. A Luke Lipscomb was living in Amelia County in 1782 and was head of a household of five whites an
2 CONC d one black. Mildred and Moses collected their inheritances from both parents and left for Kentucky around 1806, settling in Gallatin County. Moses died 1 April 1815, soon after the War of 1812. Another Moses Overton was the son o
2 CONC f William Overton and Judith Brumfield and the grandson of William Brumfield of Charlotte County (will dated 9 Feb. 1797 , recorded 2 Dec. 1799). Charlotte County listed Judith Overton head of a family of six withes and one black 
2 CONC in 1782. Moses and his sisters, Anne Overton, Susannah Overton, and Sarah Overton were mentioned in the Brumfield will. Judith married second Reuben Traynum.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # https://www.genealogy.com/ftm/o/v/e/Don-E-Overton/BOOK-0001/0012-0002.html#CHILD2 shows Moses Overton (d. 1810), . MOSES2 OVERTON (JAMES1JOHN, OR CHRISTOPHER OVERTON) died 1810.He married (1) UNKNOWN UNKNOWN.He married (2) ELIZA
2 CONC BETH CARLETON Aft. 1768, daughter of THOMAS CARLETON and SARAH SWEPSON.She was born November 03, 1745 in Lunenburg County, Virginia.He married (3) PENELOPE PARROT IRBY May 26, 1800, daughter of JOSHUA IRBY and UNKNOWN UNKNOWN.She 
2 CONC died 1821 in Prince Edward County, Virginia.
