1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The Morrison Observatory, Glasgow, Mo. To: Dr. Lyon G. Tyler:
2 CONT
2 CONT DEAR SIR:
2 CONT
2 CONT At your request, I send a part of the record contained in the old family Bible of my grandfather, Carr Waller. Some explanation is due by way of introduction.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Hayden's Virginia Genealogies, Excursus-Waller, pp. 382-3, among the descendants of Col. John Waller, Gentleman, first clerk of Spotsylvania Co., Va., the family record of Thomas Waller, one of his grandsons, is given. The olde
2 CONC st son of that family, Carr Waller, named from the family of his grandmother, Agnes (Carr) Waller, is stated to have died single.
2 CONT
2 CONT This seems to imply that he never was married. In fact, he was twice married. His first wife was Miss Elizabeth Martin, daughter of Gen. Joseph Martin, of Henry Co., Va., and his second wife was Miss Susanna Edwards, daughter of A
2 CONC mbrose Edwards, of Henry Co., and niece of Gen. Martin.
2 CONT
2 CONT The reason that so little was known to the genealogists of the family of Carr Waller is that soon after attaining his majority, he left the old family seat in Spotsylvania, and settled in the newly organized Co. of Henry. Here he 
2 CONC married, reared a family of four children, and saw them all married and settled in life. In 1842 he removed with his son, Hon. Joseph Granville Waller, to Warren Co., Mo., where he died May 7, 1843. His old family Bible, with the 
2 CONC record in his own fair handwriting, was left by his will to this writer, his oldest grandson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Carr Waller Pritchett.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Old Family Bible Record of Carr Waller, Henry Co., Va.
2 CONT
2 CONT My father, Mr. Thomas Waller, was born July 29, 1732, & departed this life February 10, 1787. 0. S.
2 CONT
2 CONT My mother, Sarah Dabney, was born October 2, 1740, & departed this life January 10, 1822, aged 81 years, 3 months and 8 days.
2 CONT
2 CONT Carr Waller was born March 12, 1769.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Martin, wife of Carr Waller, was born October 13, 1768 & departed this life June 11, 1805.
2 CONT
2 CONT Susanna Edwards, wife of Carr Waller, was born December 25, 1775, & departed this life September 19, 1831, aged 55 years and 8 months.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pomfrett Waller, Sen., was born January 20, 1747, and departed this life June 20, 1799.
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha Waller departed this life June 20, 1813.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pomfrett Waller, Jun., was born May 8th, 1775, & departed this life April 29th, 1814.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dabney Waller was born Feb. 20th, 1772.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Waller was born 1780, & departed this life 1824.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Matilda Waller, daughter of Carr Waller & Elizabeth his wife, was born July 23, 1797.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Ira Waller, son of Carr Waller & Elizabeth his wife, was born January 5, 1799.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Granville Waller, son of Carr Waller & Elizabeth his wife, was born June 17, 1802.
2 CONT
2 CONT Patsy Myra Waller, daughter of Carr Waller & Elizabeth his wife, was born December 23, 1803.
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTES - Dabney Pomfrett, Jun., & John were brothers of Carr Waller. Pomfrett, Sen., was his uncle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dabney Waller died at the old family seat, "Cedar Point," on the North Anna River, June 6, 1849.
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha Waller was the wife of Pomfrett Waller, Sen., as appears from the will of Pomfrett Waller, Sen., on record in Spotsylvania Co. She was also the sister of Gen. Joseph Martin, as appears from her will on record in Henry Co., 
2 CONC Va. Some of the genealogists have confounded Pomfrett Waller, Sen., with Pomfrett Waller, Jun., and have placed the death of the former in 1814.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Matilda Waller married Henry Edwards June 12, 1814. She died in Saint Charles Co., Mo., about 1879. Of her 10 children, 6 daughters and 4 sons, three survive. The late Judge William Waller Edward was her oldest son.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. William Ira Waller, gained distinction as a physician, but afterwards became a prominent member of the Virginia Conference of the Methodist Episcopal Church. After 1844 he took orders in the Protestant Episcopal Church, and wa
2 CONC s for some years president of Shelby College, Ky. He died in Louisville, Ky., in 1878. He married Miss Mariah Norval, of Lynchburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rev. Granville Carr Waller, of Louisville, Ky., is one of their surviving children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Granville Waller married Miss Virginia McDonald January 8, 1822. He moved to Missouri from Henry Co., Va., in 1842. For many years he was presiding Judge of the Co. court of Warren Co. He died about 1860.
2 CONT
2 CONT Three of his ten children now survive. His youngest daughter, Eliza, with her husband & 5 children, perished in the great disaster at Galveston last September.
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha Myra Waller (written Patsy by her father) married Henry Pritchett, October 23, 1822. She died Nov 23, 1857.
2 CONT
2 CONT The writer is the oldest of her ten children, of whom 5 now survive.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Research Note'''
2 CONT
2 CONT I have unlinked Mary Edwards as a wife for this profile as she was born in 1907. Templeton-1883 18:39, 29 November 2021 (UTC)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Data Changed'''
