2 CONT
2 CONT Silas Harris (DNA #6) of Virginia then Wilkes/Surry North Carolina 
2 CONT      Silas is also found on Washington Co., VA tax list as a young man, going there with his parents Dabney & Mary Harris,  brothers Benjamin & Christopher Harris, & sisters Mary Harris/Roy, Isabella Harris/Music.
2 CONT      In 1804, Silas purchased 100 acres for 100 pounds, on the south fork of Mitchell's River in Surry Co., NC from Elkanah Lewis II, with his brother- in-law, William Lewis Franklin, acting as a witness.  
2 CONT
2 CONT      Married Dec. 7, 1801, to Edith "Eady" Franklin, Surry Co., NC
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT 1. Joel, b. 1802, m. Dec. 17, 1833, to Sarah Norman in Surry Co., NC
2 CONT 2. William Lewis, b.  March 4, 1804, m. Hannah Smith, moved to Ashe, later Alleghany Co., NC
2 CONT 3. Unknown daughter b. 1805
2 CONT 4. John, b. 1808, m. Dec. 23, 1833 to Hannah Lowden in Surry Co., NC
2 CONT 5. Ambrose, b. 1810, m. Lucinda Fields, moved to Wilkes Co, NC
2 CONT 6. Sarah, b. 1811
2 CONT 7. James, b. 1813, m 1st UNK, m. 2nd Edith
2 CONT NOTE: James with 2nd wife Edith, along with daughter Mary (Mary's mothers name is not known as she is from James 1st NUK wife) are living with parents in 1850. In 1860 his father Silas has died and his mother Edith is now living w
2 CONC ith his family. Some have misinterpreted the 1850/60 census and have Edith (wife) & Mary (daughter) as his siblings, but this is wrong.
2 CONT 8.  Squire Henderson, b. 1817, m. Phoebe Fields, moved to Wilkes Co.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/211899288/silas_harris Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr
