1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Journal of Gentry Genealogh by Willard Gentry, Vol. 1, Issue 5
2 CONT
2 CONT COLONEL JOSHUA GENTRY 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 6 Jun 1797 - Cabin in the cane break, Madison Co., Kentucky Died 22 Jan 1864 - Marion Co., Missouri
2 CONT
2 CONT Colonel Joshua Gentry, was Private Richard Gentry's seventh son and a brother of Colonel Richard Gentry. In 1816, Joshua left home to make his own way in the world. Joshua's first stop was St. Louis where he sought employment from
2 CONC  Colonel John Sullivan who hired Joshua to manage his large farm on the outskirts of the city. Joshua worked for Col. Sullivan for seven years before taking the advice of a friend and moving to Northeast Missouri. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joshua settled just west of Hannibal, Missouri in 1823 where he filed for 160 acres of land. Joshua worked the land in the summer and taught school in the winter. There he met Eula "Uly" Adeline Henry, the 13-year-old granddaughte
2 CONC r of Colonel Malcolm Henry, another Revolutionary War veteran whose son William had moved west to the new Missouri frontier in 1817. Joshua and Adeline were married on April 11, 1826.
2 CONT
2 CONT Followed by a long article about their lives in Civil War times.
2 CONT
2 CONT His farm on the west side of Hannibal, MO is still in the possession of Joshua and Eual's descendants
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT !Col. Joshua Gentry was said to have been the president of the Hannibal-St. Joseph Railroad during the Civil War, and a senator from Missouri. His obituary was published in the Missouri Republican on 4 Feb 1864.
