2 CONT !From "The Gentry Family in America" by Richard Gentry: "Jane Harris Gentry...married first, Valentine White of Madison Co., Ky., Jan. 15, 1824; he died Jan. 8, 1834. Married second, Major James Blythe, her first cousin, Oct. 16, 
2 CONC 1834; her father, Richard Gentry, was a brother of his mother, Onie Gentry Blythe. Major Blythe was a man of ability and large means. He bought and improved the old Gentry homestead.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane married first Valentine White 15 Jan. 1824 in Madison Co., Kentucky and second James Blythe 16 Oct. 1834 in Madison Co., KY.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with White:
2 CONT  William H. White b: 8 OCT 1825
2 CONT  Richard J. White b: 15 DEC 1827
2 CONT  Durrett White b: 18 NOV 1829
2 CONT  Nancy Jane White b: Abt 1831 in Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane's mother was Jane Harris, daughter of Christopher HARRIS and Agnes MCCORD Harris. Her father was Richard Gentry, b. 1763 in Louisa Co., VA. d. 1843 in Madison Co., KY.
