1 NOTE {geni:about_me} First wife was Anna Tatum, they were married in Sumner Co TN in 1823. They had three children: Andrew b. 1824, Robert b. 1825 and Mary Anne b. 1827. Anna must have died in TN.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob C. BROWN then married Nancy MILLER in Wilson Co. TN.in 1830 and had moved to Illinois that year. They came to Pella Iowa in 1844, in 1846 he was listed as one of the Lake Prairie Twp. election Judges and then a Petit juror w
2 CONC ith an address of Monroe,Jasper Co.IA then summit twp in Marion Co.IA in 1847. His original Homestead in Marion Co.IA 1847 section 16 twp 77N-19W. According to an article in the Prairie City Newspaper written by Lt. Ora A. Martin 
2 CONC 16 Aug.1923 grandson of Jacob C.Brown, Jacob kept the Elk Horn Tavern at Tool's Point.
2 CONT
