1 NOTE {geni:about_me} MAUPIN, CORNELIUS. Born Feb. 3, 1758. Private under Capt. Robert Harris, Maj. Nicholas Lewis; enlisted August, 1778, for two months; again March, 1781, for two months under Capt. Henry Burk; September, 1781, three 
2 CONC months, shoemaker at Albemarle Barracks. Enlisted in Albemarle County, Va. He applied for pension, but claim was rejected on the grounds that the soldier did not render six months' service. Buried in Halley Cemetery, near Armstron
2 CONC g, Mo."
2 CONT
2 CONT Report of the National Society of the Daughters of the American Revolution, Volume 19, U.S. Government Printing Office, 1917, p274
2 CONT
2 CONT Cornelius Maupin's name is on a memorial honoring veterans of the Revolutionary War and the War of 1812 buried in Howard Co, MO. Information and pictures of this memorial can be found at the Howard County Revolutionary War Memoria
2 CONC l - Fayette, Missouri website.
2 CONT
2 CONT Served as private in company of Capt. Henry Burk under Major Nicholas Lewis of · Albemarle. Pension Office records.
2 CONT
