2 CONT Wilson, Thomas (A.G. 50,195), Lieut. in the Ill. Regt. Va. State Troops, commanded by George Rogers Clark. He d  Feb. 27, 1828, in Harrodsburg, Mercer Co., Ky., leaving a wife but no children. John Montgomery, Lieut.-Col. of  his 
2 CONC Regt testified that he served from Apr. 28, 1779 to June 23, 1782. In his will made Feb. 27, 1827, when he was  about 76 years of age, he mentions his wife, Mary, Eli Wheat, Archibald Woods of Harrodsburg, Joseph Woods,  bro. of A
2 CONC rchibald, James Woods, also bro.of Archibald, and of Springfield. To each of these three bros. he gives  one third of one thousand dollars. His exrs. were Dr. [p.579]Phillip Trapnall and Thomas Allen. The will was  witnessed by Th
2 CONC omas L. Wheat, John M. Carter and Nancy B. Pratten.
