1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Nancy Harris Woodson (Allen)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Nancy Harris Allen was born 14 December 1789 in Mercer County, Kentucky. She was the daughter of Thomas Allin and Mary Jouett.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married 23 December 1807 in Mercer County, Kentucky to Samuel Woodson.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1830, she was mentioned in her father's Last Will as having been “of uncommon feeble health from her infancy” thereby inheriting a larger share of the estate.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Nancy, age 43, died 8 October 1833 in Hopkins County and is buried at Odd Fellows Cemetery in Madisonville, Hopkins, Kentucky.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT # ↑ 1.0 1.1 Find A Grave: Memorial #111162940 accessed 17 July 2022, memorial page for Nancy Harris Allin Woodson (14 Dec 1789–8 Oct 1833), citing Odd Fellows Cemetery, Madisonville, Hopkins County, Kentucky, USA; Maintained by Li
2 CONC nda Y (contributor 47158925). Tombstone photo attached. Birth and death dates inscribed. Name inscription: Nancy Harris Woodson.
2 CONT # ↑ "Kentucky, County Marriages, 1797-1954", Sam Woodson and Nancy H Allen, 23 Dec 1807; citing Marriage, Mercer, Kentucky, United States; FHL microfilm 191,843. FamilySearch database accessed 15 July 2022.
2 CONT # ↑ Thomas Allin, Last Will, "Kentucky Probate Records, 1727-1990," Mercer County, Kentucky Will records, Will Book 9, pages 498 - 501 (images 58 - 60); Last Will Written 5 May 1830, first codicil written 13 July 1830, second codi
2 CONC cil written 10 November 1832. It was proved August Court 1833. FamilySearch database accessed 17 July 2022.
2 CONT per https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Allin-522
2 CONT ----
