1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The first school in Monticello, KY of which we have any record was opened in 1807 by Rodes Garth. He taught 'Roman history, the Scriptures, orthography, and pronunciation.' This young man was referred to by Micah T
2 CONC aul as 'a young man of 'probity and worth.' He was later admitted to the bar and served several times in the legislature. His diary of the War of 1812 gives us an idea of his knowledge of English composition. It was indeed a happy
2 CONC  beginning of the educational undertaking of the town to have a teacher of such qualifications as the first schoolmaster. From: A Century of Wayne County Kentucky by Augusta Phillips Johnson.
