1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT We do not know Jane Hescott's death date but several family genealogies state that Robert Thompson married in 1734, presumably to a 2nd wife. She may have been named Mary Viau or Jane Via and of French Huguenot origins. Many genea
2 CONC logies confuse her with Jane Hescott. These are the children credited to him after 1734:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Hannah Thompson b: 1735 in Louisa, Virginia (m. David Epperson)     
2 CONT # Elizabeth Thompson b: 1741in Virginia (m. Thomas Langford III) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Thompson, Jr., lived until June 1778 when he died in Fredricksville Parish, Albemarle County, Virginia.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT "The Story David Epperson and his Family of Albemarle, Co., VA"Page 21
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Old House" Bless it's old heart, if we could count years as it can, we too might be peaceful and restful. But our lives are so short, we come and go so fast, no wonder at times the old House seems looking down on us with sadn
2 CONC ess; for surely the graveyard in the meadow nearby tells the story of man's short existence. The happy, merry people whose voices once made the walls of the old House ring rest there under the myrtle and boxwood, watched over by t
2 CONC he nightingale and whip-poor-will. The old headstones, moss and ivy covered, lean down toward their dead lovingly, as though wishing to get nearer to them.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Edna Epperson Brinkman "David Epperson and his Family of Albemarle Co., VA"
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1802 Hannah started for Hawkins County, Tennesse, with her son Charles and family, leaving presummably five daughters and one son in Albemarle.  Hannah's daughter, Judith, who married James Gardner was said to have moved to Ten
2 CONC nesse and Kentucky with her mother and her brother Charles, but this statement was not proved.  Make your own 'conclusion' after reading the following.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Hannah left her home on the 'mountain' (Epperson Mountain), she left her dead in the little lot on the hillside overloooking the great beautiful valley toward the East. From the description in the deeds of the property sold a
2 CONC t this time, David's home and grave seem to be a part of the 'Blue Ridge Farm' in Greenwood, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah took this long journey with her son, Charles and his family.  Arriving in Kentucky, Charles bought a home in Estill County, a short distance from the little town of Richmond and just over the Madison County line.
2 CONT
2 CONT 'UNMARKED STONE'
2 CONT
2 CONT There is an unmarked stone in "Drowling Creek Church Cemetery" near the little station of Panola, on the Louisville and Nashville Railroad.  A cut of this church and cemetery is given herein.  In this cemetery, with an unmarked st
2 CONC one, is probably the grave of Charles' mother, Hannah. The family story was that "Hannah' died in Kentucky.  Land sold about this time by James Gardner and his wife, Judith, in Madison County, Kentucky, would indicate that Hannah'
2 CONC s daughter, Judith Epperson Gardner, was in Kentucky at this time with her mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN OF DAVID and HANNAH EPPERSON:
2 CONT
2 CONT - Hannah EPPERSON FREEMAN b: 1754 in Albemarle Co., Virginia - David Jr. EPPERSON b: 1755 in Albemarle Co., VA - Francis EPPERSON b: 1756 in Albemarle Co., Virginia - Thompson EPPERSON b: 1757 in 20 miles S.W. of Charlottesville, 
2 CONC Albemarle Co., VA (Epperson Mt.) - John EPPERSON b: 1761 in Albemarle Co., VA (my 4th Gr. Grandfather) - William EPPERSON b: 1762 in Albemarle Co., Virginia - Robert EPPERSON b: 1764 in Albemarle Co., Virginia - Lucy Jane EPPERSON
2 CONC  BURCH b: 1765 in Albemarle Co., Virginia - Charles EPPERSON b: 14 Jul 1766 in Albemarle Co., Virginia - Judith EPPERSON GARDNER b: 1768 in Albemarle Co., Virginia - Susanna EPPERSON LANGFORD b: 1770 in Albemarle Co., VA - Elizabe
2 CONC th EPPERSON PROCTOR b: 1776 in Albemarle Co., Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT I have been blessed to have an 'original' copy of "David Epperson and His Family of Albemarle Co., VA" handed down through the family.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
