2 CONC ch.  Wit:  David Thomson, Caty Thomson, Mary Norton. VIRGINIA COLONIAL SOLDIERS, by Lloyd DeWitt Bockstruck, 1988, reproduced on Broderbund's CD 503 (VIRGINIA COLONIAL RECORDS, 1600-1700s), "Militia Miscellany - Petitions":  Claim
2 CONC  of David Thompson for provisions for the Hampshire militia.  20 March 1767. ABSTRACTS OF WILLS, INVENTORIES, AND ADMINISTRATION ACCOUNTS OF ALBEMARLE COUNTY, VIRGINIA, 1748-1800, compiled by J. Estelle Stewart King, 1940:  Thomps
2 CONC on, David.  10 June, 1769.  Nov. Court, 1769.  Frederickville Parish, Albemarle County.  "Lawful and beloved wife" is bequeathed plantation and estate, at her d ecease it is to be divided among six children (not named).  Exrs:  Jo
2 CONC hn Pendleton (of Louisa County) and William Blackwell, of this county.  Wit:  Richard Bruce, Bezalael Brown and James Epperson.  (page 253).
