1 NOTE {geni:about_me} James and Martha Gallman Brown reared a family of eight, four sons and four daughters, all of whom they educated, which in those early days days was especially commendable, due to the fact that there were no public
2 CONC  schools and an education was very expensive for a large family. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Adjutant General's Office of the War Department, at Washington, D.C. gives the following statement: The records show that James Brown, name not found as James Brown, Sr., rank not shown, served in the Revolutionary War in Capt
2 CONC ain Robert Fenner's Company, 2nd North Carolina Battalion, Commanded by Colonel John Patten. His name appears on a Company roll dated at Camp White Plains, September 9th, 1778, which shows that he enlisted July 1, 1777 for three y
2 CONC ears." Being large of statue at an early age, which still is noticed in his decendants, he was accepted in the Army at the age cf eleven years.
