1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Notes for ELIZABETH BROWN: 1840 Tattnall County GA Census-Living in the household of son, William Joyce. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pioneers of Wiregrass Georgia-Huxford, "William Brown, a Revolutionary War martyr (Vol. II) and ancestor of the descendants of John and Elizabeth Joyce of Southern Georgia, was born in Albemarle County, Virginia, about 1735, a son
2 CONC  of Benjamin and Sarah (Dabney) Brown. In 1768, his brother, Bartlett Brown and family removed to Orangeburg District, SC, and the next year William Brown and his family moved there also. This part of Orangeburg District where the
2 CONC y settled, was later made into Barnwell District, now Barnwell County. To William and his wife Sarah (maiden name unknown) were born the following children: (See children listed). 
2 CONT       William Brown was murdered at his home in Barnwell District in May 1780, by a party of Tories commanded by the notorious McGirt. His wife, Sarah, died four years later. 
2 CONT       Two of William Brown's sons, Tarlton and Barlett, were Revolutionary soldiers, also at least four of his sons-in-law. It was the intense Whig sentiments and attachments of the Brown family that made the elder Brown the objec
2 CONC t of McGirt's wrath. 
2 CONT       An instrument on record in Barnwell County Deed Book "H" PP. 221-222, dated July 14 1810, signed by Bartlett Brown, one of the heirs, discloses the names of the above heirs as listed, and also the fact that the elder Brown h
2 CONC ad been killed as above stated, etc.: 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/48128152/elizabeth-joyce
2 CONT
