1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary first appears on the 1850 Platte, Buchanan Co, MO census with her father Pleasant Sublett and his second wife, Sarah Sales/Sails: Pleasant Sublett	M	38	KY; Sarah Sublett	F	22	VA; John Sublett	M	19	KY; William 
2 CONC Sublett	M	17	KY (fought in the Civil War); Mary Sublett	F	14	KY (this would be our Mary who marries Anderson Simmons in 1852); Nancy Sublett	F	13	KY; Rebecca Sublett	F	11	KY; David Sublett	M	9	Iowa; Julia Sublett	F	7	Iowa; Mariam 
2 CONC Sublett	F	2	Illinois (where is son Jackson, b 1870, IL? could this be the same person? census taker's error?); George Sublett	M	0	MO (this one matches up in name and age with later censuses) (born June 1850, listed as 5/12s).
2 CONT
2 CONT On Sept. 1, 1852, in Clinton Co, MO, she marries Anderson David Simmons, son of Henry and Jane Simmons. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She and her family with Anderson are nowhere to be found in the 1860 census (as of yet)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary's husband Anderson David Simmons died in the Civil War, at the army hospital at Helena, Phillips County, Arkansas, on March 15, 1863, of illness.  He fought for the Union, so I can imagine this may have been a point of conten
2 CONC tion between him and Pleasant.  (We may assume Pleasant had Confederate leanings since the Carpetbaggers ran him out of Missouri?)
2 CONT
2 CONT David's Civil War file mentions a George Slocum and a John Hughes as witnesses to Mary's widow pension application dated June 11, 1863. Her widow application is #28193, cert. no. 15699.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Jane remarried on August 28, 1866 at Buchanan Co, to Conrad Schottel, 3 1/2 years after David dies.  David's pension file for his orphans verifies this.  She died January 19, 1880, at Gentry County and is buried at the Long B
2 CONC ranch Cemetery near Stanberry.  She is listed on FAG as Mary Jane Simmons Schottel.  DAR has a record of her death, same date, on records from the Gentry County Historical Society cemetery survey. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT James Acy Simmons, born 2 Aug 1854; Martha Elizabeth, born 20 Oct 1856; Sarah Frances, born 11 Oct 1859; Levi A Lawson Simmons, b 5 Jan 1863 - he died 1954 in California.
2 CONT
2 CONT She marries Conrad Schottel on 8/28/1866 in Buchanan County MO.
2 CONT
2 CONT They are in the 1870 Andrew, MO census as follows, with Anderson's and Jane's two youngest children, plus two more who have been born prior to the census, William and Henry: Conrad Shottle	M	27	Missouri Jane Shottle		F	33	Missouri
2 CONC  Francis Shottle	F	11	Missouri Levi Shottle		M	9	Missouri William Shottle	M	3	Missouri Henry Shottle		M	1	Missouri Citing this Record "United States Census, 1870," database with images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/
2 CONC 61903/1:1:M4X3-54L : 17 October 2014), Henry Shottle in household of Conrad Shottle, Missouri, United States; citing p. 20, family 132, NARA microfilm publication M593 (Washington D.C.: National Archives and Records Administration
2 CONC , n.d.); FHL microfilm 552,254.
2 CONT
2 CONT Meanwhile, Pleasant and family have moved to Gentry Co, MO as listed in the 1870 census.
2 CONT
2 CONT After her marriage to Conrad Schottel, she had six more children: William Schottle, Henry Schottel, Mary Jane (married Sager), Frederick Schottel, Caroline and Louisa Schottel (who may be twins). After she died, in early 1880, Con
2 CONC rad remarried, to Mrs. Anna Sagers. The first five children mentioned below are children from Conrad's and Mary Jane's marriage. The others are from his second marriage to Anna: Conrad Schottel Event Type	Census Event Date	1880 Ev
2 CONC ent Place	Jackson, Gentry, Missouri, United States Gender	Male Age	33 Marital Status	Married Race	White Race (Original)	W Occupation	Farmer Relationship to Head of Household	Self Relationship to Head of Household (Original)	Self B
2 CONC irth Year (Estimated)	1847 Birthplace	Germany Father's Birthplace	Germany Mother's Birthplace	Germany Sheet Letter	C Sheet Number	529 Person Number	0 Volume	1 Conrad Schottel	Self	M	33	Germany Annie E Schottel	Wife	F	36	Germany He
2 CONC nry Schottel	Son	M	12	Missouri, United States Mary J Schottel	Daughter	F	10	Missouri, United States Frederick Schottel	Son	M	8	Missouri, United States Caroline Schottel	Daughter	F	6	Missouri, United States Louisa Schottel	Daughter
2 CONC 	F	6	Missouri, United States Chas Sagers	Stepson	M	11	Iowa, United States Anna Sagers	Stepdaughter	F	14	Iowa, United States Frank Sagers	Stepson	M	12	Iowa, United States Lizzie Sagers	Stepdaughter	F	8	Iowa, United States Carrie Sa
2 CONC gers	Stepdaughter	F	5	Iowa, United States Hettie Sagers	Stepdaughter	F	3	Missouri, United States Christian Stoll	Other	M	28	Germany Citing this Record "United States Census, 1880," database with images, FamilySearch (https://famil
2 CONC ysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:M6XS-ZS6 : 14 July 2016), Conrad Schottel, Jackson, Gentry, Missouri, United States; citing enumeration district ED 278, sheet 529C, NARA microfilm publication T9 (Washington D.C.: National Archives and 
2 CONC Records Administration, n.d.), roll 0687; FHL microfilm 1,254,687.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Death records were kept for Missouri counties starting in 1883, so Mary Jane would not have been recorded on the Gentry Co. register, (according to 'Missouri pioneers, county and genealogical records, Vol. 6' which has a reg
2 CONC istry of Gentry Co deaths from 1883 -)
