0 @N6000000004086350408@ NOTE The Will of Robert Harris is as follows: 
1 CONT June 18, 1765, probated Aug. 8, 1765,
1 CONT "In the name of God, Amen. I Robert Harris of the County of Albemarle,
1 CONT being of perfect mind, and memory, do make and ordain this my last
1 CONT will and testament, in manner and form following: first and
1 CONT principally I recommend my soul to God, who gave it me, not doubting
1 CONT but through the merits of my blessed saviour to have full pardon and
1 CONT remission of my sins, and my body, I recommend to the earth from
1 CONT whence it came, to be buried in such manner, as my executors hereafter
1 CONT named shall see fit. And as touching such temporal estate as it hath
1 CONT pleased God to bestow on me, I give and dispose of in manner and form
1 CONT following. Imprimis: I give and bequeath to my son, Christopher Harris
1 CONT forty acres of woodland, ground lying and being in the County of
1 CONT Albemarle, on a large spur of the Blue Bidge of Mountains near to a
1 CONT place commonly called and known by the name of the "Bear cornfield,"
1 CONT to him and his heirs and assigns forever.
1 CONT Item: I give and bequeath to my son, William Harris, after the decease
1 CONT of my loving wife, Morning (Mourning) Harris, all the land which I
1 CONT hold in the County of Albemarle to him and his heirs forever.
1 CONT Item: I leave to my loving wife Mourning Harris, the sole use and
1 CONT benefit of all the lands and plantations during her natural life,
1 CONT which is above given to my son, William Harris after her decease.
1 CONT Item: I leave to the said loving wife, the sole use and benefit during
1 CONT her natural life, six slaves, that is to say, Harry, Peter Dick and
1 CONT Aaron, men, Patta and Nanny, women.
1 CONT Item: My will and desire is, after the decease of my wife, that if my
1 CONT negro man, Harry should be then living, in that case I give and
1 CONT bequeath the said Harry, to my son, Robert Harris, junior, to him and
1 CONT his heirs.
1 CONT Item: My will and desire is, after the decease of my wife, that if my
1 CONT negro man, Peter, should be then living, in that case I give and
1 CONT bequeath the said Peter to my son, Tyre Harris, to him and his heirs.
1 CONT Item: My will and desire is, after the decease of my wife, that if my
1 CONT other four negroes, Dick and Aaron, men, and Patta and Nanny, women,
1 CONT be then living, I give and bequeath them and their increase to my son,
1 CONT William Harris, to him and his heirs.
1 CONT Item: My will and desire is, that if my son, William Harris should die
1 CONT before he attains the lawful age, or without issue, that in that case,
1 CONT he the said William Harris should be further educated, the charges
1 CONT thereof shall be paid out of the estate given him, after the whole
1 CONT being sold, by my executors herein after named, and the remainder of
1 CONT the money arising from such sale be equally divided amongst all my
1 CONT children, or their legal representatives.
1 CONT Item: My will and desire is, that my son William Harris to be under
1 CONT the tuition, direction and government of my son-in-law, John Rodes,
1 CONT until he shall attain to lawful age.
1 CONT Item: I give and bequeath to my loving wife, when all my lawful debts,
1 CONT and funeral expenses is paid all the residue of my estate, be it of
1 CONT whatever nature or quality soever, to her and her heirs forever. I do
1 CONT constitute and nominate and appoint my sons-in-law, John Rodes and
1 CONT William Shelton, to be my executors of this my last will and
1 CONT testament. As witness my hand and seal this eighteenth day of June in
1 CONT the year of Our Lord, one thousand seven hundred and sixty five.
1 CONT (Signed) Robert Harris. (L. S.)
1 CONT Signed, sealed, etc., in the presence of Daniel Maupin, John Mullins,
1 CONT James William Maupin, Courtley Mullins.
1 CONT At a Court held for Albemarle County, the 8th day of Aug. 1765, this
1 CONT will presented in Court, proved by the oath of Daniel Maupin and
1 CONT William Maupin witnesses thereto, and ordered to be recorded, and on
1 CONT the motion of John Rodes and William Shelton, the executors therein
1 CONT named, certificate is granted them for obtaining a probate thereof, in
1 CONT due form on giving security. Whereupon they with David Rodes and
1 CONT Christopher Harris their securites entered into and acknowledged their
1 CONT bond according to law.
1 CONT Teste, Henry Frye, C.
1 CONT A copy, Teste, W. L. Maupin, Clerk.
