0 @N6000000004086341347@ NOTE Christopher Harris came to what is now Madison County, Kentucky from 
1 CONT Albemarle County, VA in 1786. Will of Christopher Harris of Madison
1 CONT County, KY taken from Will Book A-page 54, 55. It was transcribed by
1 CONT Eileen Niederkorn.
1 CONT CHRISTOPHER HARRISS WILL - Will Book A-pg 54, 55
1 CONT In the name of God Amen. I Christopher Harris being through the
1 CONT abundant mercy and goodness of God tho weak in body yet of perfect
1 CONT understanding and memory do constitute this my last will & Testament
1 CONT and desire it should be reviewed by all as such. Imprimis that I will
1 CONT & Desire that my first Children (Viz) Dabney Harris, Sarah Martin,
1 CONT Robert Harriss, Mourning Jones, Christopher Harrifs, & Mary Jones
1 CONT should have the following negroes (excepting thirty pounds out of my
1 CONT son Dabneys Legacy which is to be paid by the Executors of this Part
1 CONT of my Will for the use & Benefit of my wife and Other Children) (Viz)
1 CONT Ritter and her Children, Pomp, Moses, Allice, George, Betty, Lucy and
1 CONT Delphy the above Negores to be Divided Agreeable to Cornelias Dabneys
1 CONT Seniors Will and I do appoint Foster Jones, and Christoph
1 CONT Harrifs as Executors of the above part of this will and as to the
1 CONT Ballance of my Estate I Direct that first my Debts shall be paid out
1 CONT of what money I have by or is owing to me the house where I live I
1 CONT Direct should be finished which together with the tract of land
1 CONT whereon I live, I leave to my Dear & loving wife during her life and
1 CONT at ther death to son Overton Harrifs as to the Ballance of my Negroes
1 CONT (David, Cate, Fanny, Stephen, and Eddy together with my House hold
1 CONT furniture Stock of every kind and Plantation utensels I desire that my
1 CONT wife may have the whole Benefit of them during her life or widowhood
1 CONT and if she should Marry the whole to be sold and Equally Divided
1 CONT amongst her & her children as to my Lands on Muddy Creek I will and
1 CONT Bequeath them as follows, the Drowning Creek Tract of land I will
1 CONT and Bequeath to my son John Harrifs the Sycamore Spring Tract to my
1 CONT son Benjamin Harris the tract on which my son Wm. has Built to my son
1 CONT Harris and the Tract Clalled the Holly Tract to my son Barnabas
1 CONT Harrifs and my land in Albemarle County together with the Stock that
1 CONT is thereon I direct shall be sold and that my sons James and Samuel
1 CONT Harris shall Receive of the money as much as Col John Miller & Robert
1 CONT Rodes shall Judge the land to be worth that I willed to my Other sons
1 CONT Viz to be made Equal to them, as to my three Daughters Viz Jane
1 CONT Gentry-Margret Harris, and Isabel Harris my will and Desire is that
1 CONT Jean Gentry should Receive ten pounds and Margret and Isbel
1 CONT Harris to have fifty pounds apeice out of the Ballance of what my
1 CONT Albermarld land and the Proffits arising from that place and if that
1 CONT should not be Sufficient that It shall be made up to htem out of any
1 CONT of Personal Estate that my wife and Executors after nemtioned shall
1 CONT think best as to my lands on Sinking Waters my will is that if they
1 CONT are obtained it should be sold and Wqually divided amongst my last Set
1 CONT of Children and I do appoint my dear & loveing wife with John
1 CONT Sappington and John Harris to execute that part of my will that
1 CONT respects my wife and her Children as witnefs my hand & seal this
1 CONT twentyeth day of February one thousand seven hundred and ninety four.
1 CONT Witnefs-Hartly Sappington Christopher Harrifs
1 CONT Rich®d Sappington Joseph Wells
1 CONT At a Court held for Madison County on Tuesday the 15th day of March
1 CONT 1794 This Will was proved to be the last will & testament of
1 CONT Christopher Harris by the oath of Joseph Wells, Hartly & Richard
1 CONT Sappington witnefses thereto and ordered to be recorded. Teste Will
1 CONT Irvine CMC
1 CONT Typed as spelled in will.
1 CONT The following is some research on Christopher Harris done by my cousin
1 CONT Evelyn W. Wallace:
1 CONT Preparer:  Evelyn W. Wallace, southern California
1 CONT Edited 2/2000
1 CONT      CHRISTOPHER HARRIS. (ca. 1725 VA-1794 KY). WIR00050 An entry in
1 CONT DAR LINEAGE BOOK, V. 80, p. 353 reads:  "Christopher Harris (1725-94)
1 CONT served in the Kentucky Militia, 1780.  He was born in Albemarle
1 CONT County, VA; died in Madison County, KY. ... Christopher Harris and
1 CONT Agness McCord (b. 1740), his wife, m. 1762." (Mrs. Mary Allen Mathews,
1 CONT No. 79960).
1 CONT      As with many older DAR applications, this, too, has flaws.  We
1 CONT deduce from the following deeds that Christopher's date of birth as
1 CONT given is approximately correct.  He was of age by 1753.  However,  his
1 CONT more likely birthplace was Hanover Co., VA, the parent county of
1 CONT Louisa Co., which was formed 1742 from Hanover Co.  Later. "the
1 CONT western portion of Louisa County was annexed to Albemarle County 1 May
1 CONT 1761," according to Rosalie Edith Davis, who has transcribed or
1 CONT abstracted many deeds and vestry records of both Louisa and Albemarle
1 CONT Cos.
1 CONT    In Vol. 7 of the Lineage Book of the Daughters of the American
1 CONT Colonists, p, 277, Christopher Harris (1725-94) is said to have
1 CONT married Mary Dabney in 1745.  No documentation is presented.  (Lineage
1 CONT of Mrs. Virginia Field Walton Brooks, born in Jonesboro, Arkansas.)
1 CONT (Lineage Books were at Santa Monica PL, 369.12 D263).  However,
1 CONT Christopher's 1794 will makes reference to Cornelius Dabney, who MAY
1 CONT have been his brother-in-law rather than his father-in-law.
1 CONT Another source states the marriage probably took place at Brown's
1 CONT Cove. This place may be in reference to the family of Benjamin Brown,
1 CONT who were neighbors of the Harrises.
1 CONT      Christopher Harris probably was named for a relative of another
1 CONT generation.  This name is found in a list of processioners ca. 1718,
1 CONT Hanover Co., VA, along with other surnames associated with the family
1 CONT of Robert Harris "the immigrant," i.e., Overton, Glenn, Garland,
1 CONT Grubbs.
1 CONT      From The Vestry Book of St. Paul's Parish, Hanover Co., VA
1 CONT 1706-1786, as transcribed and edited by C. G. Chamberlayne [Richmond:
1 CONT 1940], p. 266:
1 CONT "p. [206]" "The lands of Edw Garland, Jas. Overton, Xpher Harris, Jno
1 CONT Glenn, Saml Reynolds, Henry Farmer, Robt Jennings & Abra: Venable
1 CONT being one precinct of which Edwd Garland and Jas Overton were
1 CONT Overseers who made this return, the within Order executed in presence
1 CONT of James Glenn, Saml Reynolds, Abra: Venable, Henry Farmer, Mr. Robt
1 CONT Jennings did not appear, for his Land and Saml Reynolds is all in one
1 CONT pattent and no Division."
1 CONT      Another in St. Paul's Parish with whom the Harris family was
1 CONT associated was David Crawford. One of the daughters of Robert Harris
1 CONT and Mourning [Glenn], Frances or Nancy Harris was to marry Joel
1 CONT Crawford (qv), to whom David Crawford  probably was related. (More
1 CONT reseach is needed on the Crawford family.)
1 CONT      In 1746/47 Christopher Harris patented land.
1 CONT      Patent Bk 28:  Christopher Harris, 350 acs. Louisa Co., under the
1 CONT foot of ragged Mountains and on both sides of a West fork of Rockey
1 CONT Cr. on the Goochland Co. Line [N65 degrees W] on a ridge, adj. Mosias
1 CONT Jones & James Merideth; 12 Jan 1746/47, p. 25.  1 pd. 15 shillings (D.
1 CONT R. Hudgins, CAVALIERS AND PIONEERS, V. V, [Richmond, VA:  Virginia
1 CONT Genealogical Society, 1994] p. 304)
1 CONT      From Louisa Co. DB B. P. 500-501.  27 Mary 1753  Robert Harris of
1 CONT Fredericksville Par., Louisa Co., Gent., and Mourning, his wife, to
1 CONT William Keaton of same.  For and in consideration that sd. Keaton and
1 CONT Margaret, his wife, shall by deed make over to Christopher Harris (Son
1 CONT of afsd. Robert) for fee simple estate, 331 acres of land and
1 CONT plantation of William Keaton's; bounded as in a patent granted
1 CONT sd. Keaton in City of Williamsburg 12 Jan. 1747.  Sd. Harris have sold
1 CONT to sd. Keaton 400 acres and plantation of sd. Robert Harris on both
1 CONT sides of Rockey Creek, being land whereon sd. Keaton now lives,
1 CONT bounded as by patent granted sd. Harris in City of Williamsburg 15
1 CONT Sept. 1752.
1 CONT                     Robert Harris
1 CONT                     Mourning Harris
1 CONT Wit:  John Hawkins, David Watts, John (X) McCauley.
1 CONT 27 Mar 1752 acknowledged by Robert Harris and Mourning, his wife.
1 CONT      (Mourning Harris, Robert's wife, is said to have been was the
1 CONT former Mourning Glenn. Refer to her biography.)
1 CONT      P. 501-502.  27 Mar 1753  William Keaton of Fredericksville Par.,
1 CONT Louisa Co., and Margaret, his wife, to Christopher Harris of same.  In
1 CONT consideration that Robert Harris of Louisa Co., and Mourning, his
1 CONT wife, shall by deed make over to William Keaton 400 acres and
1 CONT plantation, bounded as in a patent granted sd. Harris in 1752, land
1 CONT whereon William Keaton now lives. Have sold to sd. Christopher Harris
1 CONT 331 acres on both sides of the south fork of Rocky Creek whereon sd.
1 CONT Christopher Harris now lives; bounded as in a patent
1 CONT granted sd. Keaton in the City of Williamsburg 12 Jan. 1747.
1 CONT                    William (M) Keaton
1 CONT                    Margaret (X) Keaton
1 CONT Wit:  John Hawkins, David Watts, John (X) McCauley
1 CONT 27 Mar. 1753 acknowledged by William Keaton.
1 CONT      George II to Mosias Jones, David Milles, Gentlemen Justices of
1 CONT Louisa Co.  Power granted to take acknowledgment of Margaret Keaton,
1 CONT who is so impotent that without great Danger of her body she cannot
1 CONT travel to the Court of our County.  3 Apr 1753.
1 CONT                 James Littlepage, Clk.
1 CONT 20 Apr. 1753  By virtue of this writ we have examined sd. Margaret,
1 CONT wife of William Keaton, who acknowledgted her right of dower.
1 CONT                Mosias Jones, David Mills
1 CONT      (Rosalie Edith Davis, LOUISA COUNTY, VIRGINIA DEED BOOKS A AND B,
1 CONT 1742-1759 [Bellevue, WA  1976] p. 84)
1 CONT (To be continued)
1 CONT E.W.Wallace(hdanw@aol.com)
1 CONT This is a continuation of the biographical sketch of Christopher
1 CONT Harris (the elder) of Madison Co., KY.
1 CONT      A Virginia land patent of Tully Choice, Pat. Bk 31-711 indicates
1 CONT that his land is on the Branches of Rockey Creek and the Albemarle Co.
1 CONT Line [N50W] and adjoins Christopher Harris, William Keatton, Patrick
1 CONT Wood & William Owens.
1 CONT Christopher Harris's Marriages
1 CONT      Christopher's first wife, according to Hazel Spraker in THE BOONE
1 CONT FAMILY, ("Harris Family" by Bess Hawthorne, a Harris descendant) was
1 CONT Mary Dabney.  In Christopher's will (1794, Madison Co., KY), cited
1 CONT below, he mentions bequest of Cornelius Dabney, probably Mary's father
1 CONT or possibly brother. The bequest was to Harris's oldest children,
1 CONT implying that these were his children by Mary Dabney. A Cornelius
1 CONT Dabney was in King William Co. ca. 1723, but also in Hanover Co.
1 CONT 1733-34 (Hanover Co. Court Records), and in Louisa Co., VA as late as
1 CONT 1782.  The latter Cornelius Dabney would
1 CONT have been contemporaneous with Christopher Harris but possibly
1 CONT predeceasing him. It is known there were several men by this name of
1 CONT succeeding generations.
1 CONT      The Dabneys were neighbors in Albemarle Co. in 1768 as evidenced
1 CONT by the following deed, DB-5, pp. 37-38:
1 CONT     William Dabney & his wf. Jane of Albemarle Co. to William Shelton
1 CONT for 200 pds. current money of VA, a tract of land on Mechams River,
1 CONT adj Wm. Wallace. (s) Wm. Dabney  Wit:  Thomas Grubbs, Elizabeth Jones,
1 CONT Christopher Harris, Robert Harris, Tyre Harris.  2 Jun 1768; delivery
1 CONT of deed acknd by witnesses on same date.  Rec. Nov Ct 1768
1 CONT      (Tyre or Tyree Harris, brother of Christopher, found in some
1 CONT Louisa Co. records, later removed to Orange Co. NC from which Caswell
1 CONT Co. was formed in 1777. William Shelton married into the Harris
1 CONT family.  He had a son named Tyree and so did Christopher Harris.)
1 CONT Louisa County VA Records
1 CONT       Christopher Harris was a witness in Louisa Co. 24 Nov 1750 to
1 CONT Martin's improvements, apparently an appraisal by three men (by order
1 CONT of Louisa Court Oct 1750).
1 CONT      An indication of the approximate location of the land of
1 CONT Christopher Harris in Louisa Co. is found in this entry in
1 CONT Fredericksville Parish Vestry Book:
1 CONT     P. 35: [ca 28 Nov 1750]  "Ordered that Mosias Jones and
1 CONT Christopher Harris do procession all the lands on the up[p]er side of
1 CONT Buck mountain Creek and a Cross Moormans river to the Coty. Line and
1 CONT up the Same to the Ragged Mountains and under them to Brown's road and
1 CONT down the Same to Buck Mountain Creek."
1 CONT      (Rosalie Edith Davis, FREDERICKSVILLE PARISH VESTRY BOOK,
1 CONT 1742-1787, VOL. I [Manchester, MO:  privately printed, 1978], p. 38
1 CONT      "Pursuant to an Order of Court Dated ye 24th Day of June 1752,"
1 CONT an almost identical order was issued to Moisas Jones Gent. and
1 CONT Christopher Harris.  (p. 51)
1 CONT      Also living in Fredericksville Parish at the same time were
1 CONT Christopher's father, Robert Harris "Gent." and brother Tyree Harris.
1 CONT Tyree succeeded his father Robert as vestryman, but he later migrated
1 CONT to North Carolina.  Jeremiah Glen, no doubt a relative of Christopher
1 CONT and Tyree's mother, Mourning Glen, was a resident in the parish also.
1 CONT (Mourning's father is believed to have been James Glen, but the exact
1 CONT identity of Mourning's parents is in dispute among contemporary
1 CONT genealogists.)
1 CONT      Much later, Christopher was again ordered to procession:
1 CONT      P. 81 [ca 1767]  "Ordered that Xtopher Harris & Daniel Maupine
1 CONT Junr. do procession all the lands above (a hole in the page) ... res
1 CONT Meeting House between Moreman's river and Woods Road up to the top of
1 CONT the Great Mountain." (Davis, op. cit., p. 85)
1 CONT      A William Dabney appears in the orders.  He was to procession
1 CONT between Wood's and Rhodes Road & the River and Ivy Creek.
1 CONT Albemarle Co. Records
1 CONT        Albemarle Co., VA was formed 1744 from Louisa and Goochland
1 CONT Cos.
1 CONT       In Albemarle Co., there is this deed:  DB A?-p158:  13 May 1762
1 CONT Christopher Harris to Saml. Karr, Augusta [Co.] for 65 pds., 331 acres
1 CONT both sides S fork Rockey Creek adj. Henry Bunch, Mosias [transcribed
1 CONT as Morias but other records show Mosias] Jones.
1 CONT       (Rev. Bailey Fulton Davis, THE DEEDS OF AMHERST COUNTY, VIRGINIA
1 CONT 1761-1807 AND ALBEMARLE COUNTY, VIRGINIA 1748-1763, p. 54)
1 CONT      This parcel of 331 acres seems to be the same which Keaton had
1 CONT sold to Christopher Harris nine years earlier and which Robert Harris,
1 CONT Christopher's father, had earlier sold to Keaton with proviso that it
1 CONT was to be later transferred to Christopher.  (This type of conveyance
1 CONT usually occurred between an older man to a younger relative or a
1 CONT trusted friend when the son of the grantor was underage.  The
1 CONT relationship of Keaton to the Harris family is unknown.  Perhaps he
1 CONT was a brother-in-law of Robert Harris.)
1 CONT      From Albemarle Co., VA court papers 1744-1783:
1 CONT      1770 [p. 32] Promissory note:  Philip Thurman of Albemarle Co. to
1 CONT Christopher Harris, dated 10 Mar 1770, witnessed by Robert Harris and
1 CONT Benjamin Thurman.  (On back "To Mr. Robert Harvey:  Sir, please pay
1 CONT this bond.  Signed Philip Thurman.)   (Comment:  This may be the
1 CONT younger Robert Harris, Christopher's brother or perhaps Christopher's
1 CONT son of the same name.)
1 CONT      (Benjamin B. Weisiger III, ALBEMARLE CO., VA COURT PAPERS
1 CONT 1744-1783, SLC film 1,697,895 Item 9)
1 CONT To be continuedPart 3   (Two other parts of the biography of
1 CONT Christopher Harris have already been posted.  This is a continuation.)
1 CONT The following deeds of Louisa Co. make reference to Albemarle Co.
1 CONT line: Deed Bk. B-136-137 makes mention of Christopher Harris's land.
1 CONT The deed is dated 14 Jul 1756 is from Tully Choice of Halifax Co.,
1 CONT grantor, to James Ennis of Louisa Co....on branches of Rockey
1 CONT Creek...Christopher Harris and William Keaton's corner...Patrick Woods
1 CONT line...Williams Owens line, corner in Albemarle Co. line...Christopher
1 CONT Harris' corner in the County line.
1 CONT      Deed Bk. B-300 also makes reference to land of Christopher
1 CONT Harris. James Ennis & wife of Louisa to James Read of same...on
1 CONT branches of Rockey Creek..
1 CONT Christopher Harrises and William Keaton's corner...Patrick Wood's
1 CONT line...William Owens line to Owen's corner oak in Albemarle Co.
1 CONT line...Christopher Harris' corner in Co. line.
1 CONT      (Rosalie Edith Davis, LOUISA COUNTY, VA DEED BOOKS A AND B,
1 CONT 1742-1759 [Bellevue, WA, 1976])
1 CONT More Albemarle Co., VA Records
1 CONT      DB Bk 3-171 3 Apr 1762, Christopher Harris was a witness to a
1 CONT deed Ro. Harris, planter, to son Ro., Jr., love - on Blue Ridge, Doyle
1 CONT River, pat. of 521 acres 6 Dec 1753. Other witnesses were Jas. Harris
1 CONT and Wm. Brown.
1 CONT      On 3 Apr 1762, DB 3-175 Benj. Brown deeded property to his
1 CONT daughter, Lucretia Harris.  The witnesses were Jas. & Christopher
1 CONT Harris, Wm. Brown, and Benj. Thurman.
1 CONT     (Of interest is the fact that Benj. Brown a few months earlier had
1 CONT deeded land on Doyle River [in Albemarle Co.] to Benjamin Brown [Jr.]
1 CONT of Hanover. But he is not specified as Benj. Brown, Jr..  Hanover Co.
1 CONT was the former home of the Harrises.  Hazel A. Spraker in THE BOONE
1 CONT FAMILY states that Brown Sr.'s wife was Sarah Dabney.  Lucretia Brown,
1 CONT a daughter of Benjamin Brown, (grantor in above deed), married Robert
1 CONT Harris, Jr.  Refer to the biography
1 CONT of Robert Harris, Jr., who is inferred from DB 3-264 to have been the
1 CONT husband of the above Lucretia [Brown] Harris. Christopher again
1 CONT witnessed that deed.)
1 CONT      (Rev. Bailey Fulton Davis, THE DEEDS OF AMHERST COUNTY, VIRGINIA,
1 CONT 1761-1807 AND ALBEMARLE COUNTY, VIRGINIA 1748-1763, Easley, SC, 1979)
1 CONT      Christopher Harris appears on the personal property tax list of
1 CONT Albemarle Co., VA, 1782.  He is shown with 9 slaves, 27 cattle, 4
1 CONT horses, paying a tax of 5 pounds, 14 shillings, and 9 pence.  Two
1 CONT other Harrises are shown as proprietors in District 3:  James and
1 CONT Thomas.
1 CONT      Harris's first wife, Mary Dabney, must have died before 1769 as
1 CONT on that date,  Agnes (McCord) appears as Harris's wife in Albemarle
1 CONT Co. deeds. Two other McCords are shown in District 3:  Jane, probably
1 CONT a widow, and William.
1 CONT      (Thomas Jefferson, Esq., is shown in District 2 on the 1782 tax
1 CONT list of Albemarle Co..  He counted 2 males over 21; 129 slaves; 106
1 CONT net cattle; 23 horses; 6 "wheels for riding carriages," paying a tax
1 CONT of 70 pounds, 12 shillings, and 6 pence.)
1 CONT      In Augusta Co. VA, Deed Bk 22-p. 395 indicates that Christopher
1 CONT Harris and Agness (--) executed a deed, 17 Nov 1778.
1 CONT      Details were not given by Lyman Chalkley, CHRONICLES OF THE
1 CONT SCOTTISH-IRISH SETTLEMENT, V. 3.  Chalkley abstracted many documents
1 CONT of what was then Augusta Co., VA.
1 CONT      Land office records in Virginia Archives show the following
1 CONT Virginia land patents or grants for Christopher Harris in Albemarle
1 CONT Co., VA:
1 CONT      1.  15 Aug 1764 - 164 A on Gingsang br. in Millstone Bottom,
1 CONT Patents No. 36, 1764-67, p. 624
1 CONT      2.  17 Aug 1770 - 234 A on the side of one of the Mountains in
1 CONT the Blue Ridge called Bucks Elbow.  Patent No. 39, 1770-71, p. 10
1 CONT      Christopher's father Robert Harris also patented land in
1 CONT Albemarle Co. in 1751.
1 CONT From Albemarle Co. Deed Bk 5:
1 CONT      14 Nov 1771 Christopher Harris and his wife Agnes  Albemarle
1 CONT County of one part and William Crawford of the said County for ..
1 CONT pounds current money of Virginia 350 A.in Albemarle Co. under the foot
1 CONT of the Ragged Mountains and both sides of a West Fork of Rock Creek ..
1 CONT in Mosias Jones's line, adj James Merridiths line to a corner in
1 CONT Goochland Co. line, West Fork of Rockey Creek to the first station.
1 CONT    Signed Sealed and Delivered in the presence of
1 CONT      Bennet Henderson    Robert Miller.            Christopher Harriss
1 CONT      Thomas Maupin         Minian Mills              Agness Harriss
1 CONT      Recd of the within named William Crawford the sum of Forty pounds
1 CONT current money of Virginia which is the consideration money in this
1 CONT Deed mentioned Received per me.
1 CONT                Christor.  Harriss
1 CONT      At Albemarle June Court 1772
1 CONT This indenture and Receipt were acknowledged by Christopher Harris and
1 CONT Agnes his Wife parties thereto and ordered to be recorded.
1 CONT      In 1785, in Albemarle Co., Christopher Harris was surety at
1 CONT marriage of John Harris to Margaret Maupin, daughter of John Maupin.
1 CONT      The 1787 Albemarle County Personal Property Tax, List A, shows
1 CONT Christopher Harris as "self" charged with tax; 2-3-5-4-8. The first
1 CONT column indicates number of white males above 16 and under 21.  Cols. 2
1 CONT and 3 indicate slaves and their age brackets; Col. 4 is number of
1 CONT horses, etc.; Col. 5 indicates number of cattle.   The same tax list
1 CONT shows the following McCords: Wm., Jr., Samuel and Wm. Sr. Other
1 CONT related families are shown: Maupin, Rodes.
1 CONT      (Netti Schreiner-Yantis and Florine Love, THE 1787 CENSUS OF
1 CONT VIRGINIA, V. 2, p. 140.)
1 CONT Revolutionary War Service
1 CONT     Hamilton J. Eckenrode in VIRGINIA SOLDIERS OF THE AMERICAN
1 CONT REVOLUTION, V. I (VA State Library & Archives, 1989) lists "Harris,
1 CONT Christopher (Kentucky m.) Fx. Coms. 1780."  No verification of this
1 CONT could be located at the Virginia State Library Oct 1995.
1 CONT      Christopher Harris qualifies for "patriotic service" by virtue of
1 CONT the
1 CONT fact that he furnished an item or items of value during the
1 CONT Revolution.  His name appears in "Public Service Claims, Albemarle
1 CONT County Court Booklet," unnumbered page.  The number beside his name is
1 CONT 154:  "for 572 do taken by the Wh for State use."  The preceding
1 CONT person's payment was for items taken by militia for State use, and the
1 CONT "WH" in Harris's claim may be an abbreviation for militia.   He was
1 CONT paid 4 pds., 9 shillings, and 6 pence.
1 CONT      Virginia State Library enclosed the following paper pertaining to
1 CONT Christopher Harris, not all of which is legible:
1 CONT No. 29
1 CONT I do hereby certifie that I have Received of Christopher Harris for
1 CONT public uses agreable to an Act of Assembly for procuring a supply
1 CONT provisions and other necessary [torn] in the uss of the army four
1 CONT Hundred & thirty seven [torn] at five pounds ... amounting to two
1 CONT thousand and six hundred & eighty five pounds as witness my hand this
1 CONT 18 October 1781.
1 CONT L  2685 - 537
1 CONT           89.6                  John Key C. P. ?
1 CONT     537 - a 3 d        46.14.3          for Albemarle County
1 CONT Removal to Kentucky
1 CONT      By 1780, Christopher Harris was beginning to make his move to
1 CONT Kentucky.
1 CONT      A land grant for Christopher Harris has been recorded as follows:
1 CONT      Original survey no: 8551
1 CONT      Name:  Christopher Harris
1 CONT      Acreage:  1,200
1 CONT      County:  Fayette
1 CONT      Watercourse:  Hinkston Fk., Licking
1 CONT      Survey Date:  1-20-1786
1 CONT      Original Bk & Page:  10-412
1 CONT      Grantee:  Same & heirs
1 CONT      Grant Date:  1-25-1792
1 CONT      Original Bk & Page:  14-385-386
1 CONT     (Joan E. Brookes-Smith, MASTER INDEX VIRGINIA SURVEYS AND GRANTS
1 CONT 1774-1791 [Frankfort, KY:  Kentucky Historical Society, 1976], p. 84)
1 CONT      (Note:  In 1786, one Francis Eppes Harris was granted land on the
1 CONT same watercourse, same county.  Whether there is a relationship is
1 CONT unknown.  None has been discovered.)
1 CONT      Jefferson Land Entries show on 17 May 1780, Christopher Harris
1 CONT entered 1200 A on Licking [River], North Fork, Bk. A-66  It is unclear
1 CONT whether this is Christopher Harris the father or his son, Christopher
1 CONT Harris.  If correct, this date precedes the 1786 survey date mentioned
1 CONT above.  Recent perusal of Madison Co. deeds reveals there was a deed
1 CONT involving this acreage, of which his heirs seemed unaware. At the time
1 CONT of the deed of some of the heirs, the land was then in Bourbon Co.
1 CONT      By 1788, Christopher Harris is listed as a tithable in Madison
1 CONT Co., KY: 1-0-2 first col. is no. of tithables; Col 2. is blacks over
1 CONT 16; Col. 3 is horses and cattle.  (It is unclear whether this is the
1 CONT older Christopher Harris or his son.  However, this  seems to belie
1 CONT the story that Christopher Harris and a large group of kinsman moved
1 CONT to Kentucky with many slaves.  They may have sent back to Virginia for
1 CONT slaves, but there appears only one black over 16 in 1787.)
1 CONT        Christopher Harris himself appears on the 1787 tax list as
1 CONT taxable, 1 black over 16, 3 horses, 5 cattle.
1 CONT      Christopher Harris, appears on 1792 tax list of Madison Co., KY.
1 CONT He had 9 blacks, 15 horses, 43 cattle, and 700 acres of land.
1 CONT (Excerpt from REGISTER of the Kentucky State Historical Society).
1 CONT       Other Harrises on same tax list: William Harrias (?) (no land or
1 CONT slaves); Richmd Harris (no land or slaves); Sherwood Harris (80
1 CONT acres); Benj. Harris (no land or slaves).
1 CONT      Other Harrises listed by Joan Colbert Gioe in her tax abstracts
1 CONT for
1 CONT Madison Co. were David, Andrew, James [2X], John [2X], Samuel, Thomas,
1 CONT Mary and Wm.  Whether they were related, we do not know. Except for
1 CONT John Harris, these do not seem to be the heirs named in Christopher's
1 CONT will.  Perhaps other documents would show relationships.
1 CONT      Madison Co. deed indexes show that Christopher Harris was the
1 CONT grantee (buyer) in these deeds:
1 CONT      DB A-109, Tract Muddy ?? [incomplete copy], grantor:  Wallace
1 CONT Estill, Nov 4, 1788; recorded Jun 2, 1789
1 CONT      DB B-360, 200 A Calloway ?, grantor:  Caleb Callaway & wf, Oct 6,
1 CONT 1790, recorded Dec 7, 1790
1 CONT Submitted by:  Evelyn W. Wallace
1 CONT hdanw@aol.com
