0 @N6000000004086481139@ NOTE The following is some research of Evelyn W. Wallace: 
1 CONT Submitted by E.W.Wallace   hdanw@aol.com
1 CONT DABNEY HARRIS.  WIR2020  Little is known of Dabney Harris, who appears
1 CONT to the be the son of the elder Christopher Harris of early Madison
1 CONT Co., KY. His birthdate of 15 Dec 1745, apparently unconfirmed, is
1 CONT taken from DAR application 598925.  Those of his siblings and most of
1 CONT the marriages are given, indicating the applicant MAY have used a
1 CONT Bible record.  He died after Apr 1795, according to Surry Co., NC
1 CONT records.
1 CONT      In Nov 1774 he was witness in Albemarle Co., VA to a will of one
1 CONT William Blackwell, written 23 Nov 1774, proved Mar court 1775.  Other
1 CONT witnesses were Philip Thurmon and James Gardner.
1 CONT (J. Estelle Stewart King, ABSTRACTS OF WILLS, INVENTORIES AND
1 CONT ADMINISTRATION ACCOUNTS OF ALBEMARLE COUNTY, VA 1748-1800 [Beverly
1 CONT Hills, CA, 1940], p. 22)
1 CONT      Dabney apparently moved to Surry Co., NC.(1)  His name appears in
1 CONT Madison Co., KY Grant Deed Index.  Dabney Harris, grantor; Christopher
1 CONT Harris, grantee; C-381, 9 Mar 1795; recorded 5 May 1795; power of
1 CONT attorney. "Know all men by these presents that I Dabney Harris of
1 CONT Surry County, North Carolina for sundry [reasons?] etc do constitute
1 CONT and appoint my son and Friend Christopher Harris of the said county &
1 CONT state my true & lawfull attorney to act demand sue for recover & ...
1 CONT of Christopher Harris & Foster Jones of Madison County & in the State
1 CONT of Kentucke  Exrs to the Estate  of my Deceased Father all such
1 CONT Legacys as may be due to me on that behalf? hereby
1 CONT ratifying and confirming whatever my said Attorney may do in and
1 CONT touching Premises in as full and Ample manner as though I were
1 CONT personally present in Witness whereof I have hereunto set my hand and
1 CONT affixed my seal this ninth (?] day of March one Thousand seven hundred
1 CONT and ninety four. /s/ Dabney Harris  Teste Reuben Canterbury, John
1 CONT Canterbury, J. P. ----"
1 CONT A Dabney Harris is listed in the 1820 census of Kentucky as being in
1 CONT Pulaski Co., but we have no idea whether he is the son of Christopher,
1 CONT decd, of Madison Co., KY.  A Christopher Harris is also listed in
1 CONT Pulaski Co.; possibly he is the son of Dabney Harris.  More research
1 CONT is needed.
1 CONT (1)  On Family Tree Maker CD ROM CENSUS INDEX:  COLONIAL AMERICA
1 CONT 1607-1789, he is listed in ... North Carolina, Hardin's District.
1 CONT I welcome additional information.  Parentage of Dabney Harris is
1 CONT suspected to be son of Christopher Harris, Sr. of Albemarle Co., VA
1 CONT and later of Madison Co., KY.  Note he names a son Christopher Harris.
1 CONT If he is the son of the elder Christopher Harris, then his mother was
1 CONT reportedly Mary Dabney.  Mary
1 CONT Dabney's parentage unknown, although Christopher Harris the elder in
1 CONT his Madison KY will makes reference to the will of Cornelius Dabney.
1 CONT Was Cornelius Dabney Mary's father?  If so, does anyone know where
1 CONT Dabney's will is recorded?
1 CONT Evelyn W. Wallacesouthern California
1 CONT The following is a responsive e-mail from Glenn E. Harris:
1 CONT From: "Glenn E. Harris" <geharris@juno.com>
1 CONT Subject: [MADKY-L] Dabney Harris, s/o Christoper Harris
1 CONT In reference to the message posted below from Evelyn W. Wallace, I too
1 CONT am interested in the family of Dabney Harris born 15 Dec. 1745 in VA.
1 CONT I suspect him to be the father of Solomon Harris of Surry Co., NC who
1 CONT is my direct line.  Solomon married Nancy Blackwell of Surry NC abt
1 CONT 1797. Nancy is the dau of David Blackwell and Sarah Harris of Surry
1 CONT NC. Sarah's father, Robert Harris is brother to the elder Christopher
1 CONT Harris mentioned below who moved from Albemarle Co., VA to Madison
1 CONT Co., KY and of course Dabney is the eldest son of Christopher and was
1 CONT grown and most likely married when he moved to Surry Co., NC where he
1 CONT lived in Wilkes and Surry counties in NC near his uncle Robert.  It is
1 CONT interesting to note that Solomon Harris and wife Nancy with children
1 CONT moved to Garrard Co., KY in 1804 which is next to Madison Co and
1 CONT Christopher Harris. I have found little solid info on Dabney Harris
1 CONT but below is some notes I have collected, mostly from Surry Co., NC
1 CONT records.
1 CONT 1.  Dabney must have died after 1800, not 1795 as stated below, as he
1 CONT is on the 1800 Surry, NC census, Dabney Harris, 02101-0110100.
1 CONT 2.  Dabney apparently lived in both Wilkes and Surry counties.  Found
1 CONT Dabney Harris on Wilkes Co., NC, Hardins District, pg 002, 1787 state
1 CONT census.
1 CONT 3.  1790 Federal census for Wilkes Co., NC;  Dabney Haris (Harris), 2M
1 CONT 16+, 3M 16-, 6Fem, 0 slaves.  (Dabney, wife, 5 sons, 5 dau)
1 CONT 4.   Dabney Harris is on 1782 Surry Tax list; Capt. Humphries
1 CONT District:
1 CONT Dabney has one horse, 2 cows and 100 acres. (No location given).
1 CONT 5.  From William Harris Millier's History and Genealogies, 1907
1 CONT version, pgs 278-9.  -  "By his first wife, Mary Dabney, Christopher
1 CONT Harris had...Dabney Harris, who was a resident of Surry County, North
1 CONT Carolina on May 5th 1795, and whose son Christopher Harris at that
1 CONT time being a man of maturity, came to Madison County, Ky,. from North
1 CONT Carolina with a power of attorney from his father (Dabney Harris)
1 CONT authorizing his said son to receipt for his (Dabney Harris) part of
1 CONT his fathers estate, and from this it is known that Dabney Harris had
1 CONT one child but as to any other children no history is at hand."
1 CONT (parentheses as in original)..............Although this info is from a
1 CONT book I had not been able to confirm it.  The power of attorney,
1 CONT submitted by Evelyn below, appears to be the source of this book info
1 CONT and indicates that Dabney did indeed have a son named Christopher.
1 CONT 6.  From Surry Co., NC abstracts: deed books D, E and F (1779-1797)  -
1 CONT 6 Aug 1793, Dabney Harris to John Personate, for 75 pounds, 95 acres
1 CONT adjacent Jesse Franklin and Mark Kenned(a)y.  Wits: (X) James
1 CONT Franklin, Thomas Ross, William Snow.  Signed Dabney Harris.  (this
1 CONT land was most likely on Butler creek)
1 CONT 7.  Extracted from McNeil, George F.: Abstracts of North Carolina.
1 CONT Land Grant Files of Grants Issued for Land in Wilkes County;
1 CONT Published, 1994 by Wilkes Genealogical Society, North Wilkesboro, NC.
1 CONT -  Pg 73, Vol 1, 1778-1798, File #727.  Dabney Harris received grant
1 CONT #724, 22 Sep 1785 for 150 acres, both sides of Glade creek of the
1 CONT Little river, adjoining Young Edwards.  Based on Warrent/entry #1160
1 CONT dated 2 Jan 1785.  Grant is recorded in Book 59, pg 332.  Chain
1 CONT carriers: Edward Franklin, Jno. Edwards.  Surveyed by William Johnson.
1 CONT This land was in present day Alleghany Co., adj Greyson Co., VA
1 CONT border.  However Dabney appears to have actually lived on Butler
1 CONT creek, on the south fork of the Mitchell river, next door to David
1 CONT Austin..............According to Austin family researchers, Benjamin
1 CONT Austin, son of David Austin above, married a Sarah
1 CONT Harris who is suppose to be a daughter of Dabney Harris.  However I
1 CONT can find no one who can prove this to me.  I do not have the notes
1 CONT with me but I believe Sarah Harris and Benjamin Austin moved to
1 CONT Kentucky also.
1 CONT 8.  I am aware of the Dabney Harris and Christopher Harris names in
1 CONT Pulaski Co., KY but am not sure who either were or how they may be
1 CONT connected.  I had thought that Dabney may be the son of Dabney or his
1 CONT grandson or the son of one of Dabney's many brothers who moved to
1 CONT Madison KY with their father Christopher.  Could the Christopher found
1 CONT there be the son of the elder Christopher?
1 CONT 9.  My info is that Mary Dabney was the first wife of the elder
1 CONT Christopher Harris and Dabney Harris was their eldest son.  The
1 CONT parents of Mary were Cornelius Dabney and Sarah Ann Jennings of
1 CONT Hanover county VA.  Their son John Dabney supposedly married Anna
1 CONT Harris, the sister of Christopher Harris.
1 CONT Hope this all helps and maybe someone out there can add to or correct
1 CONT this info.
1 CONT Glenn E. Harris
