1 CONT ***************attached below to above*****************
1 CONT *****************below note to second entry with  kids!!!jhll mess contradiction*************
1 CONT This is the Thomas Harris Brother to Mary Harris who md Thomas Ligon and both children of Capt Thomas Harris 1586 md Joan Gurgarney**************has nothing to do with Thomas who md Mary Giles- son Robert Harris and Mary Clairborn
1 CONT
1 CONT Thomas was son of Major Wm Harris & Lucy Day Stewart There is no mention of a surviving wife or children in this will. ------------------- NOTE: Proven Henrico County Court 2 Jun 1679 Record Book #1 pg 199 There is a will of a Tho
1 CONC mas Harris which reads: In the name of God, Amen. I, Thomas Harris being very ill and sick and very weak, make this my last Will & Testament, being in sound and perfect memory. 1st I bequeath my soul to God that gave it, & my body
1 CONC  to the earth from whence it came. I give & bequeath unto my sister-in-law, Love Harris*, my land at ye (the) Ware, according to the bounds set in my father's will, to her and her heirs forever & give her as much power of the afor
1 CONC es'd land as I myself had in my life time. I give and bequeath unto my Cozen (Cousin), Richard Lygon** all my horses mare or foles y't can be found or to be said or proved to be mine to him and his heirs forever, they not being gi
1 CONC ven by my Grandfather into the hands of the overseers for the true and honest p'formance of this my last Will I have hereunto set my hand and seal. In the year of our Lord God, 10 Feb 1678-79. /s/ Thomas Harris Testes: Alice (x) H
1 CONC arris Mary (x) Lygon, Jun'r Rich'd Lygon** Proved in Henrico Co., Court the 2nd day of June, 1679 by the oath of Mrs. Mary Lygon, the younger. ------------------- *Note: Love Harris was his 1/2 sister dau. of Alice and Major Wm Ha
1 CONC rris (he calls her sister-in-law [really his 1/2 sister] in his will) Love appears to be short for Lovewell ref: Fran Fletcher. ------------------- ** Richard Ligon (died 1724) was oldest living son of Mary Harris Ligon
