1 CONT Name: Judge Marmaduke Williams Sex: M Birth: 6 APR 1774 in Orange County, North Carolina (Virginia per 1850 census) Death: 29 OCT 1850 in Tuscaloosa County, Alabama Event: Misc.#1 1832 Elected Judge of Tuscaloosa Co., Alabama Buri
1 CONC al: Greenwood Cemetery, Tuscaloosa County, Alabama Note: 
1 CONT [McMillin & Williams Families 20.FTW]WILLIAMS, Marmaduke, 1774-1850WILLIAMS, Marmaduke, (cousin of John Williams, of Tennessee, Lewis Williams, and Robert Williams), a Representative from North Carolina; born in Caswell County, N.
1 CONC C., April 6, 1774; completed preparatory studies; studied law; was admitted to the bar and practiced; member of the State senate in 1802; elected as a Republican to the Eighth, Ninth, and Tenth Congresses (March 4, 1803-March 3, 1
1 CONC 809); was not a candidate for renomination; moved to Mississippi Territory in 1810 and later to Huntsville, Madison County, Ala.; in 1818 settled in Tuscaloosa, Ala.; delegate to the State constitutional convention in 1819 and the
1 CONC  same year was an unsuccessful candidate for Governor of Alabama; member of the State house of representatives 1821-1839; judge of the Tuscaloosa County Court 1832-1842; died in Tuscaloosa, Ala., October 29, 1850; interment in Gre
1 CONC enwood Cemetery.Marmaduke, member of congress. born in Caswell county, North Carolina, 6 April, 1772; died in Tuscaloosa, Alabama, 29 October, 1850, studied and practised law, was a member of the state senate in 1802, and served i
1 CONC n congress three successive terms, entering the house when his cousin retired. After the conclusion of his last term he emigrated to Alabama in 1810. He was a delegate from Tuscaloosa county to the convention that framed the state
1 CONC  constitution in 1819, and on its adoption was a candidate for governor, but was defeated by William W. Bibb, who had held that office in the territorial government. He was elected to the legislature in 1821, and was ten times re-
1 CONC elected. In 1826 he was appointed a commissioner to settle territorial accounts between Alabama and Mississippi, and he was judge of the county court from 1832 till 1842, when he was retired by limitation of age.--1850Williams, M.
1 CONC  D.AL Tuscaloosa CountyDistrict 1 1850 16 191
1 CONT Father: Nathaniel B. Jr. Williams  b: 1 OCT 1742 in Hanover County, Virginia Mother: Mary Ann Williamson  b: 3 JUN 1745 in VirginiaMarriage 1 Agnes Payne Harris  b: 1775 in Virginia 
