0 @N6000000008630583074@ NOTE SOUTH TO WEST, Margaret Bell Harrell Farnham, 1947, page 15:
1 CONT
1 CONT "Grandmother Bell died soon after we moved to the new home on
1 CONT the plains. She was rather small of stature with a keen sense of
1 CONT humor, in fact something of a practical joker. She always found
1 CONT a way to accomplish a purpose. She could always find a
1 CONT substitute when what she required was not available."
1 CONT
1 CONT page 8: "My first lesson in politeness I learned from
1 CONT grandmother. After supper in the winter the family would gather
1 CONT in her room for a few moments. There was always a roaring fire
1 CONT in the fireplace. Her bed was one of those high post massive
1 CONT beds, double castors on all the posts, too heavy for any
1 CONT housemaid to move and was never placed close to the wall. I well
1 CONT remember squeezing wetween that bed and the wall when I wanted
1 CONT to cross over from one side of the fireplace to the other,
1 CONT because she had told me it was impolite to pass or stand between
1 CONT anyone and the fire or light."
