1 CONT comdg. 4th     Brigade, Buford's (2nd) Div., Forrest's Cav.
1 CONT (Insp. Report F 3)
1 CONT
1 CONT May 14, 1864. Col. T.H. Bell, condg. Grigade, recommended J. T.
1 CONT Bell as A.D.C.     The letter was returned from the A.&I.G.O.
1 CONT Aug. 8, 1864, with the following         indorsement: "Res.
1 CONT returned through Lt. Gen. S.D. Lee, disapproved. An       A.D.C.
1 CONT is only allowed to a general officer." (1-156-23; 1-161-175.)
1 CONT Report A.O.
1 CONT
1 CONT May 3, 1865. J. T. Bell [no rank given], A.D.C. to Brig. Gen.
1 CONT Bell. comdg.
1 CONT
1 CONT Brigade, W.H. Jacknson's Div., Forrest's Cav. (Returns,
1 CONT Forrest's Cav.)
1 CONT
1 CONT May 10, 1865. J. T. Bell, Lieut & A.D.C., paroled. Officer with
1 CONT whom he was
1 CONT
1 CONT serving not stated. (Surrender in Ala., Miss., & E. La., May 4,
1 CONT 1865.)
1 CONT
1 CONT 1870 Census, Dyer County, Tennessee, 6th Civil District,
1 CONT Newbern, page 104, dwelling & family 327:   Isic Bell, age 26,
1 CONT farmer, $5000 real estate, $1000 personal, b. Tenn; Lizzy, age
1 CONT 19, keeping house, b. Tenn.
1 CONT
1 CONT 1880 Census, Henderson County, Tennessee, !0th District,
1 CONT Lexington, Ed 60, page 13, line 33:    Bell, Ike, age 34,
1 CONT drummer, all b. Tenn; Lizzie, age 28, wife, keeping house, all
1 CONT b. Tenn; James, age 9, son; Willie, age 7, son, Johnnie age 4,
1 CONT son; Annie, age 4, daughter.
